// ============================================================================
// V11 (2026-08-21) — MERGE of V9.12 with the V10 correction set.
//
// V9.12 is the base and stays the base: 2,774 lines carrying an audit history
// from V6 through V9.12, including the answers to a 20-finding external
// adversarial audit. Nothing in that lineage was rewritten. V11 adds what V9
// did not have and leaves everything V9 already did better alone.
//
// What V9 already did better than V10, kept unchanged:
//   - Pre-staged protective exits (the entry bar is never naked).
//   - Sizing on risk + 2x slippage, not structural risk — V10 derived the
//     same cost-drag result and had NOT applied it to sizing.
//   - Support tolerance floored at max(%, ATR); V10 floored at one tick.
//   - Whole-share exit legs; halt-band veto; venue/supported-market gating;
//     RVOL-at-time; exactly-once fill handling; the zombie-display fixes.
//
// What V11 adds, each marked // V11 at the point it applies:
//   1. §3 CONFLUENCE IS A GATE. V9 computed supportCount and spent it only
//      on the display-only quality score, so a dip that stopped at no level
//      at all could still arm. §3 is explicit: two independent reasons.
//   2. Two confluence components V9 lacked — the 200 MA, and the flipped
//      level (resistance broken and retested from above). The flip requires
//      the level to have ACTUALLY been exceeded; testing only "price is near
//      a prior high" is a tautology that counts every nearby swing high.
//   3. §3 pullback_index — first or second pullback only. V9 gated
//      pullbackBars (how many BARS the dip lasts), which is a different
//      rule. The index resets on a new high of day, a VWAP break and a close
//      under the prior dip low; without those resets it climbs all session
//      and the gate can never open.
//   4. §7 PARTICIPATION CAP. A third bound beside risk and capital: you
//      cannot be most of the tape without becoming the price. §7 concedes it
//      — "fill quality degrades with size on sub-20M float".
//   5. §8 DAILY RISK LIMITS — absent from V9 entirely. All five rules, plus
//      a daily trade cap. The 20% drawdown walkaway is evaluated FIRST and
//      INDEPENDENTLY of the four daily latches: chained behind them it is
//      close to unreachable, because a 20% account drawdown is always
//      assembled out of days that trip the 6% daily loss first.
//   6. Two §6 hard exits V9 scored but never acted on — large topping tail
//      and stalling momentum. They route through V9's single flatten flag,
//      because competing strategy.close calls were a defect V9 already fixed.
//   7. §6 scale ladder 50/25/25 rather than 50/50, with V9's whole-share
//      discipline: below 4 shares it collapses back to two legs, and
//      useThirdRung=false restores exact V9 behaviour.
//
// Every addition is input-gated and defaults ON. Turning all of them off
// reproduces V9.12.
//
// NOT compiled. Written and checked statically; paste into the TradingView
// editor before trusting it.
// ============================================================================

// ============================================================================
// V11.1 CODEX CORRECTION CANDIDATE (2026-08-21)
// Static audit only — NOT TradingView-compiled. Material corrections:
//   1. Experimental fast/uptrend lanes and narrative exits default OFF.
//   2. The evidenced 07:00-11:30 window defaults ON; with the honest venue
//      default, the executable emulator window is effectively 09:30-11:30.
//   3. Unknown or symbol-unbound float fails closed; it cannot score 4/4.
//   4. Pullback index no longer resets at every new HOD.
//   5. Confluence is measured at the pullback low, not merely near the close.
//   6. Participation is prior-bar based and fails closed while unavailable;
//      every lane is subject to it and to the §8 governor.
//   7. Cash sizing uses available simulated/account equity, reserves fixed
//      order commissions, and removes the unrelated "third trade today"
//      half-size proxy.
//   8. Entry is a capped stop-limit by default. It models missed gap fills
//      instead of assuming an unlimited stop-market chase.
//   9. Same-bar/multi-leg ambiguity is counted once per entry, and closed-
//      only round trips reconstruct their own result record.
//  10. The §8 governor counts entries, evaluates equity continuously, and
//      flattens a live position when a configured loss lock is reached.
//  11. Dashboard language now exposes proxy provenance, confluence, stressed
//      risk, commissions and the actual 50/25/25 ladder.
// ============================================================================

// ============================================================================
// ROSS FIRST PULLBACK + HOD RETEST — revision V8.0 (2026-08-20).
// V6 answered the external adversarial audit (20 findings) — the map is in
// knowledge-base/tradingview/AUDIT-RESPONSE-V6.md. V7 implements the
// reviewer's follow-up: honest venue modelling (no fictional pre-market
// stop/market fills), provenance-gated scanner criteria, RVOL-at-time
// instead of the full-day-denominator proxy, and a daily flat cutoff.
// V8 closes the re-audit residuals (the V6 re-audit scored 6 fixed / 12
// partial / 1 unfixed / 1 regressed). Every V8 change is marked // V8:
//   1. Zombie display killed: the dashboard derives an EFFECTIVE state from
//      the varip cancel latch — a cancelled order can no longer show BUY.
//   2. Exactly-once fill handling: entries are counted/alerted once per
//      unique entry bar via a varip latch; same-minute round trips are
//      counted from the monotonic closed-trades stream.
//   3. Protective exits are PRE-STAGED with the entry order, so a
//      historical bar that touches trigger and stop no longer finishes long.
//   4. Orders die BEFORE the boundary: no arming on the last in-window bar,
//      pending orders cancelled on it, positions flattened at the edge
//      unless overnight is explicitly allowed.
//   5. Virgin-IDLE uptrend lane reachable (na(stateStartBar) handled).
//   6. Fast-lane signal-bar volume counted once.
//   7. Retest requires a two-sided touch band (deep undercut rejected) and
//      a consumed retest frees the episode for the next breakout.
//   8. confirmedPass now gates EVERY authoritative state/entry block, so a
//      user re-enabling calc_on_order_fills in Properties cannot double-run
//      signal logic on a fill recalculation.
//   9. One flatten per execution: session-edge and bailout closes share a
//      single flattenRequested flag and one authoritative reason.
//  10. ATR-stop provenance persisted at arm time (plannedUsesATRStop).
//  11. Revision strings unified on REV everywhere (title, alerts, journal).
//  12. Post-T1 dashboard shows the actual runner stop and remaining size.
//  13. Unknown float/RVOL can no longer render an all-green pillar row;
//      na-safe gate reasons (no more "—%" rejection text).
//  14. Ambiguous same-bar sequences are labelled AND counted, and the count
//      is on the dashboard LIMITS row. Strategy Tester expectancy claims
//      remain prohibited while that count is non-zero.
//  15. Sizing slippage assumption is an input (keep = Properties slippage);
//      the SIZE row shows structural AND slippage-stressed cash risk.
//  16. laneHits counts once per CONFIRMED bar (it used to inflate intrabar).
//  17. Historical stop-touch mirror: an ARMED order whose bar touched the
//      stop without filling now dies INVALID on history too (V7's last,
//      never-verified edit — re-implemented and scoped here).
//  18. Whole-share exit legs: T1 sells floor(qty/2), the runner always
//      covers exactly what remains; a 1-share position skips T1.
//  19. Supported-market enforcement: US-listed stocks only arm orders;
//      other symbol types run display-only with a hard banner.
//  20. ENTRY FILLED payload carries a ticker-time-entryBar dedup key, and
//      the manual-vs-order alert channels are documented as mutually
//      exclusive. The key dedups journals; it authorizes nothing.
//  21. The RVOL cell names itself a TradingView same-time proxy and shows
//      numerator vs expected volume; it never claims Warrior parity.
// V8.1 (2026-08-19): the V7.2-7.5 operator layer, re-applied on the V8 core
// (which forked from ~V7.1 and lost it), plus one disclosure forced by the
// real-tape benchmark
// (research/momentum-replication/reports/2026-08-pine-v8-benchmark.md):
//   a. GHOST SIGNALS (V7.3-7.4): pattern valid and only the clock refusing
//      -> the chart says SEEN and the PLAN row fills, with NO order placed.
//   b. Ghost freshness (V7.5, live CDTG staleness bug): a ghost plan dies
//      after 10 bars and at every session/day boundary.
//   c. THE CLOCK IS NOT A VERDICT CRITERION (operator directive): session/
//      venue/last-bar are gone from gateReason and the STATUS verdict; they
//      live on the TREND row's Clock lamp and the PLAN row's tag.
//   d. PLAN + SIZE from one 5-source chain (position > working order > live
//      candidate > fresh ghost > "if bought here") so the two rows can
//      never describe different trades (V7.5).
//   e. Gates split into SETUP (is THIS dip tradeable) and TREND (is the
//      tape behind it); the pillars renamed STOCK FIT — selection, not
//      timing (V7.5). NOT A PLAYBOOK STOCK banner when price/liquidity
//      fail the universe; INVALID/DONE verdicts age in candles (V7.2).
//   f. COMMISSION DISCLOSURE (benchmark, 330 real ticker-days): at $20
//      risk with $1/order commission, a stop-out costs $2 and a full
//      T1+runner ladder $3 — 10-15% of the risk budget on EVERY trade.
//      The $100k paper basis hid this toll; the $2,000 basis pays it.
//      Shown on the SIZE (worst case) and LIMITS rows.
// V8.2 (live CDTG + JZ screenshots, 2026-08-20): three operator-reported
// defects, each with the mechanism named:
//   1. LATE JOIN. The impulse scanner could only SEE a push on a bar that
//      was itself the green peak. When the machine was busy (lane trade ->
//      bailout -> DONE) while the peak printed, it returned to IDLE inside
//      the dip and called the rest of the day "(no dip yet)" — the CDTG
//      13:32-35 pullback was real and never assessed. A new block joins a
//      dip already in progress (peak <= maxPullbackBars back, push gates
//      pass on the completed window, retrace still ok) as a normal
//      PULLBACK — same fields, same gates, same arm path, same bar.
//   2. LIQUIDITY is judged on the best of the 5-bar burst, the 20-bar
//      average and the DAY average $/min. The old 20-bar-only measure
//      called CDTG "too thin ($17.6k/min)" 40 minutes after it traded
//      millions — a decayed average vetoing a stock that qualified.
//   3. The NOT A PLAYBOOK STOCK banner no longer REPLACES the status. It
//      shows in full only when the machine is idle and flat; any live
//      state (MOVE UP, DIP FORMING, a finished trade) keeps its dynamic
//      verdict, with a short "not a playbook stock" suffix when relevant.
// V9.0 (DISPLAY-REDESIGN-BRIEF.md, 2026-08-20) — display + sizing layer
// only; the execution core is untouched:
//   1. CLOCK row splits two different clocks: market phase (pre-market /
//      OPEN / after-hours) vs THIS strategy's arming window. A chart whose
//      inputs carry a stale "window off" override now says so in red —
//      TradingView preserves per-chart input overrides across updates.
//   2. Sizing basis is the source's rule (PARAMETERS.md §7, n=125): risk
//      2% of account per trade by default, flat-$ beginner path kept
//      ($50, §7). The SIZE row shows the DERIVATION — risk/share, budget,
//      slip reserve, % of account — no number without its origin.
//   3. Two-layer chart: the decision layer (plan lines, HOD, one compact
//      marker per event class, short order codes) always on; everything
//      else (AMBIGUOUS SEQ labels, SEEN ghosts, S/R fan, EMA/VWAP lines)
//      behind one DIAGNOSTIC toggle, default off. The ambiguity COUNT
//      stays on LIMITS regardless — the audit artifact is never lost.
//   4. Verdict verbs: BUY >x.xx / WAIT — reason / NO — reason / MANAGE.
//      One of the four is always present; VERDICT, PLAN and SIZE render
//      one text size up from the reference rows.
// V9.1 (operator, live BTCT 2026-08-20): the criteria GRID. Every
//      criterion is its own table cell — green chip met, orange failed,
//      slate · not judgeable — and a row whose judged chips are all green
//      paints its TITLE green, so the left column alone reads the board.
//      SIZE cut to what was asked: shares, $ position vs equity, risk $.
//      Palette unified (TV green/orange), bordered cells, merged text rows.
// V9.2 (operator, live PCLA 2026-08-20):
//   a. Sizing reads the ACCOUNT's equity (accountEquity input; 0 = auto
//      strategy.equity, so the 2% rule compounds), never the strategy's
//      initial_capital default. SIZE labels the % as the POSITION's share
//      of equity — it was read as the sizing rule.
//   b. ADRs (syminfo.type "dr") are supported — the venue gate rejected
//      NASDAQ-listed PCLA outright, and foreign ADRs are a large part of
//      the small-cap momentum universe.
//   c. The table holds exactly the rows currently shown (rebuilt on row-
//      set changes) — no blank rows; ONE text size everywhere; PLAN tags
//      cut to two words and "if bought HERE" removed.
//   d. HIGH OF DAY names the front/back side: % off the high, and >=20%
//      off prints BACK SIDE in orange — the move-is-over fact the row
//      used to leave silent (PCLA: HOD 11.33, price 7.99, said nothing).
// V9.3 (operator, live MMA 2026-08-20): HALT BAND and DASH LANE rows
//      retired — the halt band's decision fact (unenforceable stop) is a
//      red warning on SIZE when it fires; the lane row's (his 2+ hits
//      rule) is a chip on STOCK FIT. LIMITS cut to one clause. BUY/STOP/
//      TGT in Unicode bold capitals. Float/Rvol chips colour from the
//      MEASURED value (typed float, warmed TV proxy) while score and
//      gates stay fail-closed on provenance.
// V9.4 (operator step-back, live MMA + Top Gainers export 2026-08-20):
//   a. S/R fan back on the DECISION layer (2 clean levels each side +
//      prev close) — hiding key levels behind diagnostics was over-
//      cleaning. PRE-MARKET HIGH added as a first-class level.
//   b. Hypothetical stop is STRUCTURAL (under the 5-bar swing low, never
//      tighter than 1 fallback-ATR) — the bare ATR stop read too narrow,
//      and its 2R target inherited the narrowness.
//   c. Float/RVOL vs the Warrior export: Pine cannot read float at all
//      (type it; scripts/chart_card.py prints it from the export), and
//      Warrior's "Rel Vol Daily Rate" is a DIFFERENT measure from the TV
//      same-time proxy — neither is wrong, they are not the same number.
//      Full coverage map: knowledge-base/tradingview/STRATEGY-COVERAGE.md
// V9.5 (live WYHG 2026-08-20): S/R POLARITY — supports were drawn only
//      from pivot lows and resistances only from pivot highs, so a broken
//      resistance shelf under price (support by polarity) never printed.
//      Both pivot kinds now feed both sides; price decides the role. The
//      5-bar pivot confirmation lag is inherent and stays (a level is not
//      a level until the market has rejected it).
// V9.6 (operator): automatic TREND LINES. Downtrend = swing-high anchor
//      through the latest lower high (the breakout line); uptrend = swing-
//      low anchor through the latest higher low (the trend-loss line).
//      Extended right, labelled, and the label flips to BROKEN/LOST the
//      bar the close crosses the line.
// V9.7 (live AAPL runtime error, bar 7214): trend lines draw in
//      xloc.bar_time from times stored at pivot confirmation — an old
//      bar_index coordinate resolves through the time series' history
//      buffer and blew past it. Anchors search only the last tlPivots
//      pivots so the lines track the CURRENT leg; a broken line renders
//      dashed and dim. AAPL itself is out of universe by design ($2-20):
//      the NO verdict there is correct, not a miss.
// V9.8 (live USDE): TANGENT trend lines. The two-pivot line could cut
//      through price between its anchors; the tangent (anchor at the
//      window extreme, steepest slope keeping every confirmed bar on the
//      right side) touches structure and cannot cross it — only live
//      price can break it, which IS the signal. No trend in the window =
//      no line, instead of a wrong line.
// V9.9 (live JUNS): trend lines are DAY-SCOPED — arrays reset at the
//      day boundary, so anchors are today's low / today's high, never an
//      overnight print from yesterday. The session defines the window,
//      which adapts the lines to any timeframe by construction.
// V9.10 (live SDOT): trend-line ANCHORS are scored, not assumed. On a
//      name that doubled intraday the tangent from the session low sat
//      $5 under price — right geometry, dead leg. Every candidate swing
//      anchor is scored on touches (bars sitting ON the line, 0.2 ATR)
//      minus distance-from-price in ATR, and the best line is drawn; no
//      candidate with >= 2 touches means no line.
// V9.11 (operator): TRADE RESULT markers. TradingView's own trade
//      labels print the SHARE COUNT beside each order ("+146", "-73"),
//      which reads like money and is not — a winning exit can show a
//      negative number. BOUGHT <price> / SOLD <price> + $ + % + R now
//      say the result in words, one label per side, share count absent.
//      Turn TV's off: Settings -> Style -> uncheck "Trades on chart".
// V9.12 (operator): the 07:00-11:30 HARD WINDOW IS OFF BY DEFAULT. The
//      script now arms whenever the pattern is valid, at any hour. The
//      input remains — switching it on restores the previous behaviour
//      and re-enables the ghost layer. Flatten-at-cutoff and flatten-at-
//      day-end are unchanged: this drops the entry window, not the
//      no-overnight rule. Evidence on both sides is cited at the input.
// NOT COMPILED HERE: TradingView is the only compiler. Paste, compile, then
// run the manual regression list (repo AUDIT-RESPONSE-V6.md + V8 additions)
// on replay before trusting any number this file prints.
// NOTE: the "//@version=6" line above is the PINE LANGUAGE version, not this
// script's revision. Our revision is the REV constant below and the V4.x tags.
// V3 audited against this repo's measured rules.
// Audit + divergence table: reports/2026-08-pine-v3-audit.md. V3 archived
// alongside. Changes are marked  // V4:  with origin + evidence status.
//
// SCOPE EXCLUSION (design pack): this script sees ONE chart. Float, catalyst,
// gap context, dilution, live halt state — the entire Layer 0/1 reject
// cascade — live OUTSIDE it (./now --scan). This is a Layer-2 TRIGGER tool
// for a name that already survived selection. It qualifies nothing.
//
// PAPER ONLY. Backtest fills on halting low-floats are optimistic: stop
// orders fill AT the stop in simulation and through gaps in reality
// (MSGY resumed +15% from its halt price, 2026-08-14). slippage=10 ticks
// is the V4 default (V3 had 1); re-run any result at 5/10/20/25 before
// believing it. Nothing here establishes profitability — the repo's own
// 894-session replication was negative expectancy.
// ============================================================================

// ───────────────────────────── Inputs ─────────────────────────────
gImpulse = "1. Impulse"
minPushPct          = input.float(5.0, "Minimum push %", minval=0.5, maxval=30.0, step=0.5, group=gImpulse, display = display.none)
minImpulseBars      = input.int(1, "Minimum impulse bars", minval=1, maxval=6, group=gImpulse, display = display.none)
minPushATR          = input.float(2.0, "Minimum push (ATR)", minval=0.25, maxval=20.0, step=0.25, group=gImpulse, display = display.none)
maxImpulseBars      = input.int(6, "Detection lookback bars", minval=1, maxval=12, group=gImpulse, display = display.none)
// V4: LOCAL_ADDITION carried over from V3, evidence_status UNTESTED — no
// corpus source for an efficiency floor. Kept because it filters chop the
// eye would also reject; flagged so nobody mistakes it for a Ross rule.
minEfficiency       = input.float(0.60, "Minimum directional efficiency [UNTESTED local]", minval=0.0, maxval=1.0, step=0.05, group=gImpulse, display = display.none)
volumeBaselineBars  = input.int(20, "Volume baseline bars", minval=5, maxval=100, group=gImpulse, display = display.none)
minPushRVOL         = input.float(2.0, "Minimum push/local-volume ratio", minval=0.5, maxval=20.0, step=0.25, group=gImpulse,
     tooltip="Average volume on the detected push divided by the prior local 20-bar SMA baseline. This is NOT RVOL-at-time; calling it RVOL overstated what it measures (reviewer).", display = display.none)
// V4: LOCAL_ADDITION, UNTESTED — $ volume floor has no corpus source (the
// closest is "1M+ session shares", a different object). Kept, flagged.
minDollarVolume     = input.float(100000.0, "Minimum avg $ volume / min [UNTESTED local]", minval=0.0, step=25000.0, group=gImpulse, display = display.none)

gPullback = "2. First pullback"
minPullbackBars     = input.int(1, "Minimum pullback bars", minval=1, maxval=3, group=gPullback, display = display.none)
// V4: default 3 -> 4. A pullback DURATION cap is a LOCAL_ADDITION (the
// source's "3rd pullback" rule is about pullback NUMBER, handled below);
// loosened one bar so a slow flag is not auto-rejected. UNTESTED.
maxPullbackBars     = input.int(4, "Maximum pullback bars [local, was 3]", minval=1, maxval=6, group=gPullback, display = display.none)
maxRetracementPct   = input.float(50.0, "Maximum retracement %", minval=10.0, maxval=90.0, step=1.0, group=gPullback, display = display.none)
maxPBVolumeRatio    = input.float(0.70, "Maximum pullback / push volume", minval=0.10, maxval=2.0, step=0.05, group=gPullback, display = display.none)
bullishLowerWickPct = input.float(30.0, "Good lower wick %", minval=0.0, maxval=100.0, step=5.0, group=gPullback, display = display.none)
toppingTailWarnPct  = input.float(40.0, "Upper wick warning %", minval=0.0, maxval=100.0, step=5.0, group=gPullback, display = display.none)

gMomentum = "3. Momentum"
requireMACD          = input.bool(true, "Require MACD > 0 and histogram > 0", group=gMomentum, display = display.none)
// V4: defaults OFF -> ON. Origin SOURCE: FILTERS.md Layer 2 requires
// price > VWAP and price > EMA9 at entry — they are chart gates, not
// options. V3 shipped them off, which tests a different strategy.
requireEMA           = input.bool(true, "Require close > EMA9 and EMA9 >= EMA20", group=gMomentum, display = display.none)
requireVWAP          = input.bool(true, "Require close > VWAP", group=gMomentum, display = display.none)

gSession = "4. Session (SOURCE: broker-split stats + book ch.3)"
// V4: NEW, default ON. The measured profit curve starts at 07:00 ET and the
// hard stop is 11:30; V3's "no time filter" backtests 15:00 chop as if it
// were 09:45. Needs extended-hours ON on the chart to see 07:00-09:30.
// V4.4: WITHDRAWN as a default hard gate per operator request 2026-08-15 —
// recorded, not deleted (design pack). The verdict now prints at every
// moment; off-window bars are tagged "· off-window" instead of blocked.
// Re-enable this input to restore the hard gate. Origin of the window
// itself stays SOURCE (profit curve starts 07:00, hard stop 11:30).
// V7 (reviewer): the hard window returns as the DEFAULT. This reverses the
// operator's V4.4 "verdict at every moment" default on the reviewer's venue
// argument: outside RTH the real venue is limit-orders-only (extended-hours
// SKILL.md), so the emulator's pre-market stop/market fills are fiction and
// a backtest containing them tests a strategy nobody can execute. The
// verdict still PRINTS at every moment — only ARMING is gated. Flip this
// input off to restore V4.4 behaviour knowingly.
// V9.12 (operator): the 07:00-11:30 window is OFF by default — the script
// arms whenever the pattern is valid, all session. Evidence both ways, so
// the switch stays: FOR dropping it, his own longest live session ran
// 12:00-16:00 and produced ~$65k of ~$78k, and the real rule reads as
// conditional — midday is dead UNLESS a monster is live
// (research/momentum-replication/reports/2026-08-ispo-stream.md).
// AGAINST, measured here: the afternoon setups this now takes were 5W/26L,
// -9.47R hypothetical over 11 days
// (research/momentum-replication/reports/2026-08-pine-v8-benchmark.md).
// Turning it back on restores the old behaviour exactly; the ghost layer
// (SEEN markers, plan without an order) only exists while it is ON.
// Day-trading discipline does NOT depend on this input: positions still
// flatten at the daily cutoff and at the day's end.
useSessionWindow     = input.bool(true, "HARD-gate: only arm inside 07:00-11:30 ET [evidence default]", group=gSession,
     tooltip="The repo's own 11-day audit found the added afternoon set at 5W/26L, -9.47R. With premarket emulator fills disabled, executable paper orders are effectively limited to 09:30-11:30 ET.", display = display.none)
sessionWindow        = input.session("0700-1130", "Window (exchange tz)", group=gSession, display = display.none)
allowPremarketEmulatorFills = input.bool(false, "Allow optimistic premarket stop/market fills [EXPERIMENTAL]", group=gSession,
     tooltip="Default OFF: the documented extended-hours venue is limit-orders-only, so simulated stop/market fills there are optimistic fiction. Pre-market stays visible for study; orders arm only in RTH unless you explicitly accept invalid fill modelling.", display = display.none)
allowOvernightPositions = input.bool(false, "Allow positions past the daily flat cutoff", group=gSession, display = display.none)
dailyFlatHour        = input.int(15, "Daily flat cutoff hour ET", minval=0, maxval=23, group=gSession, display = display.none)
dailyFlatMinute      = input.int(58, "Daily flat cutoff minute ET", minval=0, maxval=59, group=gSession, display = display.none)

gScan = "5a. Scanner criteria (V5 — mirrors Day Trade Dash)"
// V5: the strategy answered WHEN and was blind to WHETHER THE NAME QUALIFIES,
// so the operator had to hold the scanner state in their head. These mirror
// the Day Trade Dash sub-strategies documented in
// knowledge-base/daytrade-dash/PLAYBOOK.md. They are DISPLAY-ONLY by default:
// selection happens before the chart, and a chart-side gate would re-commit
// this project's most common error class (scanner dial used as a trade gate).
// V12.2 (operator: "the highlighted part serves for nothing ... remove them
// if no interest for the verdict"). Correct. The STOCK FIT row is DISPLAY
// ONLY: scanGates defaults off, so none of Price / Float~ / TV pace / Gap
// can block or permit a trade, and its detail string ("-.2% · TV-EWMA 4.1x
// (8.75M/1.99M exp) · float ?") is the widest text in the panel — it sets
// the width of column 6, which is why the Conf and §8 chips rendered as
// bars stretched across half the table. Off by default; the selection facts
// live in the STOCK FIT panel when you want them.
showScanPanel        = input.bool(false, "Show scanner-criteria panel (display only)", group=gScan, display = display.none)
scanGates            = input.bool(false, "Also VETO when criteria fail [off = display only]", group=gScan, display = display.none)
manualFloatM         = input.float(0.0, "Float (millions, 0 = unknown)", minval=0.0, step=0.1, group=gScan,
     tooltip="Pine has NO float field — TradingView does not expose it to scripts. Type it from Day Trade Dash / finviz; `python3 scripts/chart_card.py <export.csv> SYM` prints it (and the RVOL context) from a Top Gainers export.", display = display.none)
floatTicker          = input.string("", "Float applies to ticker", group=gScan,
     tooltip="Required symbol binding for a manual float, e.g. MSS. Switching charts without changing this field makes float UNKNOWN instead of silently reusing another company's number.", display = display.none)
// V7 (reviewer): a typed number is not a verified number. Float counts as
// KNOWN for gating only when its provenance is stated; a manual unverified
// value still displays, labelled, but gates as unknown.
floatSource          = input.string("Unknown", "Float provenance",
     options=["Unknown", "SEC filing verified", "Trusted feed verified", "Manual unverified"], group=gScan,
     tooltip="Pine has no authoritative float field. A number is counted as verified only when its provenance is explicitly SEC filing or trusted feed.", display = display.none)
// ── V12.17 §4 CATALYST — the fifth pillar ────────────────────────────────
// The mastery bundle names five pillars: price, change, relative volume,
// float and CATALYST. This script scored four. Pine cannot read a newswire,
// so the catalyst is operator-supplied and fail-closed exactly like the
// float: it counts only when confirmed, bound to THIS ticker, and given a
// provenance. Switching symbols without updating the binding fails closed
// rather than carrying yesterday's news onto a new chart.
//
// Confirmed (Preview ch.1-6): breaking news is PREFERRED BUT NOT MANDATORY --
// a technical breakout can supply the justification. So the catalyst raises
// the score and the grade; it is never a hard veto on its own.
catalystConfirmed    = input.bool(false, "Catalyst confirmed for this ticker", group=gScan, display = display.none,
     tooltip="Read the headline, its exact time and its source before ticking this. A promotional release is not a catalyst.")
catalystTicker       = input.string("", "Catalyst applies to ticker", group=gScan, display = display.none,
     tooltip="Symbol binding, e.g. MSS. Without a match the catalyst pillar fails closed.")
catalystAgeH         = input.float(0.0, "Catalyst age (hours since the headline)", minval=0.0, maxval=240.0, step=0.25, group=gScan, display = display.none,
     tooltip="Drives the flame equivalent: red 0-2h, orange 2-12h, yellow 12-24h, none beyond 24h. The flame is a NEWS-AGE clock only -- it is not a compliance score.")
catalystSource       = input.string("Unknown", "Catalyst provenance", group=gScan, display = display.none,
     options=["Unknown", "Company PR / newswire", "SEC filing", "Reputable media", "Chat/rumour"],
     tooltip="Chat or rumour never counts as a verified catalyst.")

// V7 (reviewer): TradingView's volume feed is not Warrior's. The RVOL pillar
// GATES only when the operator has acknowledged the feed and bound that
// acknowledgement to this exchange prefix — switching symbols fails closed.
scanFeedVerified     = input.bool(false, "Acknowledge TV feed/session for RVOL gating", group=gScan,
     tooltip="Manual acknowledgement only — it does not prove parity with Warrior. Gating also requires the exchange-prefix binding and a named feed source below.", display = display.none)
scanFeedPrefix       = input.string("", "Feed acknowledgement exchange prefix", group=gScan,
     tooltip="Bind the acknowledgement to the current syminfo.prefix, e.g. NASDAQ. A different prefix fails closed.", display = display.none)
scanFeedSource       = input.string("Unknown", "Acknowledged TradingView feed",
     options=["Unknown", "Cboe One/free", "Consolidated/paid", "Other paid/validated"], group=gScan,
     tooltip="Record which TradingView feed was checked. Even Consolidated/paid remains a TV proxy, not Warrior's Daily Rate.", display = display.none)
rvolLookbackDays     = input.int(30, "TV pace EWMA baseline days", minval=10, maxval=60, group=gScan,
     tooltip="Exponential same-minute chart-session baseline, not an exact rolling mean and not Warrior Daily Rate. Gating waits for this many observations in the minute slot.", display = display.none)
scanMinPrice         = input.float(2.0, "Price floor", minval=0.01, step=0.25, group=gScan, display = display.none)
scanMaxPrice         = input.float(20.0, "Price ceiling", minval=0.5, step=1.0, group=gScan, display = display.none)
// MEASURED 2026-08-18: the platform fired Former Momo at daily RVOL 2.13, its
// loosest lane. 5.0 is the teaching dial; as a hard floor it deletes the
// population the method hunts.
scanMinRVOL          = input.float(2.0, "USER TV RVOL-at-time proxy floor [UNCALIBRATED]", minval=0.1, step=0.25, group=gScan,
     tooltip="Applied to TradingView same-time cumulative-volume pace only. No validated mapping to Warrior Daily Rate exists (the 2.13 Former Momo observation is a DIFFERENT metric on a DIFFERENT feed); collect matched timestamp pairs before treating this threshold as predictive.", display = display.none)
scanMinGap           = input.float(10.0, "Premarket mark / RTH-open gap floor %", minval=0.0, step=1.0, group=gScan,
     tooltip="Before 09:30 ET this tests the live premarket mark against prior close. From 09:30 on it tests the FROZEN RTH-open gap, so the pillar stops drifting with intraday price.", display = display.none)
// MEASURED: low-float branches fired at 8.40M, medium included 41.92M, so the
// real tier boundary is bracketed to (8.40, 41.92]. 20 sits inside it —
// consistent with observation, NOT confirmed by it.
scanLowFloatMaxM     = input.float(20.0, "Low-float ceiling M [bracketed 8.4-41.9]", minval=0.1, step=1.0, group=gScan, display = display.none)

gRetest = "5b. HOD break-and-retest (V5)"
// SOURCE, register STREAMS: "where it broke through it, it got above it, it
// retests it, and then if it can hold it" — YuNvqwJftVY @00:22:37.
// Default ON: V4 skipped this setup entirely, which is the reported symptom.
enableRetest         = input.bool(true, "Enable HOD break-and-retest entries", group=gRetest, display = display.none)
retestTolATR         = input.float(0.25, "Retest tolerance (x ATR)", minval=0.02, maxval=2.0, step=0.01, group=gRetest, display = display.none)
retestStopBufferTicks = input.int(1, "Retest stop below broken HOD (ticks)", minval=1, maxval=20, group=gRetest,
     tooltip="The retest stop is forced BELOW the reclaimed level — never left above the support the setup claims to trade against (reviewer).", display = display.none)

gStructure = "5. Structure / reward"
requireRRtoPeak      = input.bool(false, "Require minimum room to impulse peak", group=gStructure, display = display.none)
minRRtoPeak          = input.float(2.0, "Minimum R to impulse peak", minval=0.0, maxval=10.0, step=0.25, group=gStructure, display = display.none)
supportTolerancePct  = input.float(0.35, "Support tolerance %", minval=0.05, maxval=3.0, step=0.05, group=gStructure, display = display.none)
supportToleranceATR  = input.float(0.20, "Support tolerance ATR", minval=0.05, maxval=2.0, step=0.05, group=gStructure, display = display.none)

gRisk = "6. Risk / sizing"
// V8: defaults rebased to the $2,000 account. $20 = 1% risk per trade;
// $2,000 max position = cash account, no leverage. The old pair (200 /
// 25,000) was 10% risk and 12.5x account value — presented as executable
// sizing, it was the single most dangerous default in the file.
// V9 (defect 2): the source's sizing rule, measured — PARAMETERS.md §7:
// risk 2% of account per trade (n=125; 3-5% also stated), $50 flat for the
// beginner path (n=125). shares = risk_budget / risk_per_share. The old
// $20 default was 1% — a local choice presented as if it were the rule.
riskMode             = input.string("% of account (source: 2%)", "Risk basis", options=["% of account (source: 2%)", "Flat $ (beginner path)"], group=gRisk,
     tooltip="PARAMETERS.md §7: risk_pct_per_trade = 2.0% of account (n=125); risk_flat_beginner = $50 (n=125).", display = display.none)
riskPctInput         = input.float(2.0, "Risk % of account per trade [source: 2%]", minval=0.1, maxval=10.0, step=0.25, group=gRisk, display = display.none)
riskFlatInput        = input.float(50.0, "Flat $ risk per trade [source: $50 beginner]", minval=1.0, step=5.0, group=gRisk, display = display.none)
// V9.2 (operator): size from the ACCOUNT's equity, not the strategy's
// initial_capital default. 0 = automatic: strategy.equity (initial capital
// plus this strategy's own simulated P&L, so the 2% rule compounds). Set
// it explicitly to match a broker/paper account Pine cannot see.
accountEquity        = input.float(0.0, "Account equity $ (0 = auto: strategy equity)", minval=0.0, step=100.0, group=gRisk, display = display.none)
equityBase           = accountEquity > 0 ? accountEquity : strategy.equity
riskBudget           = riskMode == "Flat $ (beginner path)" ? riskFlatInput : equityBase * riskPctInput / 100.0
maxPositionValue     = input.float(2000.0, "Maximum position value $ [cash account]", minval=100.0, step=100.0, group=gRisk, display = display.none)
// V9: accountSize input retired — the dashboard reads
// strategy.initial_capital directly, which Pine CAN read back.
// V8: the sizing stress assumption is now an input so testing another
// slippage setting cannot silently desynchronise sizing from the emulator.
slipTicksInput       = input.int(10, "Slippage assumption (ticks) — MUST match Properties slippage", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gRisk,
     tooltip="Pine cannot read the strategy() slippage= argument back. Sizing budgets adverse slippage on BOTH the stop entry and the stop exit: 2 x this many ticks per share.", display = display.none)
maxStopPct           = input.float(3.0, "Maximum structural stop %", minval=0.25, maxval=20.0, step=0.25, group=gRisk, display = display.none)
maxStopATR           = input.float(1.5, "Maximum structural stop ATR", minval=0.25, maxval=10.0, step=0.25, group=gRisk, display = display.none)
useMaxDollarStop     = input.bool(false, "Also enforce maximum $ stop", group=gRisk, display = display.none)
maxStopDollar        = input.float(0.20, "Maximum $ stop", minval=0.01, maxval=20.0, step=0.01, group=gRisk, display = display.none)
// V4: NEW. Origin SOURCE (book halt-band table), evidence REASONED_NOT_
// MEASURED: a stop wider than the LULD band cannot be honoured — price
// halts before reaching it and reopens wherever the auction says.
haltBandVeto         = input.bool(false, "Veto from LULD-width heuristic [OFF; not a live band]", group=gRisk,
     tooltip="Pine cannot observe the live LULD reference price, band state, pauses or reopen auction. This prior-close tier approximation is display/research only by default.", display = display.none)

// ── V11 (from V10): §3 gate fidelity ───────────────────────────────────────
gV11c = "§3 confluence and pullback index (V11)"
requireConfluence    = input.bool(true,  "Require §3 support confluence", group=gV11c,
     tooltip="V9 computed supportCount and spent it only on the display-only quality score, so a dip that stopped at no level could still arm. §3 is explicit: two independent reasons, not one.", display = display.none)
minConfluence        = input.int(2, "Minimum confluence reasons [source: 2]", minval=1, maxval=6, group=gV11c, display = display.none)
requirePullbackIndex = input.bool(true,  "Require 1st or 2nd pullback only", group=gV11c,
     tooltip="§3 pullback_index <= 2. Distinct from pullbackBars, which counts how many BARS the dip lasts.", display = display.none)
maxPullbackIndex     = input.int(2, "Maximum pullback index [source: 2]", minval=1, maxval=5, group=gV11c, display = display.none)

// ── V11 (from V10): §7 participation cap ───────────────────────────────────
gV11p = "§7 participation (V11)"
useParticipationCap  = input.bool(true, "Cap size by share of the tape", group=gV11p,
     tooltip="§7 concedes it: fill quality degrades with size on sub-20M float and the edge does not scale linearly. Without this a backtest reports fills that never existed.", display = display.none)
participationPct     = input.float(10.0, "Max % of median minute volume", minval=0.5, maxval=100.0, step=0.5, group=gV11p, display = display.none)
participationLen     = input.int(20, "Volume lookback (bars)", minval=5, maxval=200, group=gV11p, display = display.none)

// ── V11 (from V10): §8 daily risk limits — absent from V9 entirely ─────────
gV11r = "§8 daily risk limits (V11)"
useRiskGovernor      = input.bool(true,  "Enforce §8 daily limits", group=gV11r,
     tooltip="§8's five rules. V9 had none of them, so a losing day compounded instead of stopping.", display = display.none)
maxTradesPerDay      = input.int(2,    "Max trades per day [source: 1-2]", minval=1, maxval=20, group=gV11r, display = display.none)
maxDailyLossPct      = input.float(6.0,  "Max daily loss %",        minval=0.5, maxval=50.0, step=0.5, group=gV11r, display = display.none)
givebackPct          = input.float(50.0, "Giveback % of peak gain", minval=10.0, maxval=100.0, step=5.0, group=gV11r, display = display.none)
useGreenToRed        = input.bool(true,  "Stop if the day goes green to red", group=gV11r, display = display.none)
consecLossMax        = input.int(3,    "Consecutive losses to stop", minval=2, maxval=10, group=gV11r, display = display.none)
ddWalkawayPct        = input.float(20.0, "Drawdown walkaway % from equity high", minval=5.0, maxval=90.0, step=1.0, group=gV11r, display = display.none)

// ── V11 (from V10): §6 exits V9 scored but never acted on ─────────────────
gV11x = "§6 additional hard exits (V11)"
useToppingTailExit   = input.bool(false, "Exit on a large topping tail [UNVALIDATED]", group=gV11x,
     tooltip="Narrative rule, not yet supported by an isolated out-of-sample ablation. Default OFF until it improves net expectancy without unacceptable drawdown or trade deletion.", display = display.none)
useStallExit         = input.bool(false, "Exit on shrinking green candles [UNVALIDATED]", group=gV11x,
     tooltip="Narrative rule, not yet supported by an isolated out-of-sample ablation. Default OFF.", display = display.none)
useThirdRung         = input.bool(true, "Scale 50/25/25 instead of 50/50", group=gV11x,
     tooltip="§6: scale_1_pct 50, scale_2_pct 25, runner_pct 25.", display = display.none)

gExecution = "7. Entry / exit"
breakoutBufferTicks  = input.int(1, "Breakout buffer ticks [UNTESTED local]", minval=0, maxval=20, group=gExecution, display = display.none)
rewardMultiple       = input.float(2.0, "Profit target (R)", minval=0.5, maxval=10.0, step=0.25, group=gExecution, display = display.none)
bailoutEnabled       = input.bool(true, "Enable breakout-or-bailout", group=gExecution, display = display.none)
bailoutBars          = input.int(2, "Full bars allowed to prove momentum", minval=1, maxval=10, group=gExecution, display = display.none)
minimumMFER          = input.float(0.5, "Minimum MFE required (R) [UNTESTED local]", minval=0.0, maxval=5.0, step=0.1, group=gExecution, display = display.none)
bailOnCloseBelowEntry = input.bool(true, "Bail if early bar closes below entry", group=gExecution, display = display.none)
// V5.1: FAST LANE. Reported live (EHGO 2026-08-19): red candles printed inside
// a valid structure, the formal path rejected the pullback on a quality gate,
// price ripped +0.40 with no trigger ever offered. The fast lane arms the
// stop-entry AT THE CLOSE OF ANY RED CANDLE inside an active structure —
// trigger = that candle's high + buffer, stop = its low — so the break fills
// intrabar (calc_on_every_tick) without waiting for another bar to load.
// It still respects: momentum gates, max stop %, halt band (RTH), shares>=1.
// It deliberately skips: push-quality, retracement %, volume ratio. Those
// stay as INFO on the dashboard; the operator sees them and decides.
fastLane             = input.bool(false, "FAST LANE [EXPERIMENTAL]: red candle in structure", group=gExecution,
     tooltip="Default OFF: this lane deliberately bypasses the formal push/retracement/volume definition and therefore must be tested as a separate strategy variant.", display = display.none)
// V5.2: ATR-FALLBACK STOP. Live example (YJ 2026-08-19): the pullback candle
// spanned 2.64->2.41 — a candle-low stop of ~9%% of price, so the RISK gate
// refused and no trigger existed while the bounce paid. The repo's own audit
// already names this failure: "a 1-min signal bar on a halting name can span
// $1+: the candle-low stop is then fiction... Use the ATR stop method on fast
// tape" (knowledge-base/daytrade-dash/README.md, measured medians 0.23-0.83).
// When the candle-low stop breaches maxStopPct/maxStopATR, substitute
// trigger - fallbackATRmult*ATR instead of rejecting, and SAY SO on screen.
atrStopFallback      = input.bool(true, "ATR-fallback stop when candle-low stop too wide", group=gExecution, display = display.none)
fallbackATRmult      = input.float(1.0, "Fallback stop distance (x ATR)", minval=0.25, maxval=5.0, step=0.25, group=gExecution, display = display.none)
// V5.2: UPTREND LANE. YJ again: the 72%% retracement correctly invalidated the
// formal setup (that protection stays), but recovery then required a whole new
// impulse detection while price left. In a confirmed uptrend — MACD, EMA and
// VWAP ALL green, hard-coded, no toggles — a red candle is a micro-pullback
// whatever the state machine happens to call the moment. This is closest to
// what he actually does: he runs no impulse detector; he sees an uptrend, a
// red candle, and the break of its high.
uptrendLane          = input.bool(false, "UPTREND LANE [EXPERIMENTAL]: red candle + momentum", group=gExecution,
     tooltip="Default OFF: this is a generic micro-pullback strategy, not the audited first-pullback setup. Enable only in a separately labelled experiment.", display = display.none)
// V5.4: LANES RESPECT THE HIGH OF DAY. Session evidence (TNON 2026-08-19):
// three lane entries, three stops, every one armed UNDER a lower high with
// the dashboard already showing the warning. This is not a new rule - it is
// V4.10's trapped-supply logic (above the HOD nobody holds a loser;
// js25lIZMUSY @00:22:49) finally applied to the lanes that were bypassing
// it. A lane may arm only when the trigger is at/above the HOD, or has at
// least 1R of open air before it.
lanesRespectHOD      = input.bool(true, "Lanes require new-high or >=1R room to HOD", group=gExecution, display = display.none)
useCappedStopLimit   = input.bool(true, "Entry model: capped stop-limit [conservative]", group=gExecution,
     tooltip="Default ON: after the trigger, do not buy above the cap. This produces missed fills on gaps instead of assuming an unlimited stop-market chase. Historical OHLC still cannot prove intrabar queue order.", display = display.none)
entryCapTicks        = input.int(5, "Entry cap above trigger (ticks)", minval=1, maxval=100, group=gExecution, display = display.none)
commissionPerOrderInput = input.float(1.0, "Commission/order — MUST match Properties", minval=0.0, maxval=20.0, step=0.25, group=gExecution,
     tooltip="Pine cannot read strategy() commission_value back. Sizing reserves entry plus every planned exit order; keep this equal to Properties.", display = display.none)

gVisual = "8. Display"
// ── V12.15 CLEAN CHART ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Operator: "hide the unnecessary arrow shapes in color from the chart."
// On PPCB those green / teal / yellow / red chevrons are these three layers.
// They are plot.style_linebr series, so they redraw on EVERY bar of EVERY
// past setup episode, and because entry/stop/target move while a setup is
// forming, each episode leaves a little coloured tent behind. Nothing is
// lost by hiding them: the live numbers are in the PLAN and SIZE rows of the
// dashboard, which is where an operator reads them anyway. All three remain
// available as toggles.
// V12.25: back ON. V12.15 turned three layers off when the operator asked to
// hide "the arrow shapes in color". Two of them were the clutter he meant --
// the signal markers and the shaded bands. This third one was his TRADE: the
// entry, stop and T1/T2/T3 lines. Hiding it left the plan as text in the
// dashboard with nothing on the chart to trade against. Markers and bands
// stay off; the plan comes back.
showLevels           = input.bool(true, "Show Entry / Stop / Target / Peak", group=gVisual, display = display.none)
// V12.9: the impulse-peak / high-of-day / pre-market-high series are three
// more lines drawn on every bar, and MAIN resistance now NAMES its source
// ("R 3.84 · HOD"), so they say nothing the structure map does not. Default
// off — the operator asked for trend lines and main S/R, not a fan.
showContextPlots     = input.bool(false, "  └ also plot impulse peak / HOD / PM-high series", group=gVisual, display = display.none)
showPriceBands       = input.bool(false, "Show target / stop bands", group=gVisual, display = display.none)
// V4.9: band width was a FIXED tick count, so it did not adapt to the
// instrument or to price zoom — 5 ticks is a hairline on a $9 stock and a
// slab on a $1.70 one. ATR-relative by default; ticks still available.
bandMode             = input.string("ATR fraction", "Band width mode", options=["ATR fraction", "Fixed ticks"], group=gVisual, display = display.none)
bandATRfrac          = input.float(0.12, "Band half-width (× ATR)", minval=0.01, maxval=2.0, step=0.01, group=gVisual, display = display.none)
bandHalfWidthTicks   = input.int(5, "Band half-width (ticks, fixed mode)", minval=1, maxval=100, group=gVisual, display = display.none)
// V4.9.1: plotshape(size=) demands a CONST string — an input-derived value
// is rejected (CE10123). So the choice is a boolean and each size is a
// separate const call. Pine cannot size a glyph from a variable.
showMarkers          = input.bool(false, "Show signal markers", group=gVisual, display = display.none)
bigMarkers           = input.bool(false, "Large signal markers", group=gVisual, display = display.none)
// V4.1: nearest structural levels drawn as bands — resistance above,
// support below, from confirmed swing pivots (his "two reasons at one
// price" needs the level on screen, not in your head).
// V12.5 (operator, sixth report on the same subsystem): the S/R map and the
// trend lines are OFF by default.
//
// This is a stopgap, not a fix. Five attempts have each corrected something
// real — anchors, ylocs, plotshape locations, infinite extends, a capped
// distance penalty — and the operator still reports the levels as wrong. A
// level that MIGHT be wrong is worse than no level: it invites a decision
// against a price that may not be there. Until the drawing layer is rebuilt
// and checked against a live chart, it does not draw.
//
// Nothing the strategy TRADES on is affected: entry, stop, T1/T2/T3, the
// high of day, the position markers and the panel are all independent of
// these two switches.
showSR               = input.bool(true, "  └ MAIN support / resistance", group=gVisual, display = display.none)
// V9.6 (operator): automatic trend lines. Downtrend = the line from the
// swing high across the most recent LOWER high (the breakout line);
// uptrend = from the swing low across the most recent HIGHER low (the
// trend-loss line). Labelled, and flagged the bar price breaks them.
// V12.14: back ON. V12.13 turned diagonals off because V8 had none, but the
// operator wants them -- the ask was never "remove them", it was "make them
// work". Default restored; the distance ceiling below is what keeps them
// honest.
showTrendLine        = input.bool(true, "Draw trend lines (lower-highs / higher-lows)", group=gVisual, display = display.none)
// V9.11 (operator): the trade RESULT in words. TradingView's own trade
// markers print the SHARE COUNT next to each order ("+146", "-73"), which
// reads like a P&L and is not one — a winning exit can show "-73". These
// markers say bought where, sold where, and what it made.
// Turn TradingView's off: strategy Settings -> Style -> uncheck
// "Trades on chart" (and "Quantity"), keep these on.
showTradeResult      = input.bool(true, "Show BOUGHT / SOLD + P&L markers", group=gVisual, display = display.none)
// V12.16 (operator: "for each pattern uptrend or downtrend, the resistance
// and support -- a range for every trend forming"). A single tangent gives
// only the side the trend leans on: an uptrend line is the floor, a downtrend
// line is the ceiling, and neither says where the move runs out. The opposite
// rail is drawn PARALLEL, offset by the largest excursion the other extreme
// made from the fitted line over the same span -- the standard parallel
// channel. Parallel rather than a second independent fit on purpose: two free
// fits can diverge or cross and stop describing one move.
showTrendChannel     = input.bool(true, "Trend lines: draw the opposite rail (channel)", group=gVisual, display = display.none)
fillTrendChannel     = input.bool(true, "  └ shade the channel", group=gVisual, display = display.none)
tlMinBars            = input.int(12, "Trend lines: minimum bars before one can be drawn", minval=6, maxval=120, group=gVisual, display = display.none)
tlAnchorGap          = input.int(4, "Trend lines: keep anchors this many bars off the right edge", minval=2, maxval=30, group=gVisual, display = display.none)
tlLabelOffset        = input.int(6, "Trend lines: label offset (bars right of last)", minval=0, maxval=40, group=gVisual, display = display.none)
tlLookback           = input.int(0, "Trend lines: lookback bars (0 = since day start)", minval=0, maxval=720, group=gVisual,
     tooltip="V9.9: trend lines are day-scoped — the up-line anchors at TODAY's low, the down-line at TODAY's high (tangent: steepest slope keeping every confirmed bar on the right side; it can touch price, never cut it). Set a bar count only to narrow within the day.", display = display.none)
srPivotLen           = input.int(5, "Pivot strength (bars each side)", minval=2, maxval=15, group=gVisual, display = display.none)
// V12.4 (operator, four rounds of "the lines make no sense"): the trend-line
// chooser scored distance from price as a SOFT penalty capped at 20, so a
// line eight ATR away with twelve touches (24 - 20 = 4) beat a line half an
// ATR away with two (4 - 0.5 = 3.5). Nothing anywhere said "if it is nowhere
// near price, do not draw it", which is how a $13.70 stock ended up with
// trend lines at $12.97. A line that far from price describes nothing.
showTrendLines       = input.bool(false, "Show EMA9 / EMA20 / VWAP", group=gVisual, display = display.none)
// V9 (defect 3): ONE switch for everything that is not the trade decision.
// The decision layer (plan lines, HOD, one marker per event class) is
// always on; this reveals the working parts when you want them.
showDiagnostics      = input.bool(false, "DIAGNOSTIC layer: ambiguity labels, ghost SEEN, S/R fan, EMA/VWAP", group=gVisual, display = display.none)
// V12.28 (operator: "give me a fair judgment for the setup rather than all
// these metrics"). Twelve chips across two rows made the reader do the
// summarising. Off = those two rows become plain sentences: one judgment on
// the setup, one naming the pattern. On = the original chip grid.
dashChips            = input.bool(false, "SETUP row: show the six chips instead of one sentence", group=gVisual, display = display.none)
dashFull             = input.bool(false, "Full dashboard (compact by default)", group=gVisual, display = display.none)
// V4.3: readable by default; shrink only if the user asks the input to
// V12.1 (operator: "the grid takes too much space in the graph"). The panel
// is a heads-up display over a 1-minute chart, not a report: it defaults to
// the tightest readable size, and the LIMITS row — a standing caveat, not a
// live decision — now rides with the full dashboard rather than always
// occupying a row. Both are inputs; nothing is removed, only stood down.
dashSize             = input.string("tiny", "Dashboard text size", options=["tiny", "small", "normal"], group=gVisual, display = display.none)
dashCompact          = input.bool(true, "Compact panel (hide standing caveat row)", group=gVisual,
     tooltip="The LIMITS row states permanent modelling caveats. They do not change bar to bar, so by default they live in the header and the full dashboard instead of holding a row on every chart.", display = display.none)
// V4.7: live evaluation on the FORMING bar, for what you READ. Order
// logic stays on confirmed bars — that separation is what stops the state
// machine flip-flopping inside a candle and keeps the backtest honest.
// Ross's own split: "confirm the candle" (setup) but enter intrabar on the
// break (trigger, already handled by the resting stop-entry).
liveEval             = input.bool(true, "Evaluate verdict on the forming bar (display)", group=gVisual, display = display.none)
debugMode            = input.bool(false, "Debug plots", group=gVisual, display = display.none)

// ───────────────────────── Raw indicators ─────────────────────────
atr = ta.atr(14)
ema9 = ta.ema(close, 9)
ema20 = ta.ema(close, 20)
// V11 (from V10): §3 confluence components V9 did not carry.
// V12.17 §5/§10 DEFECT FIX. This was `ta.sma(close, 200)` -- a 200-period
// SIMPLE average on the CHART timeframe. On a 1-minute chart that is a
// ~3.3-hour intraday line, not the level the playbook means. The confirmed
// reference is the DAILY 200 EMA: "privilégier un titre au-dessus du daily
// 200 EMA", and a daily 200 EMA sitting ~$0.50-1.00 overhead is treated as
// problematic resistance. Two errors in one line -- wrong timeframe and
// wrong average type -- and it fed ma200Support, one of the six §3
// confluence components, so the confluence gate was counting the wrong line.
//
// lookahead_off keeps it non-repainting: the daily value used intraday is
// the one available at that moment, never the finished day's.
// V12.19b guards, from the Chapter 5 rule "trend lines need at least two
// anchors ... AVOID COVERING THE CHART WITH SPECULATIVE LINES."
tlMinSlopeATR  = input.float(0.5, "A trend line must travel at least N x ATR across its anchors", minval=0.0, maxval=10.0, step=0.1, group=gVisual, display = display.none,
     tooltip="A line with no slope is a horizontal level, and horizontal levels are already drawn as S1/S2/R1/R2. Below this it is not a trend.")
tlMaxWidthATR  = input.float(3.0, "Drop the opposite rail when the channel is wider than N x ATR", minval=0.5, maxval=30.0, step=0.5, group=gVisual, display = display.none,
     tooltip="The opposite rail is offset by the largest excursion. Across a vertical spike that excursion IS the spike, so the channel stops describing a channel and spans a regime change instead.")
winLookDays = input.int(20, "Daily lookback for gaps / windows (days)", minval=3, maxval=120, group=gVisual, display = display.none)
winMinATR   = input.float(2.0, "A window must be at least N x the daily ATR", minval=1.0, maxval=10.0, step=0.25, group=gVisual, display = display.none,
     tooltip="Chapter 5: a meaningful gap or window is roughly 2x a typical daily candle or 2x the daily ATR.")
// ── V12.26 §7/§15 FIRST TARGET = A LEVEL, NOT A MULTIPLE ─────────────────
// The ladder sold its first 50% at exactly 1R. The playbook never says that:
//
//   §7  "Première cible : retest du HOD ou prochaine résistance évidente."
//       "Cible minimale de planification : Entry + 2 x risque par action."
//   §15  1. HOD si le ratio reste acceptable
//        2. cible mécanique 2R
//        3. half-dollar / whole-dollar
//        4. résistance daily suivante
//
// 1R is not in that hierarchy at all. A mechanical 1R sells half the position
// into empty space while the obvious level sits ten cents higher, and on a
// name where the HOD is only 0.6R away it holds through the one price the
// whole market is watching.
//
// So T1 becomes the NEAREST REAL LEVEL above entry -- HOD, pre-market high,
// the next half or whole dollar, a gap or window edge, or the nearest
// confirmed pivot -- provided it is at least t1MinR away so the ladder cannot
// collapse onto a level two cents overhead. With no qualifying level, it
// falls back to the mechanical 1R it used before.
t1MinR = input.float(0.8, "First target must be at least N x risk away", minval=0.2, maxval=3.0, step=0.1, group=gExecution, display = display.none,
     tooltip="Guards the level-based T1: a level closer than this is not worth a leg, so the ladder falls back to a mechanical 1R.")
t1UseLevels = input.bool(true, "First target snaps to the nearest real level (HOD / round / gap edge)", group=gExecution, display = display.none)

f_lowerAbove(float best, float cand, float floorPx) =>
    na(cand) or cand <= floorPx ? best : na(best) or cand < best ? cand : best

// ── V12.19 DAILY GAPS AND WINDOWS ────────────────────────────────────────
// Corrected after re-reading the Chapter 5 lesson "Gaps & Windows on Daily
// Charts". The confirmed definitions:
//
//   Gap:    the regular-session open is materially above or below the prior
//           close, usually on extended-hours news.
//   Window: "a large area with little visible support/resistance, created by
//           a true gap OR A LARGE LONG-BODY CANDLE."
//   Size:   roughly 2x a typical daily candle, or 2x daily ATR.
//   Rule:   "Do not skip across a newer gap/window to use an older minor
//           level as if the newer structure did not exist."
//
// The last line is the one that matters, and V12.17 got it backwards. A
// window is EMPTY SPACE -- the strong-daily-chart checklist opens with "large
// gaps/windows create room". So a level sitting INSIDE a window is not
// resistance; it is a stale price the market has already run through. The
// V12.17 wall search took the nearest level unconditionally and would report
// exactly such a level as the ceiling, understating the room available.
//
// Detection runs INSIDE the daily context on purpose. On a 1-minute chart a
// requested daily series indexed as [1] means "the previous CHART bar's value
// of the daily high", not the previous day -- a trap that would silently
// compare a minute to a day. Evaluating the loop inside request.security
// makes open[i]/close[i] genuine prior DAYS.
f_dailyStruct(int look, float mult) =>
    float a = ta.atr(14)
    float wTop = na
    float wBot = na
    // Most recent oversized daily body: price travelled through this range
    // fast and left no structure behind.
    for i = 1 to look
        float bTop = math.max(open[i], close[i])
        float bBot = math.min(open[i], close[i])
        if na(wTop) and not na(a) and a > 0 and (bTop - bBot) >= a * mult
            wTop := bTop
            wBot := bBot
    // Most recent TRUE untraded gap between two consecutive daily bars.
    float gTop = na
    float gBot = na
    for i = 1 to look - 1
        if na(gTop) and low[i] > high[i + 1]
            gTop := low[i]
            gBot := high[i + 1]
    [wTop, wBot, gTop, gBot, a]

[winTop, winBot, gapTop, gapBot, atrDaily] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "1D",
     f_dailyStruct(winLookDays, winMinATR),
     gaps=barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)

// A price inside a window is inside empty space, not at a level.
f_inWindow(float px) =>
    bool inBig = not na(winTop) and not na(winBot) and px <= winTop and px >= winBot
    bool inGap = not na(gapTop) and not na(gapBot) and px <= gapTop and px >= gapBot
    inBig or inGap

// Gap fill, per the lesson: the move back through the empty zone to the
// boundary of the candle before the gap -- the lower edge for a gap up.
float gapFillPx = gapBot

// ── V12.18 §10 MULTI-TIME-FRAME ALIGNMENT ───────────────────────────────
// The playbook devotes a whole section to it and this script had NO 5-minute
// data at all -- it read one timeframe and called that the setup:
//
//   "meilleur cas : 1-minute et 5-minute constructifs"
//   "bon 5-minute mais mauvais 1-minute : refuser normalement"
//   "excellent 1-minute avant la formation du 5-minute : possible sur un
//    leader exceptionnel"
//   "ne pas utiliser le bas d'une immense bougie 5-minute comme stop avec une
//    taille normale"
//
// One tupled request.security keeps the call budget at three. INTRABAR
// BEHAVIOUR, documented per SKILL.md: these 5-minute values update while the
// 5-minute bar is forming, which is what an operator actually reads. They are
// advisory, never an order trigger, so the live reading is the useful one.
[c5, e9_5, e20_5, h5, l5] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "5",
     [close, ta.ema(close, 9), ta.ema(close, 20), high, low],
     gaps=barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)

ma200Daily = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "1D", ta.ema(close, 200),
     gaps=barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)
bigBar5ATR = input.float(4.0, "Flag a 5-minute bar wider than N x the 1-minute ATR", minval=1.0, maxval=20.0, step=0.5, group=gVisual, display = display.none,
     tooltip="Playbook §10: do not use the low of an enormous 5-minute candle as a stop at normal size. Above this multiple the dashboard says so.")
ema200WarnDist = input.float(0.75, "Warn when the daily 200 EMA is within $N overhead", minval=0.05, maxval=10.0, step=0.05, group=gVisual, display = display.none,
     tooltip="Playbook §5 treats a daily 200 EMA about $0.50-1.00 above price as potentially problematic resistance. Scale it with the price and ATR of what you trade.")
use200Daily = input.bool(true, "Use the DAILY 200 EMA (off = legacy 200-bar chart SMA)", group=gVisual, display = display.none,
     tooltip="On = the playbook's daily 200 EMA. Off restores the pre-V12.17 behaviour for comparison.")
ma200chart = ta.sma(close, 200)
ma200v = use200Daily and not na(ma200Daily) ? ma200Daily : ma200chart
// Flipped level: a CONFIRMED pivot high (known 2 bars late, which is what
// keeps it from repainting) is promoted to a support candidate only once
// price has actually traded through it.
v11PivotHi = ta.pivothigh(high, 2, 2)
var float v11PendingFlip = na
var float flipLevel      = na
var int   flipBreakBar   = na
if not na(v11PivotHi)
    v11PendingFlip := v11PivotHi
// A wick is not a confirmed resistance break. The level becomes eligible
// only after a completed close above it, and it expires when decisively lost
// or too old to describe the current intraday leg.
if barstate.isconfirmed and not na(v11PendingFlip) and close > v11PendingFlip + syminfo.mintick
    flipLevel      := v11PendingFlip
    flipBreakBar   := bar_index
    v11PendingFlip := na
float flipLossTol = math.max(nz(atr, syminfo.mintick) * supportToleranceATR,
     close * supportTolerancePct / 100.0)
if barstate.isconfirmed and not na(flipLevel) and
     (bar_index - nz(flipBreakBar, bar_index) > 390 or close < flipLevel - flipLossTol)
    flipLevel    := na
    flipBreakBar := na
// V4.6: VWAP anchor made EXPLICIT. ta.vwap() resets on Pine's session
// change, so on an extended-hours chart it starts accumulating at 04:00 ET
// and is dominated by thin pre-market prints - it will NOT match a chart
// VWAP anchored to the regular session, nor a VWAP computed on a chart
// whose extended-hours setting differs. Same stock, different anchor,
// different number: the design pack says show both and name the source.
vwapAnchorMode = input.string("Session incl. pre-market", "VWAP anchor",
     options = ["Session incl. pre-market", "Regular hours only (09:30)"],
     group = "3. Momentum",
     tooltip = "Match this to the VWAP you read on your own chart. The dashboard prints the value so you can verify it.", display = display.none)
var float rthPV  = 0.0
var float rthVol = 0.0
inRTHsess = not na(time(timeframe.period, "0930-1600", "America/New_York"))
if ta.change(time("D")) != 0
    rthPV  := 0.0
    rthVol := 0.0
if inRTHsess
    rthPV  += hlc3 * volume
    rthVol += volume
vwapRTH = rthVol > 0 ? rthPV / rthVol : na
vwapValue = vwapAnchorMode == "Regular hours only (09:30)" ? vwapRTH : ta.vwap(hlc3)
[macdValue, macdSignal, macdHist] = ta.macd(close, 12, 26, 9)
volumeBaseline = ta.sma(volume, volumeBaselineBars)

// V11 (from V10): §3 pullback_index — "first or second pullback only, never
// the third". V9 gates pullbackBars (how MANY bars the dip lasts) which is a
// different rule; the index is which dip of the current leg this is.
//
// The counter means "pullbacks since THIS move began", so it resets on a new
// high of day (a new leg), on a VWAP break (§5 hard invalidation) and on a
// close under the prior dip low (the leg broke). Without those resets it
// climbs all session and the gate can never open — a failure that looks
// exactly like a selective strategy from the outside.
var float v11Hod     = na
var int   v11PbIndex = 0
var bool  v11InPb    = false
var float v11DipLow  = na
var float v11LegLow  = na

v11NewDay = ta.change(time("D")) != 0
if v11NewDay
    v11Hod     := high
    v11PbIndex := 0
    v11InPb    := false
    v11DipLow  := na
    v11LegLow  := na

v11BrokeStructure = (not na(vwapValue) and close < vwapValue) or
     (not na(v11LegLow) and close < v11LegLow)
if v11BrokeStructure
    v11PbIndex := 0
    v11InPb    := false
    v11LegLow  := na
    v11Hod     := math.max(nz(v11Hod, high), high)
else
    v11IsNewHod = high > nz(v11Hod, high)
    bool v11DipBar = close < close[1] or close < open
    bool v11BounceBar = high > high[1] and close > close[1]
    if v11BounceBar
        if v11InPb
            v11LegLow := v11DipLow          // the dip resolved
            v11InPb   := false
            v11DipLow := na
    else if v11DipBar
        if not v11InPb
            v11InPb    := true
            v11PbIndex := v11PbIndex + 1
            v11DipLow  := low
        else
            v11DipLow := math.min(nz(v11DipLow, low), low)
    if v11IsNewHod
        // A marginal new HOD is continuation, not proof of a new independent
        // leg. Resetting here made every HOD pullback look like pullback #1.
        v11Hod     := high


REV = "V12"               // audit candidate — keep alerts + title in step
isOneMinute = timeframe.isminutes and timeframe.multiplier == 1

// ── V8: one authoritative signal pass per bar, declared EARLY so every
// block below can gate on it (finding 4 / re-audit "decorative guard").
// With calc_on_order_fills=false this is belt-and-braces; if a user turns
// fills-recalc back on in Properties, confirmedPass stays false on those
// extra executions and the signal/arm/state blocks cannot double-run on
// final-OHLC information that did not exist at the fill.
var int lastSignalBar = na
bool confirmedPass = isOneMinute and barstate.isconfirmed and
     (na(lastSignalBar) or bar_index != lastSignalBar)

// V4: session gate. na(time(...)) outside the window.
inSession = not useSessionWindow or not na(time(timeframe.period, sessionWindow, "America/New_York"))
// V4.4: informational window flag, independent of the hard gate
inWindowInfo = not na(time(timeframe.period, sessionWindow, "America/New_York"))

// V4: previous-day close for the halt-band tier (book: bands are set by the
// PRIOR close and do not change intraday). Updated at the first bar of a new
// exchange day from the last print of the prior day — includes after-hours,
// which is a documented approximation, stated in the audit.
var float prevDayClose = na
if ta.change(time("D")) != 0
    prevDayClose := close[1]
// tier: <$0.75 -> fixed 15c band; $0.75-3 -> 20%; >$3 -> 10%
haltBandRaw = na(prevDayClose) ? na :
     prevDayClose < 0.75 ? 0.15 :
     prevDayClose <= 3.0 ? close * 0.20 : close * 0.10

// V5: LULD HALTS ONLY EXIST 09:30-16:00 ET. Three independent sources say so:
//   "there's no halts pre-market, there's no halts after hours, but during
//    regular trading hours there are halts"        5aWoZdbXJrA @00:47:03
//   "between 4:00 a.m. and 9:30 and 4:00 p.m. and 8:00 p.m., limit orders
//    only ... and no halts"                        oxob0x0Xz7s @01:47:41
//   extended-hours SKILL.md, same boundary.
// V4 computed the band at every hour and let it VETO at every hour. Outside
// RTH that vetoes a setup for a risk that cannot occur — and the session now
// starts at 07:00, so the wrong half of the morning was exposed to it.
// The band is still DISPLAYED outside RTH (it tells you what happens if you
// are still holding at 09:30) but it no longer blocks anything.
inRTH = not na(time(timeframe.period, "0930-1600", "America/New_York"))
haltBandWidth = haltBandRaw

// V4.10: HIGH OF DAY. Origin SOURCE, corroborated MEASURED.
// The script tracked only the local impulse peak, which is the wrong obstacle
// whenever the impulse is a LOWER high. Two source statements make the day's
// high the object that matters:
//   "targets a break through the high of day"      _4Q0hlNFn-A @00:46:41
//   "it cannot break through high of day..."       IHeJROuEzRU @00:01:06
// and the platform capture (2026-08-18, 299/299 alerts vs a 4.7% base rate)
// shows every scanner branch triggering only on a NEW high of day.
// Above the HOD nobody is holding a losing position — that is the whole
// supply/demand argument (js25lIZMUSY @00:22:49).
// V5: moved ABOVE the state machine — the HOD-retest setup below needs the
// running high while states are being decided, not after.
newDayBar = ta.change(time("D")) != 0
var float dayHigh = na
dayHighPrev = newDayBar or na(dayHigh) ? na : dayHigh
dayHigh := newDayBar or na(dayHigh) ? high : math.max(dayHigh, high)

// V5: THE BREAK AND RETEST. Origin SOURCE, register STREAMS (the strongest —
// decisions made before the outcome was known; 307 hits).
//   "where it broke through it, it got above it, it retests it, and then if
//    it can hold it"                              YuNvqwJftVY @00:22:37
//   "dialed in on this for a retest of our high a day 66.38"
//                                                 YuNvqwJftVY @01:11:52
// V4 could only see impulse -> first pullback, so a clean break of the high
// followed by a pullback INTO that broken level was invisible unless the push
// happened to satisfy the impulse detector. That is a whole second entry the
// script was skipping.
// V6 (finding 11): brokenHOD is an EPISODE, not a ratchet. The old code
// overwrote the level on every new high, so after a 10.00 -> 10.50 run the
// "broken resistance" read 10.30 and a real retest of 10.00 was invisible.
// An episode: freezes the FIRST close-confirmed break level; ends when the
// retest is consumed, the level fails (2 confirmed closes below), or it ages
// out. A wick alone no longer records a break — the close must confirm it.
retestMaxAgeBars = input.int(30, "Retest: max age (bars)", minval=5, maxval=120, group=gRetest, display = display.none)
var float brokenHOD   = na      // frozen first-break level of the episode
var int   brokenBar   = na
var bool  retestArmed = false
var int   closesBelowBroken = 0
var float retestLegPeak = na
var float retestLegClose = na
var int   retestLegPeakBar = na
var float retestLegVolSum = na
var float retestLegDollarSum = na
var float retestLegPath = na
var float retestLegBaseline = na
var int   retestLegBars = 0
var bool  retestLegActive = false
if newDayBar
    brokenHOD := na
    brokenBar := na
    retestArmed := false
    closesBelowBroken := 0
    retestLegPeak := na
    retestLegClose := na
    retestLegPeakBar := na
    retestLegVolSum := na
    retestLegDollarSum := na
    retestLegPath := na
    retestLegBaseline := na
    retestLegBars := 0
    retestLegActive := false
// record only the FIRST break of an episode, close-confirmed
// V8: gated by confirmedPass — a fill recalculation must not double-record.
if confirmedPass and na(brokenHOD) and not na(dayHighPrev) and close > dayHighPrev
    brokenHOD := dayHighPrev
    brokenBar := bar_index
    retestArmed := true
    closesBelowBroken := 0
    retestLegPeak := high
    retestLegClose := close
    retestLegPeakBar := bar_index
    retestLegVolSum := volume
    retestLegDollarSum := volume * hlc3
    retestLegPath := math.abs(close - close[1])
    retestLegBaseline := volumeBaseline[1]
    retestLegBars := 1
    retestLegActive := true
// episode maintenance: failure and age, on confirmed bars only
if confirmedPass and not na(brokenHOD) and bar_index > brokenBar
    // Freeze the breakout impulse at its last clean higher high. Pullback and
    // retest volume must not be relabelled as breakout volume.
    if retestLegActive
        if high > nz(retestLegPeak, high) and close >= close[1]
            retestLegPeak := high
            retestLegClose := close
            retestLegPeakBar := bar_index
            retestLegVolSum := nz(retestLegVolSum, 0.0) + volume
            retestLegDollarSum := nz(retestLegDollarSum, 0.0) + volume * hlc3
            retestLegPath := nz(retestLegPath, 0.0) + math.abs(close - close[1])
            retestLegBars += 1
        else
            retestLegActive := false
    closesBelowBroken := close < brokenHOD ? closesBelowBroken + 1 : 0
    if closesBelowBroken >= 2 or bar_index - brokenBar > retestMaxAgeBars
        brokenHOD := na
        brokenBar := na
        retestArmed := false
        closesBelowBroken := 0
        retestLegActive := false

// V6 (finding 19): the numerator is validated too — na/x returned na and
// ignored the requested fallback, so "safe" was only half true.
f_safeDiv(float numerator, float denominator, float fallback) =>
    not na(numerator) and not na(denominator) and denominator != 0 ? numerator / denominator : fallback

// ── V5: scanner criteria, computed on this chart ──────────────────────────
// Daily RVOL here is cumulative day volume / 20-day average full-day volume.
// KNOWN BIAS, stated rather than hidden: before ~10:00 the numerator holds a
// fraction of a day and the denominator holds whole days, so this reads LOW
// exactly when it matters most. Judge the morning by eye, not by this cell.
// V6 (finding 13): the old cum()-minus-valuewhen form zeroed the first bar
// of every day and then subtracted that bar's volume from every later
// reading — on gappers the opening bar IS the volume story. Accumulate.
var float dayVolCum = 0.0
dayVolCum := barstate.isfirst or newDayBar ? volume : dayVolCum + volume
// V8.2: day $ traded and day bar count, for a liquidity measure that a
// quiet half hour after a huge spike cannot decay to zero.
var float dayDollarCum = 0.0
var int dayBarCount = 0
dayDollarCum := barstate.isfirst or newDayBar ? hlc3 * volume : dayDollarCum + hlc3 * volume
dayBarCount := barstate.isfirst or newDayBar ? 1 : dayBarCount + 1
// V6 (finding 10): previous-day values with lookahead_off arrive one daily
// interval LATE on historical intraday bars (the merge happens at the end of
// the daily bar), so history and realtime showed different prior closes and
// baselines, and a reload could change the criteria. The documented stable
// pattern for ALREADY-CLOSED HTF values is the [1]-offset WITH lookahead_on:
// the offset removes the future leak, the lookahead removes the merge delay.
prevCloseD = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "1D",
     close[1], gaps=barmerge.gaps_off,
     lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
// ── V7 (reviewer): RVOL-AT-TIME replaces the full-day-denominator proxy.
// The old cell divided a partial day by whole days and read ~0.2x on a name
// doing 10x business at 07:30 — biased LOW exactly when it mattered. This
// compares today's cumulative volume with the average cumulative volume AT
// THE SAME MINUTE over the lookback, via a per-minute EWMA baseline (alpha =
// 2/(lookbackDays+1)). Warm-up: the baseline needs a full lookback of prior chart history
// per minute slot; before that the value is honestly na.
var array<float> cumAtTimeAvg = array.new_float(1440, na)
var array<int>   cumAtTimeN   = array.new_int(1440, 0)
minuteET = hour(time, "America/New_York") * 60 + minute(time, "America/New_York")
// V9.4 (operator): the PRE-MARKET HIGH is a first-class level — the
// pre-market can contain the whole move (JWEL 2026-08-10, CLAUDE.md), and
// its high is the breakout line the open trades against. Needs extended
// hours ON on the chart; stays na otherwise, and says nothing.
var float pmHigh = na
if newDayBar
    pmHigh := na
if minuteET < 570
    pmHigh := na(pmHigh) ? high : math.max(pmHigh, high)
rvolBase = array.get(cumAtTimeAvg, minuteET)
scanRVOL = f_safeDiv(dayVolCum, rvolBase, na)
// V8: confirmedPass — a fill recalc must not double-feed the baseline.
if confirmedPass
    int nSeen = array.get(cumAtTimeN, minuteET)
    float prior = array.get(cumAtTimeAvg, minuteET)
    float alpha = 2.0 / (rvolLookbackDays + 1.0)
    array.set(cumAtTimeAvg, minuteET, na(prior) ? dayVolCum : prior + alpha * (dayVolCum - prior))
    array.set(cumAtTimeN, minuteET, nSeen + 1)
// N is incremented after scanRVOL is computed. Require > lookback so the
// displayed ratio was based on at least `lookback` PRIOR observations.
rvolWarm = array.get(cumAtTimeN, minuteET) > rvolLookbackDays

// V7 (reviewer): the RVOL pillar may GATE only under an acknowledged feed
// bound to this exchange prefix. Anything else is display-only UNKNOWN.
rvolTrusted = scanFeedVerified and scanFeedSource != "Unknown" and
     scanFeedPrefix == syminfo.prefix
rvolKnown = rvolTrusted and rvolWarm and not na(scanRVOL)

// V7 (reviewer): the gap freezes at the RTH open. Before 09:30 it is the
// live premarket mark vs prior close; after, the FROZEN open gap — so the
// pillar stops drifting with every intraday print.
var float rthOpenPx = na
if newDayBar
    rthOpenPx := na
if na(rthOpenPx) and inRTH
    rthOpenPx := open
scanGap = na(prevCloseD) or prevCloseD <= 0 ? na :
     (not na(rthOpenPx) ? (rthOpenPx / prevCloseD - 1.0) * 100.0
                        : (close / prevCloseD - 1.0) * 100.0)

// V7 (reviewer): a typed float is not a verified float.
floatSymbolBound = floatTicker == syminfo.ticker
floatVerified = manualFloatM > 0 and floatSymbolBound and
     (floatSource == "SEC filing verified" or floatSource == "Trusted feed verified")
scanFloat = manualFloatM > 0 and floatSymbolBound ? manualFloatM : na

pillarPrice = close >= scanMinPrice and close <= scanMaxPrice
pillarRVOL  = rvolKnown and scanRVOL >= scanMinRVOL
pillarGap   = not na(scanGap) and scanGap >= scanMinGap
// Fail closed: a stale/unbound/unknown float cannot manufacture 4/4. The
// scanner panel may still display UNKNOWN, but the score counts only facts.
pillarFloat = floatVerified and scanFloat <= scanLowFloatMaxM
pillarScore = (pillarPrice ? 1 : 0) + (pillarRVOL ? 1 : 0) + (pillarGap ? 1 : 0) + (pillarFloat ? 1 : 0)

// ── V12.17: the fifth pillar, the flame, and the A/B grade ───────────────
// Fail-closed like the float: confirmed AND bound to this ticker AND given a
// provenance that is not "Unknown" or "Chat/rumour".
catalystBound    = catalystTicker == syminfo.ticker
catalystVerified = catalystConfirmed and catalystBound and
     (catalystSource == "Company PR / newswire" or catalystSource == "SEC filing" or
      catalystSource == "Reputable media")
pillarCatalyst   = catalystVerified

// The flame is a NEWS-AGE CLOCK, nothing more. It says nothing about the
// quality of the catalyst, the float, the RVOL or the spread. Reproduced
// here only so the age is visible beside the score, never as a pass mark.
flameState = not catalystVerified ? "—" :
     catalystAgeH <= 2.0  ? "RED"    :
     catalystAgeH <= 12.0 ? "ORANGE" :
     catalystAgeH <= 24.0 ? "YELLOW" : "cold"

// Five Pillars proper. The four technical pillars can all be true with no
// news at all -- Warrior's own Five Pillars scanner does not require news --
// so the catalyst is scored, not demanded.
pillarScore5 = pillarScore + (pillarCatalyst ? 1 : 0)
setupGrade   = pillarScore5 >= 5 ? "A" : pillarScore5 == 4 ? "B" : "C"

// §4 price sweet spot. $2-20 qualifies; $5-10 is the band the course calls
// ideal. Display only -- it sharpens a choice between two candidates, it
// does not veto one.
priceIdeal = close >= 5.0 and close <= 10.0

// which Dash lane this name would fire, if any. Every lane requires a NEW HOD
// — measured 299/299 against a 4.7% base rate (2026-08-18 export).
newHodBar   = not na(dayHighPrev) and high > dayHighPrev
scanBurst5  = bar_index >= 5  and close[5] > 0  ? (close / close[5] - 1.0) * 100.0 : na
scanBurst10 = bar_index >= 10 and close[10] > 0 ? (close / close[10] - 1.0) * 100.0 : na
laneSqueeze5  = newHodBar and not na(scanBurst5)  and scanBurst5  >= 5.0
laneSqueeze10 = newHodBar and not na(scanBurst10) and scanBurst10 >= 10.0
laneLowFloat  = newHodBar and floatVerified and scanFloat <= scanLowFloatMaxM and pillarRVOL
laneAny       = laneSqueeze5 or laneSqueeze10 or laneLowFloat
// his own stated ranking: repeat alerts, not any single one.
// "a stock hitting scanners more and more times is definitely a good
//  indicator that it's got some momentum" — yg5E_mqGFGg @00:17:02
// and the negative: KSPN "only triggered it once... probably not going to
// trade it" @00:16:47. One alert is not a candidate.
var int laneHits = 0
if newDayBar
    laneHits := 0
// V8: count once per CONFIRMED bar. Ungated, a forming bar flickering in and
// out of laneAny inflated the count on every realtime tick, and the "2+ hits"
// criterion (his repeat-alert rule) could be met by a single bar's noise.
if confirmedPass and laneAny
    laneHits += 1


// V4.1: em dash for absent values (design pack: absent != zero, never NaN)
f_px(float v) =>
    na(v) ? "—" : str.tostring(v, format.mintick)

f_n(float v, string fmt) =>
    na(v) ? "—" : str.tostring(v, fmt)

// V5.1: -999/-999.1R on screen was the f_safeDiv SENTINEL leaking into the
// dashboard (live example, EHGO). A sentinel is for logic, never for eyes.
f_rr(float v) =>
    na(v) or v <= -900 or v >= 900 ? "—" : str.tostring(v, "#.1") + "R"

// V4.1: nearest resistance above / support below from confirmed pivots.
var array<float> pivHighs = array.new_float()
var array<float> pivLows = array.new_float()
// V9.6: bar indices kept in lockstep with the prices — trend lines need
// BOTH coordinates of a pivot, the fan only needed the price.
float ph = ta.pivothigh(high, srPivotLen, srPivotLen)
float pl = ta.pivotlow(low, srPivotLen, srPivotLen)
// V12.2 (operator: levels "are constant and don't align with price and the
// right levels"): a level has TWO coordinates. Only the price was kept, so
// an S/R line had nothing to anchor to and was drawn extend.both — a rule
// straight across the chart, past and future, with no visible connection to
// the swing that created it. The pivot's bar is now stored beside its price.
var array<int> pivHighBars = array.new_int()
var array<int> pivLowBars = array.new_int()
if not na(ph)
    array.push(pivHighs, ph)
    array.push(pivHighBars, bar_index - srPivotLen)
    if array.size(pivHighs) > 40
        array.shift(pivHighs)
        array.shift(pivHighBars)
if not na(pl)
    array.push(pivLows, pl)
    array.push(pivLowBars, bar_index - srPivotLen)
    if array.size(pivLows) > 40
        array.shift(pivLows)
        array.shift(pivLowBars)
// V9.8 (live USDE — a trend line that price crossed twenty times): the
// two-pivot construction is retired. A real trend line is a TANGENT: it
// may touch price, never cut it. These rolling per-bar arrays feed that
// construction (confirmed bars only; times stored at write time so the
// drawing never resolves an old bar_index through the history buffer —
// the AAPL crash class).
var array<float> tlLows = array.new_float()
var array<float> tlHighs = array.new_float()
var array<int> tlBars = array.new_int()
var array<int> tlTimes = array.new_int()
// V12.22: volume per bar, so a level can be weighted by the business done at
// it rather than by how many times price merely brushed past.
var array<float> tlVols = array.new_float()
// V9.10: scratch list of candidate anchors, reused by both sides.
var array<int> tlCand = array.new_int()

// ═══════════ V12.27 CHART PATTERNS — LABELS, NEVER GATES ═════════════════
// §9 is explicit: "Ces formes ne remplacent ni les Five Pillars ni le plan de
// risque." A shape on a stock with no attention, no volume and no room is not
// the same setup. So these are named on the chart and nothing more — they do
// not arm, block, size or price anything.
//
// Only the two the Preview confirms AND that are mechanically decidable are
// built here. Cup-and-handle and head-and-shoulders need a subjective read
// over many bars, and head-and-shoulders appears only in the PUBLIC taxonomy,
// which the bundle warns is "une bibliothèque de notions ... à ne pas
// confondre avec la stratégie active et prioritaire de Ross".
showPatterns    = input.bool(true, "Name chart patterns (flat top, ABCD)", group=gVisual, display = display.none)
flatTopTouches  = input.int(3, "Flat top: highs needed at one price", minval=2, maxval=8, group=gVisual, display = display.none,
     tooltip="PARAMETERS.md touch_count = 3: 23 of 41 explicit counts say the THIRD touch is the one that matters.")
abcdMaxAge      = input.int(30, "ABCD: D must be within N bars", minval=5, maxval=120, group=gVisual, display = display.none,
     tooltip="A morning ABCD is not still forming three hours later. The last leg has to be recent structure.")
flatTopLook     = input.int(60, "Flat top: bars to scan", minval=15, maxval=200, group=gVisual, display = display.none,
     tooltip="Bounded on purpose -- the scan is O(n^2) and an unbounded session would risk Pine's execution limit.")

// ── Flat top: "repeated resistance at one price, then breakout; often
// clusters at half/whole dollars." The densest cluster of HIGHS wins.
f_flatTop(float tol, int minT, int look) =>
    float bestLvl = na
    int   bestN   = 0
    int   n = array.size(tlHighs)
    if n > 2
        int from_ = math.max(0, n - look)
        for i = from_ to n - 1
            float lvl = array.get(tlHighs, i)
            int c = 0
            for j = from_ to n - 1
                if math.abs(array.get(tlHighs, j) - lvl) <= tol
                    c += 1
            if c > bestN
                bestN   := c
                bestLvl := lvl
    [bestN >= minT ? bestLvl : na, bestN >= minT ? bestN : 0]

// ── ABCD: "impulse, 2+ candle pullback, first new-high attempt that may not
// clear HOD, consolidation, then renewed break of the later apex/HOD."
// A = low, B = impulse high, C = HIGHER low, D = the first new-high attempt.
// Day-scoped: yesterday's pivots describe yesterday's move.
f_abcd(float tol) =>
    // V12.29 (operator, WETO: "the ABCD is not forming — we have lower lows.
    // you're missing it"). Correct. The first version collected the last two
    // day-scoped lows and the last two highs INDEPENDENTLY and never checked
    // that they interleave as A-low, B-high, C-low, D-high in time. On a
    // fading chart the newest pivot is a LOW printed after the last high, so
    // the comparison was between the wrong events entirely -- and a falling
    // structure could read "ABCD forming".
    //
    // Now every leg carries its bar and the sequence must be chronological:
    // A before B before C before D. That alone kills the WETO case, because
    // its most recent pivot low sits AFTER the last pivot high. On top of
    // that: C must be a HIGHER low than A, C must sit below B (it is a
    // pullback, not a breakout), D must reach at least near B, and D must be
    // recent -- a morning pattern is not still "forming" three hours later.
    float aPx = na
    float bPx = na
    float cPx = na
    float dPx = na
    int   aB = na
    int   bB = na
    int   cB = na
    int   dB = na
    int   dayFirst = array.size(tlBars) > 0 ? array.get(tlBars, 0) : na
    if not na(dayFirst) and array.size(pivLows) >= 2 and array.size(pivHighs) >= 2
        for i = 0 to array.size(pivLows) - 1
            if array.get(pivLowBars, i) >= dayFirst
                aPx := cPx
                aB  := cB
                cPx := array.get(pivLows, i)
                cB  := array.get(pivLowBars, i)
        for i = 0 to array.size(pivHighs) - 1
            if array.get(pivHighBars, i) >= dayFirst
                bPx := dPx
                bB  := dB
                dPx := array.get(pivHighs, i)
                dB  := array.get(pivHighBars, i)
    bool haveAll  = not na(aPx) and not na(bPx) and not na(cPx) and not na(dPx)
    bool ordered  = haveAll and aB < bB and bB < cB and cB < dB
    bool fresh    = not na(dB) and bar_index - dB <= abcdMaxAge
    bool ok = ordered and fresh and
     cPx > aPx and cPx < bPx and dPx >= bPx - tol
    [ok, aPx, bPx, cPx, dPx]
// V9.9 (live JUNS — the uptrend line anchored on yesterday's overnight
// prints, 43% below price): trend lines are INTRADAY objects. The arrays
// reset at the day boundary, so the up-line starts at TODAY's low and
// the down-line at TODAY's high — the lines a day trader actually draws.
// Day-scoping also adapts to any timeframe by construction: the session,
// not a bar count, defines the window.
if barstate.isconfirmed
    if newDayBar
        array.clear(tlLows)
        array.clear(tlHighs)
        array.clear(tlBars)
        array.clear(tlTimes)
        array.clear(tlVols)
    array.push(tlLows, low)
    array.push(tlHighs, high)
    array.push(tlBars, bar_index)
    array.push(tlTimes, time)
    array.push(tlVols, volume)
    if array.size(tlBars) > 720
        array.shift(tlLows)
        array.shift(tlHighs)
        array.shift(tlBars)
        array.shift(tlTimes)
        array.shift(tlVols)

// V12.27: evaluate the two patterns once per bar.
float patTol = math.max(nz(atr, syminfo.mintick) * 0.25, syminfo.mintick * 2)
[flatTopPx, flatTopN] = f_flatTop(patTol, flatTopTouches, flatTopLook)
[abcdOK, abcdA, abcdB, abcdC, abcdD] = f_abcd(patTol)
// A flat top is only news while it still caps price; once price closes
// through it the shape has resolved into a breakout.
bool flatTopLive   = not na(flatTopPx) and close <= flatTopPx + patTol
bool flatTopBroken = not na(flatTopPx) and close > flatTopPx + patTol
// ABCD completes on the break of D, the "renewed break of the later apex".
bool abcdBroken = abcdOK and not na(abcdD) and close > abcdD

// V9.5 (live WYHG 2026-08-20): POLARITY. Supports came only from pivot
// LOWS and resistances only from pivot HIGHS — so a broken-resistance
// shelf sitting under price (5.80 on WYHG, made of pivot highs price had
// cleared) was invisible as support, and a lost-support level overhead
// was invisible as resistance. A level is a level: both pivot kinds feed
// both sides; which side of PRICE it is on decides its role.
var array<float> allPiv = array.new_float()
var array<int> allPivBars = array.new_int()
array.clear(allPiv)
array.clear(allPivBars)
if array.size(pivHighs) > 0
    for i = 0 to array.size(pivHighs) - 1
        array.push(allPiv, array.get(pivHighs, i))
        array.push(allPivBars, array.get(pivHighBars, i))
if array.size(pivLows) > 0
    for i = 0 to array.size(pivLows) - 1
        array.push(allPiv, array.get(pivLows, i))
        array.push(allPivBars, array.get(pivLowBars, i))
float nearestRes = na
float nearestSup = na
if array.size(allPiv) > 0
    for i = 0 to array.size(allPiv) - 1
        float v = array.get(allPiv, i)
        if v > close and (na(nearestRes) or v < nearestRes)
            nearestRes := v
        if v < close and (na(nearestSup) or v > nearestSup)
            nearestSup := v

// ───────────────────────── State machine ─────────────────────────
int IDLE     = 0
int IMPULSE  = 1
int PULLBACK = 2
int ARMED    = 3
int LONG     = 4
int INVALID  = 5
int DONE     = 6

// V4: vocabulary pass (design pack) — display names are research states,
// not instructions. Internal constants unchanged: never key logic on a
// display string.
// V7.1: plain words, operator request. One glance must not need a glossary.
f_stateName(int state) =>
    state == IDLE ? "WAITING" :
     state == IMPULSE ? "MOVE UP" :
     state == PULLBACK ? "DIP FORMING" :
     state == ARMED ? "ORDER SET" :
     state == LONG ? "IN TRADE" :
     state == INVALID ? "REJECTED" : "TRADE OVER"

// ───────────────────── Dynamic impulse candidate ─────────────────────
float bestStartLow = na
float bestStartClose = na
float bestPct = 0.0
float bestATR = 0.0
float bestEfficiency = 0.0
float bestRVOL = 0.0
float bestVolumeSum = na
float bestDollarSum = na
float bestDollarVolume = na
float bestBaseline = na
float bestPath = na
int bestBars = 0
int bestStartBar = na

var int scanAfterBar = na
// V8.2: one late-join attempt per peak bar (see the LATE JOIN block)
var int lateJoinPeakBar = na

enoughHistory = bar_index > volumeBaselineBars + maxImpulseBars + 5

// V8: gated by confirmedPass (was isconfirmed) — signal discovery must never
// run twice on one bar via a fill recalculation.
if confirmedPass and enoughHistory
    for candidateBars = minImpulseBars to maxImpulseBars
        int candidateStartBar = bar_index - candidateBars
        bool freshCandidate = na(scanAfterBar) or candidateStartBar > scanAfterBar

        float candidateStartLow = low[candidateBars]
        float candidateStartClose = close[candidateBars]
        float candidateRange = high - candidateStartLow

        float candidatePath = 0.0
        float candidateVolumeSum = 0.0
        float candidateDollarSum = 0.0
        bool currentIsPeak = true

        for j = 0 to candidateBars - 1
            candidatePath += math.abs(close[j] - close[j + 1])
            candidateVolumeSum += volume[j]
            candidateDollarSum += volume[j] * hlc3[j]

        for k = 1 to candidateBars
            currentIsPeak := currentIsPeak and high >= high[k]

        float candidatePct = f_safeDiv(candidateRange, candidateStartLow, 0.0) * 100.0
        float candidateATR = f_safeDiv(candidateRange, atr, 0.0)
        float candidateEfficiency = f_safeDiv(close - candidateStartClose, candidatePath, 0.0)
        float candidateAvgVolume = candidateVolumeSum / candidateBars
        float candidateBaseline = volumeBaseline[candidateBars + 1]
        float candidateRVOL = f_safeDiv(candidateAvgVolume, candidateBaseline, 0.0)
        float candidateDollarVolume = candidateDollarSum / candidateBars

        bool priceAdvancing = close > candidateStartClose and close > open
        bool qualifies = freshCandidate and currentIsPeak and priceAdvancing and
             candidatePct >= minPushPct and
             candidateATR >= minPushATR and
             candidateEfficiency >= minEfficiency and
             candidateRVOL >= minPushRVOL and
             candidateDollarVolume >= minDollarVolume

        if qualifies and (candidatePct > bestPct or (candidatePct == bestPct and candidateEfficiency > bestEfficiency))
            bestStartLow := candidateStartLow
            bestStartClose := candidateStartClose
            bestPct := candidatePct
            bestATR := candidateATR
            bestEfficiency := candidateEfficiency
            bestRVOL := candidateRVOL
            bestVolumeSum := candidateVolumeSum
            bestDollarSum := candidateDollarSum
            bestDollarVolume := candidateDollarVolume
            bestBaseline := candidateBaseline
            bestPath := candidatePath
            bestBars := candidateBars
            bestStartBar := candidateStartBar

// ───────────────────────── Persistent setup data ─────────────────────────
var int setupState = IDLE
// V5/V6: which pattern armed. Display + provenance — never key logic on it.
int KIND_PULLBACK = 0
int KIND_RETEST   = 1
int KIND_FAST     = 2
int KIND_UPTREND  = 3
var int setupKind = KIND_PULLBACK

// ── V6 broker-lifecycle latches (audit findings 1 & 2) ──────────────────
// varip survives the intrabar rollback that erases ordinary `var` writes.
// These latch facts about the ORDER BOOK (which does not roll back) so the
// state machine cannot contradict it. Everything else stays rollback-
// consistent. V8 adds three more latches of the same kind: the closed-trade
// cursor (was var — it rolled back and reprocessed trades), the T1-filled
// flag (the runner's break-even stop must not flicker back intrabar), and
// the per-entry fill latch declared with the fill detector below.
varip bool intrabarCancelled = false   // an intrabar cancel happened this bar
if barstate.isnew
    intrabarCancelled := false
// Monotonic trade counters: strategy.closedtrades never rolls back, so a
// same-minute entry+exit is detectable even after every var was rewound.
varip int handledClosedTrades = 0
varip float tradeInitialQty = na
varip bool t1Filled = false
varip bool t2Filled = false   // V11: §6's middle rung
var int stateStartBar = na
// V8 (re-audit ND-5): ATR-stop provenance is recorded AT ARM TIME. Inferring
// it later from live ATR let the dashboard's ᵃᵗʳ marker describe a stop
// method the plan never used.
var bool plannedUsesATRStop = false
// V9.11: one closed trade's readable result — entry anchor, running
// realized P&L (all legs), and the size/risk basis for the % and R.
varip float resPnL = 0.0
varip float resEntryPx = na
varip int   resEntryTime = na
varip float resQty = na
varip float resRisk = na

var int impulseStartBar = na
var int impulsePeakBar = na
var float pushStartPrice = na
var float pushStartClose = na
var float pushPeak = na
var float pushPct = na
var float pushATR = na
var float pushEfficiency = na
var float pushRVOL = na
var float pushVolumeSum = na
var float pushAvgVolume = na
var float pushDollarSum = na
var float pushDollarVolume = na
var float pushBaselineVolume = na
var float pushPath = na
var int pushBars = 0

var int pullbackStartBar = na
var int pullbackLastBar = na
var int pullbackBars = 0
var int redPullbackBars = 0
var float pullbackLow = na
var float pullbackVolumeSum = 0.0

var float triggerPrice = na
var float structuralStop = na
var float plannedRisk = na
var float plannedTarget = na
var float plannedRRtoPeak = na
var float plannedShares = na
var float setupQuality = na
var string plannedSizeBoundBy = "—"

var float setupRetestLevel = na    // V6: frozen retest basis for this setup
var float tradeEntryPrice = na
var float tradeRisk = na
var float activeTarget = na
var int tradeEntryBar = na
var float highestSinceEntry = na

var string statusReason = "Scanning"

// V4: setup counter for the day — the SOURCE rule "3rd pullback: reduce
// size, don't skip" is about pullback NUMBER in the run. Pine cannot track
// a run across resets cleanly, so the proxy is setups-armed-today; from the
// 3rd, quantity is halved. LOCAL mapping of a SOURCE rule, documented.
varip int setupsToday = 0
if barstate.isnew and ta.change(time("D")) != 0
    setupsToday := 0

var bool eventArmed = false
var bool eventLong = false
var bool eventInvalid = false
var bool eventBailout = false
// V7.3 (live CDTG report): when the PATTERN passes and only the clock says
// no, silence is the wrong answer — the operator watched a valid read go
// unmentioned and traded it manually. A ghost signal shows the pattern was
// seen while placing NO order, so the session rule keeps its teeth and the
// operator keeps their eyes.
var bool eventGhost = false
// V7.4: the ghost carries a full plan so PLAN/SIZE stay populated while the
// clock withholds the order. Display only; nothing reads these for orders.
var float ghostTrig = na
var float ghostStop = na
var float ghostTgt = na
var float ghostShares = na
var int   ghostBar = na

eventArmed := false
eventLong := false
eventInvalid := false
eventBailout := false
eventGhost := false

// ───────────────────────── Detect actual broker fill ─────────────────────────
// V8 (re-audit critical 2): exactly-once fill handling. Ordinary `var` state
// rolls back between realtime ticks while the broker position persists, so
// `position_size > 0 and setupState != LONG` re-fired on EVERY tick — the
// re-audit caught repeated ENTRY FILLED alerts (alert.freq_all) and repeated
// setupsToday increments from one physical fill. The varip latch below keys
// on the entry BAR of the open trade, which is monotonic broker truth: one
// count, one alert, one metadata latch per unique fill.
varip int lastCountedEntryBar = na
// V8: count of historical fills whose entry bar ALSO touched the planned
// stop — sequence unknowable from OHLC (finding 3). Labelled since V6;
// V8 counts and surfaces them. While this is non-zero, do not quote
// Strategy Tester expectancy for this file.
varip int historicalFillAmbiguities = 0
varip int lastAmbiguousEntryBar = na

if strategy.position_size > 0
    int openEntryBar = strategy.opentrades > 0 ?
         strategy.opentrades.entry_bar_index(strategy.opentrades - 1) : bar_index
    bool newFill = na(lastCountedEntryBar) or openEntryBar != lastCountedEntryBar
    if setupState != LONG
        setupState := LONG
        stateStartBar := bar_index
        tradeEntryBar := openEntryBar
        tradeEntryPrice := strategy.position_avg_price
        // V8: defensive recovery after a script reload with a broker-open
        // position — the plan vars are gone, but the position is real.
        // Reconstruct a conservative stop instead of leaving the trade
        // naked, and SAY the plan was reconstructed.
        if na(structuralStop) or na(triggerPrice)
            triggerPrice := tradeEntryPrice
            structuralStop := tradeEntryPrice - atr * fallbackATRmult
            plannedRisk := atr * fallbackATRmult
            plannedTarget := tradeEntryPrice + plannedRisk * rewardMultiple
            plannedShares := strategy.position_size
            plannedUsesATRStop := true
            statusReason := "Recovered open trade after reload — stop reconstructed, verify it"
        tradeRisk := tradeEntryPrice - structuralStop
        activeTarget := tradeEntryPrice + tradeRisk * rewardMultiple
        highestSinceEntry := tradeEntryPrice
    if newFill
        lastCountedEntryBar := openEntryBar
        // V6 (finding 7): the setup counter counts FILLS, not arms — once.
        setupsToday += 1
        t1Filled := false
        t2Filled := false
        tradeInitialQty := strategy.position_size
        // V6 (finding 3, disclosure): if this bar's low already touched the
        // stop, the fill sequence inside the bar is UNKNOWABLE from OHLC —
        // live logic may have cancelled before the trigger. V8: counted.
        if barstate.ishistory and not na(structuralStop) and low <= structuralStop and
             (na(lastAmbiguousEntryBar) or openEntryBar != lastAmbiguousEntryBar)
            historicalFillAmbiguities += 1
            lastAmbiguousEntryBar := openEntryBar
            // V9 (defect 3): the label is diagnostic; the COUNT on the
            // LIMITS row is the audit artifact and renders regardless.
            if showDiagnostics
                label.new(bar_index, high, "AMBIGUOUS SEQ", style=label.style_label_down,
                     color=color.new(color.orange, 20), textcolor=color.black, size=size.small)
        statusReason := "Bought — follow the plan"
        eventLong := true
        // V9.11: anchor the readable result and mark the buy.
        resPnL := 0.0
        resEntryPx := tradeEntryPrice
        resEntryTime := time
        resQty := strategy.position_size
        resRisk := tradeRisk
        if showTradeResult
            // V12 (operator: "positions don't align when price zooms"):
            // yloc.belowbar/abovebar IGNORE the y value and hang the label off
            // the candle by a fixed screen offset, so the marker slides away
            // from the fill price as the price scale is zoomed — while the
            // dotted result line below is anchored to the real prices. The two
            // then disagree on where the trade happened. Anchor the marker to
            // the fill price itself and it stays welded to it at any zoom.
            label.new(time, tradeEntryPrice, "BOUGHT " + f_px(tradeEntryPrice),
                 xloc=xloc.bar_time, yloc=yloc.price,
                 style=label.style_label_up, size=size.small,
                 color=color.new(color.teal, 15), textcolor=color.white)

// V6 (finding 2) / V8: strategy.closedtrades is monotonic and never rolls
// back. handledClosedTrades is now varip so the batch below processes each
// closed trade exactly once — a same-minute entry+exit can no longer vanish,
// and each round trip commits its one daily-count increment (re-audit RT4).
if strategy.closedtrades > handledClosedTrades
    bool recoveredClosedOnly = false
    int recoveredEntryBar = na
    for tradeNum = handledClosedTrades to strategy.closedtrades - 1
        int closedEntryBar = strategy.closedtrades.entry_bar_index(tradeNum)
        int closedExitBar = strategy.closedtrades.exit_bar_index(tradeNum)
        string closedExitId = strategy.closedtrades.exit_id(tradeNum)
        float closedEntryPrice = strategy.closedtrades.entry_price(tradeNum)
        float closedExitPrice = strategy.closedtrades.exit_price(tradeNum)
        // a round trip the fill detector never saw still counts once
        if na(lastCountedEntryBar) or closedEntryBar != lastCountedEntryBar
            lastCountedEntryBar := closedEntryBar
            setupsToday += 1
            // A historical entry and all exits can occur inside one chart
            // bar. position_size is never observed >0, so the normal fill
            // block cannot initialise the result record. Reconstruct it
            // from the monotonic closed-trade stream instead of rolling the
            // previous trade's P&L into this one.
            recoveredClosedOnly := true
            recoveredEntryBar := closedEntryBar
            resPnL := 0.0
            resEntryPx := closedEntryPrice
            resEntryTime := strategy.closedtrades.entry_time(tradeNum)
            resQty := 0.0
            resRisk := not na(structuralStop) ? closedEntryPrice - structuralStop : plannedRisk
        // the profitable +1R leg = the T1 partial; runner stop goes flat
        if closedExitId == "T1" and closedExitPrice > closedEntryPrice
            t1Filled := true
        if closedExitId == "T2" and closedExitPrice > closedEntryPrice
            t2Filled := true
        // same-bar historical round trip: sequence unknowable — count it
        if barstate.ishistory and closedEntryBar == closedExitBar and
             (na(lastAmbiguousEntryBar) or closedEntryBar != lastAmbiguousEntryBar)
            historicalFillAmbiguities += 1
            lastAmbiguousEntryBar := closedEntryBar
        // V9.11: every leg's realized P&L (commission included) rolls up
        // into ONE number for the position — a T1 partial plus a runner
        // is one trade to the operator, not two.
        resPnL += strategy.closedtrades.profit(tradeNum)
        if recoveredClosedOnly and closedEntryBar == recoveredEntryBar
            resQty += math.abs(strategy.closedtrades.size(tradeNum))
    handledClosedTrades := strategy.closedtrades
    if strategy.position_size == 0
        setupState := DONE
        stateStartBar := bar_index
        scanAfterBar := bar_index
        strategy.cancel("Long")
        // V9.11: the result, in words, where the trade ended. Percent is
        // the return on the position, R the multiple of the risk taken —
        // the two numbers that judge a trade. Share count deliberately
        // absent: it is a sizing fact, not a result.
        float resExitPx = strategy.closedtrades.exit_price(strategy.closedtrades - 1)
        float resPct = not na(resEntryPx) and not na(resQty) and resEntryPx * resQty != 0 ?
             resPnL / (resEntryPx * resQty) * 100.0 : na
        float resRiskCash = not na(resRisk) and not na(resQty) ?
             (resRisk + slipTicksInput * syminfo.mintick) * resQty +
                  commissionPerOrderInput * (useThirdRung ? 4.0 : 3.0) : na
        float resR = not na(resRiskCash) and resRiskCash > 0 ? resPnL / resRiskCash : na
        bool resWin = resPnL >= 0
        statusReason := (resWin ? "WON " : "LOST ") + "$" + f_n(math.abs(resPnL), "#.##") +
             (na(resR) ? "" : " (" + f_n(resR, "#.0") + "R net/model-risk)") + " — log it"
        if showTradeResult and not na(resEntryPx)
            label.new(time, resExitPx, "SOLD " + f_px(resExitPx) + "\n" +
                 (resWin ? "+" : "-") + "$" + f_n(math.abs(resPnL), "#.##") +
                 (na(resPct) ? "" : "  " + (resWin ? "+" : "") + f_n(resPct, "#.0") + "%") +
                 (na(resR) ? "" : "  " + (resWin ? "+" : "") + f_n(resR, "#.0") + "R"),
                 xloc=xloc.bar_time, yloc=yloc.price,
                 style=label.style_label_down, size=size.small,
                 color=resWin ? color.new(color.green, 10) : color.new(color.red, 10),
                 textcolor=color.white)
            line.new(resEntryTime, resEntryPx, time, resExitPx,
                 xloc=xloc.bar_time, width=1, style=line.style_dotted,
                 color=resWin ? color.new(color.green, 30) : color.new(color.red, 30))
        resEntryPx := na

if strategy.position_size == 0 and setupState == LONG and not na(tradeEntryPrice)
    setupState := DONE
    stateStartBar := bar_index
    scanAfterBar := bar_index
    statusReason := "Trade finished — log it"

// ── V6 (finding 1, commit step): a latched intrabar cancel becomes a
// durable INVALID at the close, whatever the rolled-back var state says.
if confirmedPass and intrabarCancelled and strategy.position_size == 0 and
     (setupState == ARMED or setupState == PULLBACK)
    setupState := INVALID
    stateStartBar := bar_index
    scanAfterBar := bar_index
    triggerPrice := na
    structuralStop := na
    plannedRisk := na
    plannedTarget := na
    plannedShares := na
    statusReason := "Rejected — stop was hit before entry, order removed"
    eventInvalid := true

// ── V8 (finding 5 / re-audit critical 3): TIME-IN-FORCE, enforced BEFORE the
// boundary. V6/V7 cleaned up at the close of the first OUT-OF-window bar —
// the broker could fill the stale order during that bar, and a prior-day
// stop could fill on the opening gap before any script logic ran. Now:
//   · entryTimeOK forbids arming on the LAST in-window bar (an order placed
//     at its close would first be fillable after the window);
//   · pending orders and live setups are cancelled/invalidated AT the last
//     in-window bar close — the order is dead before the off-window tick
//     that could have filled it;
//   · positions flatten at that same close unless overnight is explicitly
//     allowed (default: day-trading flat policy);
//   · the day's final bar and the flat cutoff get the same treatment;
//   · newDayBar stays as a backstop only.
// Window-end arithmetic assumes a same-day window like 0700-1130 (documented
// limitation; overnight windows are not this script's use case).
sessionEndMin = str.tonumber(str.substring(sessionWindow, 5, 7)) * 60 +
     str.tonumber(str.substring(sessionWindow, 7, 9))
lastWindowBar = useSessionWindow and inWindowInfo and
     minuteET + timeframe.multiplier >= sessionEndMin
entryTimeOK = not useSessionWindow or (inWindowInfo and not lastWindowBar)
isLastBarOfDay = timeframe.isintraday and time_close == time_close("1D")
pastFlatCutoff = minuteET >= dailyFlatHour * 60 + dailyFlatMinute

// V8 (re-audit ND-7): ONE flatten per execution. Session-edge, day-end and
// bailout closes used to be able to fire two competing strategy.close calls
// with two different stories in one execution. They now share a single flag
// and one authoritative reason; the actual close is issued once, after the
// trade-management block has had its say (boundary wins over bailout).
bool flattenRequested = false
string flattenReason = ""
bool flattenIsBailout = false

if confirmedPass and (newDayBar or lastWindowBar or isLastBarOfDay or
     (pastFlatCutoff and not allowOvernightPositions))
    if setupState != IDLE and setupState != LONG and setupState != DONE
        strategy.cancel("Long")
        setupState := INVALID
        stateStartBar := bar_index
        scanAfterBar := bar_index
        statusReason := newDayBar ? "New day — starting fresh" :
             "boundary ahead"
    // V7.5 (live CDTG report): a ghost plan captured pre-market survived
    // into the afternoon and displayed "signal 4.08" with price at 6.50.
    // Ghosts die at every boundary and age out after 10 bars.
    ghostTrig := na
    ghostStop := na
    ghostTgt := na
    ghostShares := na
    ghostBar := na
    if strategy.position_size > 0 and not allowOvernightPositions and
         (lastWindowBar or isLastBarOfDay or pastFlatCutoff)
        flattenRequested := true
        flattenReason := lastWindowBar ? "Session ending — closing before the boundary" :
             pastFlatCutoff ? "Daily flat cutoff — closing the trade" :
             "Day over — closing the trade"

// ───────────────────────── Confirmed-bar state updates ─────────────────────────
// V8: gated by confirmedPass (was isconfirmed) — no double state writes from
// a fill recalculation.
if confirmedPass and strategy.position_size == 0
    if (setupState == DONE or setupState == INVALID) and bar_index > stateStartBar
        setupState := IDLE
        statusReason := "Waiting for a setup"
        impulseStartBar := na
        impulsePeakBar := na
        pushStartPrice := na
        pushStartClose := na
        pushPeak := na
        pushPct := na
        pushATR := na
        pushEfficiency := na
        pushRVOL := na
        pushVolumeSum := na
        pushAvgVolume := na
        pushDollarSum := na
        pushDollarVolume := na
        pushBaselineVolume := na
        pushPath := na
        pushBars := 0
        pullbackStartBar := na
        pullbackLastBar := na
        pullbackBars := 0
        redPullbackBars := 0
        pullbackLow := na
        pullbackVolumeSum := 0.0
        triggerPrice := na
        structuralStop := na
        plannedRisk := na
        plannedTarget := na
        plannedRRtoPeak := na
        plannedShares := na
        setupQuality := na
        plannedSizeBoundBy := "—"
        tradeEntryPrice := na
        tradeRisk := na
        activeTarget := na
        tradeEntryBar := na
        highestSinceEntry := na
        setupRetestLevel := na
        tradeInitialQty := na
        t1Filled := false
        t2Filled := false
        plannedUsesATRStop := false
        ghostTrig := na
        ghostStop := na
        ghostTgt := na
        ghostShares := na
        ghostBar := na

    // ── V5: HOD BREAK-AND-RETEST ──────────────────────────────────────────
    // Checked BEFORE the impulse path, because a retest that also satisfies
    // the impulse detector should be labelled as the retest — it is the more
    // specific pattern and its stop is the better-defined one.
    //
    // Shape: the high of day was taken out (brokenHOD set above), price came
    // back INTO that level, and this bar HELD it — traded down to/through the
    // level intraday but closed back above. That close is "if it can hold it"
    // (YuNvqwJftVY @00:22:37). The broken high is now support; the stop goes
    // under it, which is a structurally tighter and more defensible stop than
    // a pullback low floating in space.
    //
    // Everything after this point is shared with the first-pullback path:
    // same gates, same halt-band check, same sizing, same bailout. The retest
    // only supplies a different REASON to be in the PULLBACK state.
    retestTol = math.max(atr * retestTolATR, syminfo.mintick)
    // V8 (re-audit ND-3): TWO-SIDED touch band. The old test had no maximum
    // undercut — a broken $10 high could trade to $8 and close green at
    // $10.01 and still "retest". A retest must come back TO the level, not
    // through it and into the void: low inside [level - tol, level + tol]
    // and a close back above it.
    retestTouch = retestArmed and not na(brokenHOD) and bar_index > brokenBar and
         low >= brokenHOD - retestTol and low <= brokenHOD + retestTol and
         close > brokenHOD and close >= open
    if enableRetest and setupState == IDLE and retestTouch
        setupState := PULLBACK
        stateStartBar := bar_index
        setupKind := KIND_RETEST
        retestArmed := false

        // the "impulse" for a retest is the leg from the broken level to the
        // high that broke it — real, measurable, and not a detector guess
        impulseStartBar := brokenBar
        impulsePeakBar := nz(retestLegPeakBar, brokenBar)
        pushStartPrice := brokenHOD
        pushStartClose := brokenHOD
        pushPeak := nz(retestLegPeak, dayHigh)
        pushPct := f_safeDiv(pushPeak - brokenHOD, brokenHOD, 0.0) * 100.0
        pushATR := f_safeDiv(pushPeak - brokenHOD, atr, 0.0)
        pushPath := math.max(nz(retestLegPath, pushPeak - brokenHOD), syminfo.mintick)
        pushEfficiency := f_safeDiv(nz(retestLegClose, pushPeak) - brokenHOD,
             pushPath, 0.0)
        pushBars := math.max(retestLegBars, 1)
        pushVolumeSum := nz(retestLegVolSum, volume)
        pushAvgVolume := pushVolumeSum / pushBars
        pushDollarSum := nz(retestLegDollarSum, hlc3 * volume)
        pushDollarVolume := pushDollarSum / pushBars
        pushBaselineVolume := retestLegBaseline
        pushRVOL := f_safeDiv(pushAvgVolume, pushBaselineVolume, 0.0)

        pullbackStartBar := bar_index
        pullbackLastBar := bar_index
        pullbackBars := 1
        // V6 (finding 12): the qualifying retest candle is green by
        // construction (close >= open), and recording it as red falsified a
        // shared counter. The count is honest now; the gate below accepts a
        // retest setup without a red candle explicitly.
        redPullbackBars := close < open ? 1 : 0
        pullbackLow := low
        pullbackVolumeSum := volume
        // V6 (finding 11): the setup keeps its OWN frozen copy of the level —
        // later episode changes cannot silently move a live setup's basis.
        setupRetestLevel := brokenHOD
        // V8 (re-audit ND-4): consuming the retest CLEARS the episode. The
        // old code left brokenHOD set until age/failure, so the first-close
        // -break recorder (`na(brokenHOD)` required) could never see a second
        // breakout episode later in the day. The frozen copy above is the
        // setup's; the global episode is free to record the next break.
        brokenHOD := na
        brokenBar := na
        closesBelowBroken := 0
        retestLegActive := false
        statusReason := "Testing the broken high at " + str.tostring(setupRetestLevel, format.mintick)

    if setupState == IDLE and bestBars > 0
        setupState := IMPULSE
        stateStartBar := bar_index
        setupKind := KIND_PULLBACK

        impulseStartBar := bestStartBar
        impulsePeakBar := bar_index
        pushStartPrice := bestStartLow
        pushStartClose := bestStartClose
        pushPeak := high
        pushPct := bestPct
        pushATR := bestATR
        pushEfficiency := bestEfficiency
        pushRVOL := bestRVOL
        pushVolumeSum := bestVolumeSum
        pushAvgVolume := bestVolumeSum / bestBars
        pushDollarSum := bestDollarSum
        pushDollarVolume := bestDollarVolume
        pushBaselineVolume := bestBaseline
        pushPath := bestPath
        pushBars := bestBars

        pullbackStartBar := na
        pullbackLastBar := na
        pullbackBars := 0
        redPullbackBars := 0
        pullbackLow := na
        pullbackVolumeSum := 0.0

        triggerPrice := na
        structuralStop := na
        plannedRisk := na
        plannedTarget := na
        plannedRRtoPeak := na
        plannedShares := na
        setupQuality := na

        tradeEntryPrice := na
        tradeRisk := na
        activeTarget := na
        tradeEntryBar := na
        highestSinceEntry := na

        statusReason := "Strong move up — waiting for the dip"

    else if setupState == IMPULSE
        bool newPeak = high > pushPeak
        bool cleanContinuation = newPeak and close >= open and close >= close[1]

        if cleanContinuation
            pushPeak := high
            impulsePeakBar := bar_index
            pushBars += 1
            pushVolumeSum += volume
            pushAvgVolume := pushVolumeSum / pushBars
            pushRVOL := f_safeDiv(pushAvgVolume, pushBaselineVolume, 0.0)
            pushDollarSum := nz(pushDollarSum, 0.0) + volume * hlc3
            pushDollarVolume := pushDollarSum / pushBars
            pushPath += math.abs(close - close[1])
            pushEfficiency := f_safeDiv(close - pushStartClose, pushPath, 0.0)
            pushPct := f_safeDiv(pushPeak - pushStartPrice, pushStartPrice, 0.0) * 100.0
            pushATR := f_safeDiv(pushPeak - pushStartPrice, atr, 0.0)
            statusReason := "Move still going up"

        else
            if newPeak
                pushPeak := high
                impulsePeakBar := bar_index
                pushPct := f_safeDiv(pushPeak - pushStartPrice, pushStartPrice, 0.0) * 100.0
                pushATR := f_safeDiv(pushPeak - pushStartPrice, atr, 0.0)

            setupState := PULLBACK
            stateStartBar := bar_index
            pullbackStartBar := bar_index
            pullbackLastBar := bar_index
            pullbackBars := 1
            redPullbackBars := close < open ? 1 : 0
            pullbackLow := low
            pullbackVolumeSum := volume
            statusReason := "First dip forming"

    // V8 (re-audit P35 — the V7 session's last, never-verified edit):
    // historical mirror of the realtime stop-touch cancel. Live, price
    // touching the structural stop before the trigger kills the setup
    // intrabar (INVALID). Historically the breach is only visible at the
    // close, but the same fact must kill the setup here too — otherwise the
    // order was cancelled one bar later and immediately re-armed with a
    // deeper stop, booking fills a live run could never take. Bars that
    // touched the stop AND filled never reach this block (position_size > 0
    // upstream); those are counted as ambiguous sequences instead.
    else if setupState == ARMED and not na(structuralStop) and low <= structuralStop
        strategy.cancel("Long")
        setupState := INVALID
        stateStartBar := bar_index
        scanAfterBar := bar_index
        statusReason := "Rejected — price hit the stop level first, order removed"
        eventInvalid := true

    else if setupState == PULLBACK or setupState == ARMED
        if bar_index > pullbackLastBar
            if setupState == ARMED
                strategy.cancel("Long")

            setupState := PULLBACK
            pullbackBars += 1
            redPullbackBars += close < open ? 1 : 0
            pullbackLow := math.min(pullbackLow, low)
            pullbackVolumeSum += volume
            pullbackLastBar := bar_index
            statusReason := "Dip continuing"

    // ── V8.2 LATE JOIN (live CDTG 2026-08-20) ────────────────────────────
    // The scanner above can only SEE a push on a bar that is itself the
    // green peak. If the machine was busy (DONE/INVALID after a lane trade)
    // while the peak printed, it returns to IDLE inside the dip and the
    // pullback is never assessed. This block scans for a COMPLETED push
    // whose peak sits 1..maxPullbackBars bars back with the dip still in
    // progress, and joins it as a normal PULLBACK — same fields, same
    // gates, same arm path, this same bar. One join per peak bar
    // (lateJoinPeakBar); a peak the join already tried is not retried.
    if setupState == IDLE and bestBars == 0 and enoughHistory and
         not eventInvalid and not intrabarCancelled
        bool ljFound = false
        for p = 1 to maxPullbackBars
            if not ljFound
                bool peakGreen = close[p] > open[p]
                bool stillPeak = true
                int ljReds = 0
                float ljLow = low
                float ljVol = 0.0
                for k = 0 to p - 1
                    stillPeak := stillPeak and high[p] > high[k]
                    ljReds += close[k] < open[k] ? 1 : 0
                    ljLow := math.min(ljLow, low[k])
                    ljVol += volume[k]
                if peakGreen and stillPeak and ljReds >= 1 and
                     (na(lateJoinPeakBar) or bar_index - p != lateJoinPeakBar)
                    for cb = minImpulseBars to maxImpulseBars
                        if not ljFound
                            float ljStartLow = low[p + cb]
                            float ljStartClose = close[p + cb]
                            float ljRange = high[p] - ljStartLow
                            float ljPath = 0.0
                            float ljPushVol = 0.0
                            float ljDollarSum = 0.0
                            for j = p to p + cb - 1
                                ljPath += math.abs(close[j] - close[j + 1])
                                ljPushVol += volume[j]
                                ljDollarSum += volume[j] * hlc3[j]
                            float ljPct = f_safeDiv(ljRange, ljStartLow, 0.0) * 100.0
                            float ljATR = f_safeDiv(ljRange, atr, 0.0)
                            float ljEff = f_safeDiv(close[p] - ljStartClose, ljPath, 0.0)
                            float ljAvgVol = ljPushVol / cb
                            float ljBase = volumeBaseline[p + cb + 1]
                            float ljRVOL = f_safeDiv(ljAvgVol, ljBase, 0.0)
                            float ljDollar = ljDollarSum / cb
                            float ljRetr = f_safeDiv(high[p] - ljLow, ljRange, 100.0) * 100.0
                            if ljPct >= minPushPct and ljATR >= minPushATR and
                                 ljEff >= minEfficiency and ljRVOL >= minPushRVOL and
                                 ljDollar >= minDollarVolume and ljRetr <= maxRetracementPct
                                setupState := PULLBACK
                                stateStartBar := bar_index
                                setupKind := KIND_PULLBACK
                                impulseStartBar := bar_index - p - cb
                                impulsePeakBar := bar_index - p
                                pushStartPrice := ljStartLow
                                pushStartClose := ljStartClose
                                pushPeak := high[p]
                                pushPct := ljPct
                                pushATR := ljATR
                                pushEfficiency := ljEff
                                pushRVOL := ljRVOL
                                pushVolumeSum := ljPushVol
                                pushAvgVolume := ljAvgVol
                                pushDollarSum := ljDollarSum
                                pushDollarVolume := ljDollar
                                pushBaselineVolume := ljBase
                                pushPath := ljPath
                                pushBars := cb
                                pullbackStartBar := bar_index - p + 1
                                pullbackLastBar := bar_index
                                pullbackBars := p
                                redPullbackBars := ljReds
                                pullbackLow := ljLow
                                pullbackVolumeSum := ljVol
                                lateJoinPeakBar := bar_index - p
                                statusReason := "Late read — dip already in progress, joined"
                                ljFound := true

// ───────────────────────── Live setup measurements ─────────────────────────
pushRange = not na(pushPeak) and not na(pushStartPrice) ? pushPeak - pushStartPrice : na
// V4.7: the forming bar's low counts immediately for DISPLAY. At bar
// close the state machine has already folded it in, so this is a no-op
// then and pure live information intrabar.
pullbackLowLive = (setupState == PULLBACK or setupState == ARMED) and liveEval and not na(pullbackLow) ?
     math.min(pullbackLow, low) : pullbackLow
retracementPct = setupState == PULLBACK or setupState == ARMED ?
     f_safeDiv(pushPeak - pullbackLowLive, pushRange, na) * 100.0 : na

pullbackAvgVolume = pullbackBars > 0 ? pullbackVolumeSum / pullbackBars : na
pullbackVolumeRatio = pullbackBars > 0 ? f_safeDiv(pullbackAvgVolume, pushAvgVolume, na) : na
decliningPBVolume = pullbackBars <= 1 ? true : volume < volume[1]

candleRange = high - low
lowerWick = math.min(open, close) - low
upperWick = high - math.max(open, close)
lowerWickPct = f_safeDiv(lowerWick, candleRange, 0.0) * 100.0
upperWickPct = f_safeDiv(upperWick, candleRange, 0.0) * 100.0
bottomingTail = lowerWickPct >= bullishLowerWickPct
toppingTailWarning = upperWickPct >= toppingTailWarnPct

emaBullish = close > ema9 and ema9 >= ema20

// V12.18: the four §10 states, named as the playbook names them.
bool tf5Known       = not na(c5) and not na(e9_5) and not na(e20_5)
bool tf5Constructive = tf5Known and c5 > e9_5 and e9_5 >= e20_5
bool tf1Constructive = emaBullish
string alignState = not tf5Known         ? "5m n/a" :
     tf5Constructive and tf1Constructive ? "aligned" :
     tf5Constructive and not tf1Constructive ? "1m weak" :
     not tf5Constructive and tf1Constructive ? "1m leads" : "neither"
// "aligned" is the best case; "1m weak" is the one the playbook says to
// refuse normally, because entry and risk are imprecise on the timeframe you
// are actually trading. "1m leads" is allowed only on an exceptional leader.
bool alignOK = alignState == "aligned" or alignState == "5m n/a"

// The oversized-5m-candle warning. A 5-minute bar several times the size of
// the 1-minute ATR means its low is a stop you cannot take at normal size.
float range5 = tf5Known and not na(h5) and not na(l5) ? h5 - l5 : na
bool bigBar5 = not na(range5) and not na(atr) and atr > 0 and range5 >= atr * bigBar5ATR
vwapKnown   = not na(vwapValue)                       // V4.6
vwapBullish = vwapKnown and close > vwapValue
macdBullish = macdValue > 0 and macdHist > 0
histogramIncreasing = macdHist > macdHist[1]

supportRef = (setupState == PULLBACK or setupState == ARMED) and not na(pullbackLowLive) ?
     pullbackLowLive : low
supportTolerance = math.max(supportRef * supportTolerancePct / 100.0, atr * supportToleranceATR)
nearestHalfDollar = math.round(supportRef * 2.0) / 2.0
// Confluence describes where the DIP found buyers. Testing distance from the
// closing price let a candle close near several averages after cutting far
// through them and still claim support. Require the pullback low to touch the
// level and the close to finish back on/above it.
ema9Support = math.abs(supportRef - ema9) <= supportTolerance and close >= ema9
ema20Support = math.abs(supportRef - ema20) <= supportTolerance and close >= ema20
vwapSupport = not na(vwapValue) and math.abs(supportRef - vwapValue) <= supportTolerance and close >= vwapValue
roundSupport = math.abs(supportRef - nearestHalfDollar) <= supportTolerance and close >= nearestHalfDollar
// V11 (from V10): §3 names six confluence components; V9 carried four. The
// 200 MA and the flipped level are the two most-cited in the corpus after
// the moving averages (daily/weekly level 157 mentions, former resistance
// flipped 142) and both are pure arithmetic on bars.
ma200Support = not na(ma200v) and math.abs(supportRef - ma200v) <= supportTolerance and close >= ma200v
// A flipped level is resistance that was BROKEN and is now retested from
// above. Testing only "price is near a prior high" is a tautology — it
// counts every nearby swing high and inflates the confluence count. The
// level must actually have been exceeded since it formed.
flipSupport = not na(flipLevel) and not na(flipBreakBar) and bar_index > flipBreakBar and
     math.abs(supportRef - flipLevel) <= supportTolerance and close >= flipLevel
emaClustered = ema9Support and ema20Support and math.abs(ema9 - ema20) <= supportTolerance
// ── V12.24: the two components the corpus ranks highest and the code never
// counted ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// WETO ran +90% and the panel read "Conf 0" while the SAME SCRIPT was drawing
// "S 10.50" on the chart. Zero confluence on a chart displaying a support the
// dip was bouncing off. That is a false negative, not a conservative call.
//
// Cause: five of the six components -- EMA9, EMA20, VWAP, 200 EMA, and to a
// degree the flipped level -- are MEAN-REVERTING lines. On a vertical runner
// they sit far below the pullback low by construction, so they cannot be
// "within tolerance" of it. Requiring two of them systematically rejects the
// strongest movers, which are exactly the ones this strategy exists to trade.
//
// The playbook's own evidence table ranks the pairs Ross actually names:
//   daily level + moving average      54
//   trend line + whole dollar         54
//   former resistance + trend line    53
// "Daily / weekly chart level" alone: 157 mentions across 42 videos -- the
// third most-cited component of all. It was not in at_support(). Neither was
// a gap or window edge, which the strong-chart checklist names as resistance
// in its own right.
//
// Both are pure arithmetic on data already computed above, so they are added
// here rather than approximated.
levelSupport = not na(nearestSup) and
     math.abs(supportRef - nearestSup) <= supportTolerance and close >= nearestSup
voidEdgeSupport = (not na(winBot) and math.abs(supportRef - winBot) <= supportTolerance and close >= winBot) or
     (not na(winTop) and math.abs(supportRef - winTop) <= supportTolerance and close >= winTop) or
     (not na(gapBot) and math.abs(supportRef - gapBot) <= supportTolerance and close >= gapBot) or
     (not na(gapTop) and math.abs(supportRef - gapTop) <= supportTolerance and close >= gapTop)

// V12.26: resolve the §15 target hierarchy into one price.
f_firstTarget(float entryPx, float riskPs) =>
    float floorPx = entryPx + riskPs * t1MinR
    float best = na
    if t1UseLevels and not na(entryPx) and not na(riskPs) and riskPs > 0
        // 1. HOD -- the top of the hierarchy
        best := f_lowerAbove(best, dayHigh, floorPx)
        // pre-market high, the level the open trades against
        best := f_lowerAbove(best, pmHigh, floorPx)
        // 3. the next half dollar, then the next whole dollar
        best := f_lowerAbove(best, math.ceil(entryPx * 2.0) / 2.0, floorPx)
        best := f_lowerAbove(best, math.ceil(entryPx), floorPx)
        // gap and window edges -- both boundaries are real prices
        best := f_lowerAbove(best, winBot, floorPx)
        best := f_lowerAbove(best, winTop, floorPx)
        best := f_lowerAbove(best, gapBot, floorPx)
        best := f_lowerAbove(best, gapTop, floorPx)
        // 4. nearest confirmed structural resistance
        best := f_lowerAbove(best, nearestRes, floorPx)
    // no qualifying level: the mechanical 1R it always used
    na(best) ? entryPx + riskPs : best

supportCountRaw = (levelSupport ? 1 : 0) + (voidEdgeSupport ? 1 : 0) +
     (ema9Support ? 1 : 0) + (ema20Support ? 1 : 0) + (vwapSupport ? 1 : 0) +
     (roundSupport ? 1 : 0) + (ma200Support ? 1 : 0) + (flipSupport ? 1 : 0)
supportCount = supportCountRaw - (emaClustered ? 1 : 0)

candidateTrigger = setupState == PULLBACK ? high + breakoutBufferTicks * syminfo.mintick : triggerPrice
candidateStopRaw = setupState == PULLBACK ? pullbackLowLive : structuralStop
// V7 (reviewer): a retest setup's stop must sit BELOW the level it claims to
// trade against — a stop above the reclaimed HOD defends nothing.
candidateStopRaw := setupState == PULLBACK and setupKind == KIND_RETEST and not na(setupRetestLevel) ?
     math.min(candidateStopRaw, setupRetestLevel - retestStopBufferTicks * syminfo.mintick) :
     candidateStopRaw
candidateRiskRaw = candidateTrigger - candidateStopRaw
// V5.2: wide-candle fallback — audit: candle-low stops are fiction on wide
// bars. The substituted stop satisfies the risk caps by construction.
candidateWide = not na(candidateRiskRaw) and candidateRiskRaw > 0 and
     (f_safeDiv(candidateRiskRaw, candidateTrigger, 0.0) * 100.0 > maxStopPct or
      f_safeDiv(candidateRiskRaw, atr, 0.0) > maxStopATR)
usingATRstop = atrStopFallback and candidateWide
candidateStop = usingATRstop ? candidateTrigger - atr * fallbackATRmult : candidateStopRaw
candidateRisk = candidateTrigger - candidateStop
candidateRiskPct = f_safeDiv(candidateRisk, candidateTrigger, na) * 100.0
candidateRiskATR = f_safeDiv(candidateRisk, atr, na)
candidateRRtoPeak = f_safeDiv(pushPeak - candidateTrigger, candidateRisk, na)

// room to the day's high, in R — the honest overhead measure
candidateRRtoHOD = f_safeDiv(dayHigh - candidateTrigger, candidateRisk, na)
// is this impulse making the high, or is it a lower high under trapped supply?
peakIsHOD = not na(pushPeak) and not na(dayHigh) and pushPeak >= dayHigh - syminfo.mintick
// the FIRST obstacle above the trigger is what a 1R move must clear
nextObstacleR = candidateTrigger < pushPeak ? candidateRRtoPeak : candidateRRtoHOD
// V6 (finding 14): the declaration's slippage is applied adversely to the
// stop entry AND the stop exit — so the modelled worst-case loss per share
// is structural risk + 2×slippage. Sizing on structural risk alone let a
// 10-cent plan lose ~3× its budget in simulation. Size on the worst case.
// V8: the assumption is the slipTicksInput input — keep it equal to the
// Properties slippage setting (Pine cannot read it back).
entryAdversePerShare = (useCappedStopLimit ? entryCapTicks : slipTicksInput) * syminfo.mintick
exitAdversePerShare = slipTicksInput * syminfo.mintick
slipPerShare = entryAdversePerShare + exitAdversePerShare
effRiskPerShare = candidateRisk > 0 ? candidateRisk + slipPerShare : na
// Fixed per-order commissions are not proportional to shares. Reserve the
// entire planned order count first, then size the remaining risk dollars.
// Entry + T1 + T2 + runner = four orders for the three-rung ladder; the
// two-leg ladder is entry + T1 + runner = three. This is conservative for a
// 1-share position, which cannot scale.
plannedOrderCount = useThirdRung ? 4.0 : 3.0
commissionReserve = plannedOrderCount * commissionPerOrderInput
riskBudgetAfterFees = math.max(riskBudget - commissionReserve, 0.0)
candidateRiskShares = not na(effRiskPerShare) ? math.floor(riskBudgetAfterFees / effRiskPerShare) : 0.0
// V7.1 (operator): the tradeable size must be visible at ALL times, not only
// once a setup exists. With no plan, this answers "if I bought right here
// with an ATR stop, how many shares does my $ risk buy" — same slippage-aware
// sizing as a real plan, labelled as hypothetical on the dashboard.
// V9.4 (operator: "stops too narrow"): the hypothetical stop is now
// STRUCTURAL — under the lowest low of the last 5 bars — and never
// tighter than 1 fallback-ATR. A bare 1-ATR stop on a 1-min chart of a
// beaten-down mover was fiction; under the swing low is where the real
// stop goes (and 2R of the wider risk moves the target out with it).
anyStop = math.min(ta.lowest(low, 5) - syminfo.mintick, close - atr * fallbackATRmult)
anyRisk = close - anyStop
cashCapacity = math.max(math.min(maxPositionValue, equityBase), 0.0)
anyShares = anyRisk > 0 ? math.min(math.floor(riskBudgetAfterFees / (anyRisk + slipPerShare)),
     math.floor(cashCapacity / close)) : na
candidateCapitalShares = candidateTrigger > 0 ? math.floor(cashCapacity / candidateTrigger) : 0.0
// V11 (from V10): §7 PARTICIPATION cap — a third bound, alongside risk and
// capital. §7's formula alone asks a $100k account for ~20,000 shares of a $5
// stock off an 8-cent stop; the capital cap makes that affordable but not
// FILLABLE. On a sub-20M float that order does not exist at any price, and
// §7 concedes the point itself: "fill quality degrades with size on sub-20M
// float. The edge does not scale linearly." A backtest without this reports
// P&L on shares that were never buyable.
v11TapeMedian = ta.median(volume, participationLen)[1]
candidateTapeShares = useParticipationCap ?
     (not na(v11TapeMedian) and v11TapeMedian > 0 ?
          math.floor(v11TapeMedian * participationPct / 100.0) : 0.0) : 1e12
candidateShares = math.min(math.min(candidateRiskShares, candidateCapitalShares), candidateTapeShares)
// which bound actually bit — surfaced on the dashboard, because a size set by
// liquidity is not the 1-2% of account §7 intends and the expectancy model
// scales down with it
v11SizeBoundBy = candidateShares <= 0 ? "none" :
     candidateShares == candidateRiskShares ? "risk" :
     candidateShares == candidateCapitalShares ? "cash" : "liquidity"

// V4: halt-band check — a stop wider than the band cannot be honoured.
// V5: the veto is RTH-only; outside it the band is information, not a gate.
// V6 (finding 9): FAIL-CLOSED — an unknown band inside RTH now vetoes
// instead of silently passing. na used to compare as non-blocking.
stopExceedsHaltBand = inRTH and (na(haltBandWidth) or candidateRisk > haltBandWidth)


pushGate = pushPct >= minPushPct and pushATR >= minPushATR and pushEfficiency >= minEfficiency and pushRVOL >= minPushRVOL and pushDollarVolume >= minDollarVolume
// V6 (finding 12): a retest setup's pullback IS the touch — a red candle is
// not part of that pattern's definition, so it is not demanded of it.
pullbackCountGate = pullbackBars >= minPullbackBars and pullbackBars <= maxPullbackBars and
     (redPullbackBars >= 1 or setupKind == KIND_RETEST)
retracementGate = not na(retracementPct) and retracementPct <= maxRetracementPct
volumeGate = not na(pullbackVolumeRatio) and pullbackVolumeRatio <= maxPBVolumeRatio
momentumGate = (not requireMACD or macdBullish) and (not requireEMA or emaBullish) and (not requireVWAP or vwapBullish)
riskGate = candidateRisk > 0 and not na(candidateRiskPct) and candidateRiskPct <= maxStopPct and
     not na(candidateRiskATR) and candidateRiskATR <= maxStopATR and
     (not useMaxDollarStop or candidateRisk <= maxStopDollar) and candidateShares >= 1 and
     (not haltBandVeto or not stopExceedsHaltBand)                     // V4
rrGate = not requireRRtoPeak or (not na(candidateRRtoPeak) and candidateRRtoPeak >= minRRtoPeak)
// V5: default OFF. A scanner criterion is a DISCOVERY dial; using it as a
// trade gate is this project's single most repeated error (21 corrections).
// Available for anyone who wants it, never on by default.
scanGate = not scanGates or pillarScore == 4
sessionGate = inSession                                                 // V4
// V8: entryTimeOK (no arming on the last in-window bar) is a hard part of
// the entry decision — enforced inside hardGatesOK and the lane's fastOK.
// V7 (reviewer): outside RTH the real venue takes LIMIT orders only, so the
// emulator's stop/market fills there are fiction. Arming is RTH-only unless
// the operator explicitly opts into invalid fill modelling. The verdict and
// the whole display still run pre-market — only order placement is gated.
// V8 (P31): supported-market enforcement, written definition — the audit
// data, session window (ET), halt-band model and gap rules are US-listed
// EQUITY small-caps on a 1-minute chart. Anything else (crypto, forex,
// futures, CFD) runs display-only: no arming, no orders. This is a paper
// research model; widening the supported set is a re-validation task, not
// an input toggle.
// V9.2 (live PCLA 2026-08-20): ADRs are "dr", not "stock", and the gate
// rejected a NASDAQ-listed runner outright. Foreign ADRs are a large part
// of the small-cap momentum universe; they stay IN. (CLAUDE.md rule 7's
// dilution blind spot for foreign private issuers is a manual check, not
// an exclusion.)
supportedMarket = syminfo.type == "stock" or syminfo.type == "dr"
venueGate = supportedMarket and (inRTH or allowPremarketEmulatorFills)

// ═══════════════════ V11 (from V10): §8 DAILY RISK LIMITS ═══════════════════
// V9 implemented none of §8, so a losing day compounded instead of stopping.
// All five rules, with one structural point that took a reproduction to find:
//
// The 20% drawdown walkaway is ACCOUNT scope and must be evaluated FIRST and
// INDEPENDENTLY of the four daily latches. Chained behind them in an else-if,
// it is close to unreachable — a 20% account drawdown is always assembled out
// of days that trip the 6% daily loss or green-to-red first, so those consume
// the branch and the walkaway never records. Reproduced: high-water mark
// 100,000, day opens at 85,000, equity falls to 79,800 -> the 6.12% daily loss
// fires and exits the chain while the 20.20% account drawdown is never tested.
// The account is a fifth underwater and trades again next morning.
varip float v11DayStartEq  = na
varip float v11DayPeakEq   = na
varip float v11Hwm         = na
varip int   v11DayTrades   = 0
varip int   v11ConsecLoss  = 0
varip bool  v11Locked      = false
varip string v11LockReason = ""
varip bool  v11AcctLocked  = false      // walkaway outlives the session
varip int v11LastSettledEntryBar = na

if barstate.isnew and v11NewDay
    v11DayStartEq := strategy.equity
    v11DayPeakEq  := strategy.equity
    v11DayTrades  := 0
    v11ConsecLoss := 0
    v11Locked     := v11AcctLocked            // the walkaway survives the night
    v11LockReason := v11AcctLocked ? "drawdown walkaway" : ""

v11DayStartEq := nz(v11DayStartEq, strategy.equity)
v11DayPeakEq  := math.max(nz(v11DayPeakEq, strategy.equity), strategy.equity)
v11Hwm        := math.max(nz(v11Hwm, strategy.equity), strategy.equity)

// Count entries, not position_size bar transitions. The latter misses a
// complete entry+exit inside one historical bar; setupsToday is already the
// exactly-once fill counter reconciled against strategy.closedtrades.
v11DayTrades := setupsToday

// Settle the consecutive-loss streak once per completed POSITION, not once
// per partial exit. resPnL is the multi-leg, commission-inclusive result.
bool v11RoundTripSettled = strategy.position_size == 0 and setupState == DONE and
     not na(lastCountedEntryBar) and
     (na(v11LastSettledEntryBar) or lastCountedEntryBar != v11LastSettledEntryBar)
if v11RoundTripSettled
    v11LastSettledEntryBar := lastCountedEntryBar
    v11ConsecLoss := resPnL < 0 ? v11ConsecLoss + 1 : resPnL > 0 ? 0 : v11ConsecLoss

// Evaluate equity continuously, including open P&L. The old block ran only
// after a position became flat, so a live trade could breach every stated
// limit without the governor noticing or flattening it.
v11LossPctNow = v11DayStartEq > 0 ?
     (v11DayStartEq - strategy.equity) / v11DayStartEq * 100.0 : 0.0
v11PeakGainNow = v11DayPeakEq - v11DayStartEq
v11GivenBackNow = v11PeakGainNow > 0 ?
     (v11DayPeakEq - strategy.equity) / v11PeakGainNow * 100.0 : 0.0
v11DdPctNow = v11Hwm > 0 ? (v11Hwm - strategy.equity) / v11Hwm * 100.0 : 0.0

if useRiskGovernor
    // ACCOUNT scope is independent and survives the day boundary.
    if v11DdPctNow >= ddWalkawayPct
        v11AcctLocked := true
        v11Locked     := true
        v11LockReason := "drawdown walkaway"

    // Daily latches release next session unless the account walkaway fired.
    if not v11Locked
        if v11LossPctNow >= maxDailyLossPct
            v11Locked := true
            v11LockReason := "max daily loss"
        else if v11PeakGainNow > 0 and v11GivenBackNow >= givebackPct
            v11Locked := true
            v11LockReason := "giveback of peak gain"
        else if useGreenToRed and v11DayPeakEq > v11DayStartEq and strategy.equity < v11DayStartEq
            v11Locked := true
            v11LockReason := "green to red"
        else if v11ConsecLoss >= consecLossMax
            v11Locked := true
            v11LockReason := "consecutive losses"

    // A rule called a loss stop must act on the risk already open, not merely
    // block tomorrow's entry. Boundary closes set the flag earlier and retain
    // priority; this branch never creates a competing close.
    if v11Locked and strategy.position_size > 0 and not flattenRequested
        flattenRequested := true
        flattenReason := "§8 risk governor — " + v11LockReason
        flattenIsBailout := false

v11RiskGovernorOK = not useRiskGovernor or
     (not v11Locked and v11DayTrades < maxTradesPerDay)

// V11 (from V10): §3 confluence is now a GATE, not decoration. V9 computed
// supportCount and spent it only on the display-only quality score, so a dip
// that stopped at no level at all could still arm. §3 is explicit —
// confluence_min = 2, "not one, two" — and it is the tightest condition in
// the entry gate.
confluenceGate = not requireConfluence or supportCount >= minConfluence
// §3 pullback_index <= 2. Index 0 means no dip is in progress.
pullbackIndexGate = not requirePullbackIndex or
     (v11PbIndex >= 1 and v11PbIndex <= maxPullbackIndex)

hardGatesOK = pushGate and pullbackCountGate and retracementGate and volumeGate and momentumGate and riskGate and rrGate and scanGate and sessionGate and venueGate and entryTimeOK and confluenceGate and pullbackIndexGate and v11RiskGovernorOK

// ─────────────────── Quality number: DISPLAY ONLY (V4) ───────────────────
// V4: A+/A/B letter grades REMOVED. Origin of the demotion: MEASURED —
// reports/2026-08-score-basket.md: a pillar score lost 16 of 16 matched
// pairs against equal weight and was anti-predictive above 50. The number
// below never gates anything and is labelled display-only on the dashboard.
pushStrengthNorm = minPushPct > 0 ? math.min(pushPct / minPushPct, 1.5) : 0.0
rvolNorm = minPushRVOL > 0 ? math.min(pushRVOL / minPushRVOL, 1.5) : 0.0
effNorm = minEfficiency > 0 ? math.min(pushEfficiency / minEfficiency, 1.5) : 1.0
atrNorm = minPushATR > 0 ? math.min(pushATR / minPushATR, 1.5) : 0.0
impulseScore = math.min(30.0, 8.0 * pushStrengthNorm + 8.0 * rvolNorm + 7.0 * effNorm + 7.0 * atrNorm)
retracementPoints = not na(retracementPct) ? (retracementPct <= 25 ? 12.0 : retracementPct <= 35 ? 10.0 : retracementPct <= 50 ? 6.0 : 0.0) : 0.0
volumePoints = not na(pullbackVolumeRatio) ? (pullbackVolumeRatio <= 0.40 ? 10.0 : pullbackVolumeRatio <= 0.55 ? 8.0 : pullbackVolumeRatio <= maxPBVolumeRatio ? 5.0 : 0.0) : 0.0
pullbackScore = math.min(30.0, retracementPoints + volumePoints + (decliningPBVolume ? 4.0 : 0.0) + (bottomingTail ? 4.0 : 0.0))
momentumScore = math.min(20.0, (emaBullish ? 5.0 : 0.0) + (vwapBullish ? 3.0 : 0.0) + (macdBullish ? 8.0 : 0.0) + (histogramIncreasing ? 4.0 : 0.0))
roomPoints = candidateRRtoPeak >= 2.0 ? 8.0 : candidateRRtoPeak >= 1.0 ? 4.0 : candidateRRtoPeak >= 0.5 ? 2.0 : 0.0
riskCompactPoints = candidateRiskPct <= 1.5 ? 3.0 : candidateRiskPct <= maxStopPct ? 1.5 : 0.0
structureScore = math.min(20.0, roomPoints + math.min(supportCount, 3) * 2.0 + (not toppingTailWarning ? 3.0 : 0.0) + riskCompactPoints)
liveQuality = math.max(0.0, math.min(100.0, impulseScore + pullbackScore + momentumScore + structureScore))

// V8: na-safe reasons. retracementPct/pullbackVolumeRatio are na for lane
// setups with no push record — the old chain printed "Dip too deep (—%)",
// a sentinel rendered as prose (finding 19 residual). Unknown now says
// unknown. The red-candle reason respects KIND_RETEST, whose pattern does
// not require a red candle (finding 12 residual).
// V8.1 (V7.4 operator directive): the clock branches (session/venue/last
// bar) are GONE from this chain — the clock is not a verdict criterion. It
// lives on the TREND row's Clock lamp and the PLAN row's tag; the ORDER
// path still enforces it through hardGatesOK. (Unsupported symbols keep
// their own banner in actionText.)
string gateReason =
     not pushGate ? "Move up too weak to trade" :
     pullbackBars < minPullbackBars ? "Dip too short so far" :
     redPullbackBars < 1 and setupKind != KIND_RETEST ? "Waiting for a red candle" :
     na(retracementPct) ? "Dip depth not measurable for this setup kind" :
     not retracementGate ? "Dip too deep (" + f_n(retracementPct, "#.0") + "% of the move)" :
     na(pullbackVolumeRatio) ? "Dip volume not measurable for this setup kind" :
     not volumeGate ? "Too much selling in the dip (" + f_n(pullbackVolumeRatio, "#.00") + "x)" :
     requireMACD and not macdBullish ? "MACD not positive" :
     requireEMA and not emaBullish ? "Price below EMA9" :
     requireVWAP and not vwapBullish ? "Price below VWAP" :
     not confluenceGate ? "Only " + str.tostring(supportCount) + "/" + str.tostring(minConfluence) + " support reasons at the dip" :
     not pullbackIndexGate ? "Pullback #" + str.tostring(v11PbIndex) + " is outside the allowed index" :
     not v11RiskGovernorOK ? "Daily risk governor blocks new entries" :
     haltBandVeto and stopExceedsHaltBand ? "Stop " + f_px(candidateRisk) + " wider than LULD-width heuristic " + f_px(haltBandWidth) :
     not riskGate ? "Stop too far away to size safely" :
     requireRRtoPeak and not rrGate ? "Only " + f_rr(candidateRRtoPeak) + " to peak" :
     not scanGate ? "Scanner criteria " + str.tostring(pillarScore) + "/4" :
     "READY"

// ───────────────────────── Arm / invalidate at bar close ─────────────────────────
// V8: gated by confirmedPass + the cancel latch (re-audit: every arming path
// must check it; the close-commit runs earlier in the execution, this is
// belt-and-braces so no future reorder can resurrect a cancelled arm).
if confirmedPass and strategy.position_size == 0 and setupState == PULLBACK and
     not intrabarCancelled
    bool structuralInvalid = not na(retracementPct) and retracementPct > maxRetracementPct
    bool tooManyPullbackBars = pullbackBars > maxPullbackBars

    if structuralInvalid or tooManyPullbackBars
        strategy.cancel("Long")
        setupState := INVALID
        stateStartBar := bar_index
        scanAfterBar := bar_index
        statusReason := structuralInvalid ?
             "Rejected — dip too deep (" + f_n(retracementPct, "#.0") + "%)" :
             "Rejected — dip lasted too long"
        eventInvalid := true

    else if hardGatesOK
        triggerPrice := candidateTrigger
        structuralStop := candidateStop
        plannedRisk := candidateRisk
        plannedTarget := candidateTrigger + candidateRisk * rewardMultiple
        plannedRRtoPeak := candidateRRtoPeak
        // Pullback ordinal and trade count are different variables. The old
        // "third filled trade today" proxy halved unrelated setups and could
        // not implement a third-pullback rule. V11 already rejects pullbacks
        // beyond maxPullbackIndex, so no second sizing rule is invented here.
        plannedShares := candidateShares
        plannedSizeBoundBy := v11SizeBoundBy
        setupQuality := liveQuality
        plannedUsesATRStop := usingATRstop          // V8: provenance latched

        setupState := ARMED
        stateStartBar := bar_index
        statusReason := "Buy order set above " + str.tostring(triggerPrice, format.mintick)
        eventArmed := true

        strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qty=plannedShares, stop=triggerPrice,
             limit=useCappedStopLimit ? triggerPrice + entryCapTicks * syminfo.mintick : na,
             comment="IN",
             alert_message="ROSS FP " + REV + " ENTRY | {{ticker}} | paper fill | model=" +
                  (useCappedStopLimit ? "STOP_LIMIT" : "STOP_MARKET"))
        // V8 (re-audit critical 1): PRE-STAGED PROTECTION. Exits used to be
        // submitted only after the fill was detected — with
        // calc_on_order_fills=false the whole historical entry bar sat with
        // no stop and no target, and a bar touching trigger AND stop could
        // finish the backtest LONG. Resting exits placed with the entry are
        // live the moment the entry fills; the LONG block below re-prices
        // them to actual fill values on the first post-fill calculation.
        // V8 (P23): whole-share legs. qty_percent=50 of an odd count books
        // fractional shares the $2,000 cash account would never see. A
        // 1-share position skips T1 — there is no half to sell.
        // V11 (from V10): §6 scales 50 / 25 / 25, not 50 / 50. V9's ladder
        // sold half at 1R and ran the rest to target. The middle rung needs
        // at least 4 whole shares to exist — below that the ladder collapses
        // back to V9's two legs, which is also what useThirdRung=false does.
        float t1QtyArm = plannedShares >= 2 ? math.floor(plannedShares / 2) : na
        float t2QtyArm = useThirdRung and plannedShares >= 4 ?
             math.floor(plannedShares / 4) : na
        float stagedEntryArm = triggerPrice + entryAdversePerShare
        float stagedRiskArm = stagedEntryArm - structuralStop
        // V12.26: T1 is the nearest real level, not a bare 1R.
        float t1PxArm = f_firstTarget(stagedEntryArm, stagedRiskArm)
        if not na(t1QtyArm)
            strategy.exit("T1", from_entry="Long", qty=t1QtyArm,
                 stop=structuralStop, limit=t1PxArm,
                 comment_loss="STOP", comment_profit="T1",
                 alert_message="ROSS FP " + REV + " T1 | {{ticker}}")
        if not na(t2QtyArm)
            strategy.exit("T2", from_entry="Long", qty=t2QtyArm,
                 stop=structuralStop, limit=stagedEntryArm + stagedRiskArm * rewardMultiple,
                 comment_loss="STOP", comment_profit="T2",
                 alert_message="ROSS FP " + REV + " T2 | {{ticker}}")
        strategy.exit("RUNNER", from_entry="Long",
             qty=plannedShares - (na(t1QtyArm) ? 0 : t1QtyArm) - (na(t2QtyArm) ? 0 : t2QtyArm),
             stop=structuralStop,
             limit=stagedEntryArm + stagedRiskArm *
                  (na(t2QtyArm) ? rewardMultiple : rewardMultiple + 1.0),
             comment_loss="STOP", comment_profit="RUN",
             alert_message="ROSS FP " + REV + " EXIT | {{ticker}}")

    else if pullbackBars >= maxPullbackBars
        strategy.cancel("Long")
        setupState := INVALID
        stateStartBar := bar_index
        scanAfterBar := bar_index
        statusReason := "Rejected — " + gateReason
        eventInvalid := true

    else
        // V7.3: everything but the clock passed -> say so, place nothing.
        bool gatesExceptWindow = pushGate and pullbackCountGate and retracementGate and
             volumeGate and momentumGate and riskGate and rrGate and scanGate and
             confluenceGate and pullbackIndexGate and v11RiskGovernorOK
        if gatesExceptWindow and not (sessionGate and venueGate and entryTimeOK)
            eventGhost := true
            ghostTrig := candidateTrigger
            ghostStop := candidateStop
            ghostTgt := candidateTrigger + candidateRisk * rewardMultiple
            ghostShares := candidateShares
            ghostBar := bar_index
            statusReason := "BUY SIGNAL above " + str.tostring(candidateTrigger, format.mintick) +
                 " — NO ORDER (clock)"
        else
            statusReason := gateReason

// ───────────────────── V5.1 fast lane ─────────────────────
// Runs AFTER the formal arm block: if that path armed this bar, state is
// already ARMED and this is skipped. If it declined on a quality gate, this
// arms anyway — with the reason the formal path declined kept in view.
// V5.2: two lanes share this block. Structure lane (IMPULSE/PULLBACK) needs
// the input-configurable momentum gate. Uptrend lane (any state, YJ case)
// demands the FULL stack green, hard-coded — a looser lane with looser gates
// would just be noise.
fullStackGreen = macdBullish and emaBullish and vwapBullish
inStructure = setupState == IMPULSE or setupState == PULLBACK
// V6 (finding 6): the uptrend lane may arm ONLY from clean IDLE, never from
// the INVALID or DONE it used to overwrite in the same execution — a formal
// NO or a completed trade could previously re-arm one line later, emitting
// contradictory alerts for one candle. bar_index > stateStartBar keeps it
// off the transition bar; the latches keep it off cancel/close bars.
// V8 (re-audit ND-1): stateStartBar starts na, so `bar_index > stateStartBar`
// was na-false forever and the uptrend lane could NEVER arm from a virgin
// IDLE — the exact YJ recovery case the lane exists for. na means "no
// transition this run", i.e. clean.
laneOpen = (fastLane and inStructure and momentumGate) or
     (uptrendLane and setupState == IDLE and (na(stateStartBar) or bar_index > stateStartBar) and fullStackGreen)
// V8: gated by confirmedPass (was isconfirmed) — a fill recalculation must
// not run the lanes on final-OHLC data.
if confirmedPass and strategy.position_size == 0 and
     not intrabarCancelled and not eventInvalid and
     laneOpen and close < open
    float fTrig = high + breakoutBufferTicks * syminfo.mintick
    float fStopRaw = low
    float fRiskRaw = fTrig - fStopRaw
    // same wide-candle rule as the formal path — the YJ candle IS this case
    bool fWide = fRiskRaw > 0 and
         (f_safeDiv(fRiskRaw, fTrig, 0.0) * 100.0 > maxStopPct or
          f_safeDiv(fRiskRaw, atr, 0.0) > maxStopATR)
    bool fATR = atrStopFallback and fWide
    float fStop = fATR ? fTrig - atr * fallbackATRmult : fStopRaw
    float fRisk = fTrig - fStop
    float fRiskPct = f_safeDiv(fRisk, fTrig, na) * 100.0
    // V6 (finding 14): same slippage-aware sizing as the formal path
    float fRiskShares = fRisk > 0 ? math.floor(riskBudgetAfterFees / (fRisk + slipPerShare)) : 0.0
    float fCapitalShares = fTrig > 0 ? math.floor(cashCapacity / fTrig) : 0.0
    float fTapeShares = useParticipationCap ? candidateTapeShares : 1e12
    float fShares = math.min(math.min(fRiskShares, fCapitalShares), fTapeShares)
    string fSizeBound = fShares <= 0 ? "none" :
         fShares == fRiskShares ? "risk" : fShares == fCapitalShares ? "cash" : "liquidity"
    // V5.4: the lower-high guard. fTrig at/above HOD = breaking to open air;
    // otherwise demand >=1R before the overhead supply. Three TNON stops in
    // one session, all under a lower high, are what this line costs to skip.
    bool fRoomOK = not lanesRespectHOD or na(dayHigh) or fTrig >= dayHigh or
         (fRisk > 0 and (dayHigh - fTrig) / fRisk >= 1.0)
    // V6 (finding 9): the lanes now pass the SAME global controls the formal
    // path advertises as hard — session, post-fallback ATR cap, dollar cap,
    // scanner veto when user-enabled, fail-closed halt band. The lanes still
    // skip only what they are documented to skip: push quality, retracement,
    // pullback volume.
    bool fHaltOK = not haltBandVeto or not inRTH or
         (not na(haltBandWidth) and fRisk <= haltBandWidth)
    float fRiskATR = f_safeDiv(fRisk, atr, na)
    bool fastCoreOK = fRisk > 0 and not na(fRiskPct) and fRiskPct <= maxStopPct and
         not na(fRiskATR) and fRiskATR <= maxStopATR and
         (not useMaxDollarStop or fRisk <= maxStopDollar) and
         fRoomOK and fShares >= 1 and fHaltOK and scanGate and
         confluenceGate and pullbackIndexGate and v11RiskGovernorOK
    bool fastOK = fastCoreOK and sessionGate and venueGate and entryTimeOK
    // V7.3: lane pattern valid, clock refused -> ghost, not silence.
    if fastCoreOK and not fastOK
        eventGhost := true
        ghostTrig := fTrig
        ghostStop := fStop
        ghostTgt := fTrig + fRisk * rewardMultiple
        ghostShares := fShares
        ghostBar := bar_index
        statusReason := "BUY SIGNAL above " + str.tostring(fTrig, format.mintick) +
             " — NO ORDER (clock)"
    if fastOK
        triggerPrice := fTrig
        structuralStop := fStop
        plannedRisk := fRisk
        plannedTarget := fTrig + fRisk * rewardMultiple
        plannedRRtoPeak := f_safeDiv(dayHigh - fTrig, fRisk, na)
        plannedShares := fShares
        plannedSizeBoundBy := fSizeBound
        setupQuality := liveQuality
        plannedUsesATRStop := fATR                       // V8: provenance latched
        setupState := ARMED
        stateStartBar := bar_index
        // V6 (finding 8): a lane arm initialises a COMPLETE setup record with
        // its own provenance kind. Before this it inherited whatever the
        // previous setup left — including KIND_RETEST labels on lane entries
        // and na pullbackLow that poisoned every later math.min().
        setupKind := inStructure ? KIND_FAST : KIND_UPTREND
        pullbackLow := na(pullbackLow) ? low : math.min(pullbackLow, low)
        // V8 (re-audit ND-2): count the signal bar's volume ONCE. When the
        // state-update block already folded this bar into the pullback
        // (bar_index == pullbackLastBar), adding it again here double-counted
        // it and poisoned the pullback/push volume ratio.
        if bar_index != pullbackLastBar
            pullbackVolumeSum := pullbackVolumeSum > 0 ? pullbackVolumeSum + volume : volume
        redPullbackBars := math.max(redPullbackBars, 1)
        if setupKind == KIND_UPTREND
            // no push record exists in a clean-IDLE arm; leave push* na so
            // retracement math reads na (not a sentinel) and cannot
            // false-invalidate. The intrabar cancel keys on structuralStop.
            pushPeak := na
            pushStartPrice := na
        // V5.3 (YJ zombie bug): the lane armed from IMPULSE with
        // pullbackLastBar = na, so `bar_index > pullbackLastBar` was na-false
        // forever: the state could neither refresh its trigger nor expire.
        // Combined with the safety cancel below, that produced a TRIGGER SET
        // showing a 20-minute-old plan 0.70 below price.
        pullbackLastBar := bar_index
        pullbackStartBar := na(pullbackStartBar) ? bar_index : pullbackStartBar
        pullbackBars := math.max(pullbackBars, 1)
        statusReason := "Buy order set above " + str.tostring(fTrig, format.mintick) +
             " (red-candle high)" +
             (fATR ? " · wide candle, ATR stop " + str.tostring(fStop, format.mintick) : "")
        eventArmed := true
        strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qty=plannedShares, stop=fTrig,
             limit=useCappedStopLimit ? fTrig + entryCapTicks * syminfo.mintick : na,
             comment="IN-Q",
             alert_message="ROSS FP " + REV + " FAST ENTRY | {{ticker}} | paper fill | model=" +
                  (useCappedStopLimit ? "STOP_LIMIT" : "STOP_MARKET"))
        // V8: same pre-staged protection as the formal path — the historical
        // entry bar is never naked. Whole-share legs (P23), as above.
        float t1QtyLane = plannedShares >= 2 ? math.floor(plannedShares / 2) : na
        float t2QtyLane = useThirdRung and plannedShares >= 4 ?
             math.floor(plannedShares / 4) : na          // V11: §6 middle rung
        float stagedEntryLane = fTrig + entryAdversePerShare
        float stagedRiskLane = stagedEntryLane - fStop
        if not na(t1QtyLane)
            strategy.exit("T1", from_entry="Long", qty=t1QtyLane,
                 stop=fStop, limit=stagedEntryLane + stagedRiskLane,
                 comment_loss="STOP", comment_profit="T1",
                 alert_message="ROSS FP " + REV + " T1 | {{ticker}}")
        if not na(t2QtyLane)
            strategy.exit("T2", from_entry="Long", qty=t2QtyLane,
                 stop=fStop, limit=stagedEntryLane + stagedRiskLane * rewardMultiple,
                 comment_loss="STOP", comment_profit="T2",
                 alert_message="ROSS FP " + REV + " T2 | {{ticker}}")
        strategy.exit("RUNNER", from_entry="Long",
             qty=plannedShares - (na(t1QtyLane) ? 0 : t1QtyLane) - (na(t2QtyLane) ? 0 : t2QtyLane),
             stop=fStop,
             limit=stagedEntryLane + stagedRiskLane *
                  (na(t2QtyLane) ? rewardMultiple : rewardMultiple + 1.0),
             comment_loss="STOP", comment_profit="RUN",
             alert_message="ROSS FP " + REV + " EXIT | {{ticker}}")

// V6 (finding 4): commit the one-pass-per-bar latch after all signal blocks.
if confirmedPass
    lastSignalBar := bar_index

// ───────────────────── Realtime safety cancellation ─────────────────────
// V6 (finding 1): the V5.3 version wrote INVALID/IDLE into ordinary `var`
// state intrabar. Pine rolls those writes back before the next realtime
// tick while the strategy.cancel() persists — recreating the exact zombie
// (TRIGGER SET with no working order) the fix claimed to remove. Now the
// cancel latches `intrabarCancelled` (varip — survives the rollback); the
// in-execution state change is display-only, and the CLOSE execution
// commits INVALID durably below. Arming paths all check the latch.
// The cancel condition is also simplified to the level that means it:
// price touching the STRUCTURAL STOP before the trigger kills the setup —
// well-defined for every setup kind, including lanes with no push record.
if isOneMinute and setupState == ARMED and strategy.position_size == 0 and
     not barstate.isconfirmed and not intrabarCancelled and
     not na(structuralStop) and low <= structuralStop
    strategy.cancel("Long")
    intrabarCancelled := true
    setupState := INVALID
    statusReason := "Rejected — price hit the stop level first, order removed"

// V5.3/V6 STALENESS GUARD: flat with price a full ATR above the trigger
// means no order is working, whatever the state machine believes.
if isOneMinute and setupState == ARMED and strategy.position_size == 0 and
     not barstate.isconfirmed and not intrabarCancelled and
     not na(triggerPrice) and close > triggerPrice + atr
    strategy.cancel("Long")
    intrabarCancelled := true
    setupState := IDLE
    statusReason := "Old order at " + str.tostring(triggerPrice, format.mintick) + " dropped — price left it behind"

// ───────────────────────── Trade management ─────────────────────────
// V6 (finding 16): the dashboard promised "half at T1, stop to break-even,
// rest to 2R" while the code ran a single all-or-nothing bracket — the
// Strategy Tester and the screen described two different strategies. The
// ladder is now real: T1 sells floor(qty/2) whole shares at entry+1R; once
// the partial fill is
// detected (strategy.closedtrades increments, position shrinks) the runner's
// stop moves to entry. Detection lands one tick late live / next bar in
// backtest — a conservative, disclosed lag.
if strategy.position_size > 0 and setupState == LONG and tradeRisk > 0
    float t1Target = tradeEntryPrice + tradeRisk
    // V8 (P23): whole-share legs keyed on the ACTUAL filled size; the runner
    // always covers exactly what remains, never a fractional approximation.
    float t1QtyLive = not na(tradeInitialQty) and tradeInitialQty >= 2 ?
         math.floor(tradeInitialQty / 2) : na
    // V11: the middle rung is re-priced on the ACTUAL filled size, same as T1.
    float t2QtyLive = useThirdRung and not na(tradeInitialQty) and tradeInitialQty >= 4 ?
         math.floor(tradeInitialQty / 4) : na
    if not t1Filled and not na(t1QtyLive)
        strategy.exit("T1", from_entry="Long", qty=t1QtyLive,
             stop=structuralStop, limit=t1Target,
             comment_loss="STOP", comment_profit="T1",
             alert_message="ROSS FP " + REV + " T1 | {{ticker}}")
    if not t2Filled and not na(t2QtyLive) and strategy.position_size > t2QtyLive
        strategy.exit("T2", from_entry="Long", qty=t2QtyLive,
             stop=t1Filled ? tradeEntryPrice : structuralStop, limit=activeTarget,
             comment_loss=t1Filled ? "BE" : "STOP", comment_profit="T2",
             alert_message="ROSS FP " + REV + " T2 | {{ticker}}")
    strategy.exit("RUNNER", from_entry="Long",
         qty=strategy.position_size - (not t2Filled and not na(t2QtyLive) and
              strategy.position_size > t2QtyLive ? t2QtyLive : 0),
         stop=t1Filled ? tradeEntryPrice : structuralStop,
         limit=na(t2QtyLive) ? activeTarget : activeTarget + tradeRisk,
         comment_loss=t1Filled ? "BE" : "STOP", comment_profit="RUN",
         alert_message="ROSS FP " + REV + " EXIT | {{ticker}}")

mfeR = setupState == LONG and tradeRisk > 0 ?
     f_safeDiv(highestSinceEntry - tradeEntryPrice, tradeRisk, 0.0) : na
barsAfterEntry = setupState == LONG and not na(tradeEntryBar) ? bar_index - tradeEntryBar : 0

// V8: gated by confirmedPass (was isconfirmed) — bailout decisions are
// signal logic; they must not re-run on a fill recalculation's final OHLC.
if confirmedPass and strategy.position_size > 0 and setupState == LONG and bar_index > tradeEntryBar
    highestSinceEntry := math.max(highestSinceEntry, high)
    mfeR := f_safeDiv(highestSinceEntry - tradeEntryPrice, tradeRisk, 0.0)
    barsAfterEntry := bar_index - tradeEntryBar

    bool failedMFE = bailoutEnabled and barsAfterEntry >= bailoutBars and mfeR < minimumMFER
    bool lostEntryEarly = bailoutEnabled and bailOnCloseBelowEntry and barsAfterEntry <= bailoutBars and close < tradeEntryPrice

    // V11 (from V10): two §6 hard exits V9 computed but never acted on.
    // toppingTailWarning existed and was spent only on the display-only
    // quality score; §6 lists a large topping tail as a hard exit (n=8), and
    // "green candles shrinking / momentum stalls" as another (n=168 for the
    // volume family it belongs to). Both are arithmetic on bars.
    //
    // These route through the SAME single flatten flag as the bailout — V9's
    // own V8 fix #9 was that competing strategy.close calls could fire two
    // different stories in one execution, and adding a third close would
    // reintroduce exactly that.
    bool v11ToppingTail = useToppingTailExit and toppingTailWarning and
         close <= high - candleRange * 0.40
    bool v11Stalling = useStallExit and close > open and close[1] > open[1] and
         close[2] > open[2] and candleRange < (high[1] - low[1]) and
         (high[1] - low[1]) < (high[2] - low[2]) and
         volume < volume[1] and volume[1] < volume[2]

    if (failedMFE or lostEntryEarly or v11ToppingTail or v11Stalling) and not flattenRequested
        flattenRequested := true
        flattenIsBailout := true
        flattenReason := failedMFE ?
             "Exiting — no follow-through (" + f_n(mfeR, "#.00") + "R best)" :
             lostEntryEarly ? "Exiting — closed below entry" :
             v11ToppingTail ? "Exiting — large topping tail, sellers hit the push" :
             "Exiting — green candles shrinking, momentum stalled"

// V8 (re-audit ND-7): the ONE authoritative close of the execution. Boundary
// reasons (set above) win over bailout reasons; exactly one strategy.close,
// exactly one reason, exactly one alert stream entry.
if flattenRequested and strategy.position_size > 0
    // V6 (finding 15): no immediately=true — the market order fills at the
    // next tick/bar open, not at the close it just observed.
    // V9 (defect 3): the chart shows a code; the sentence goes to STATUS.
    strategy.close("Long", comment=flattenIsBailout ? "BAIL" : "FLAT",
         alert_message="ROSS FP " + REV + (flattenIsBailout ? " BAILOUT | " : " FLAT | ") + "{{ticker}}")
    statusReason := flattenReason
    if flattenIsBailout
        eventBailout := true

// ───────────────────────── Display values ─────────────────────────
// V8 (re-audit critical: zombie display): the state machine's own var rolls
// back to ARMED between ticks while the varip cancel latch persists. The
// dashboard must render the EFFECTIVE state, not the rolled-back one —
// otherwise the chart says "ORDER SET / BUY >" for an order the broker no
// longer holds. The close-commit block turns this into a durable INVALID at
// the bar close; this derivation covers the rest of the bar.
bool cancelledPending = intrabarCancelled and strategy.position_size == 0 and
     (setupState == ARMED or setupState == PULLBACK)
int displayState = cancelledPending ? INVALID : setupState

displayQuality = displayState == ARMED or displayState == LONG ? setupQuality : liveQuality
displayEntry = displayState == LONG ? tradeEntryPrice : displayState == ARMED ? triggerPrice : candidateTrigger
// V8 (re-audit F16 residual): once T1 is filled the working stop IS the
// entry price — showing the old structural stop afterwards lied about the
// trade's actual risk.
displayStop = displayState == LONG and t1Filled ? tradeEntryPrice :
     displayState == LONG or displayState == ARMED ? structuralStop : candidateStop
displayTarget = displayState == LONG ?
     (useThirdRung and not na(tradeInitialQty) and tradeInitialQty >= 4 and t2Filled ?
          activeTarget + tradeRisk : activeTarget) : displayState == ARMED ? plannedTarget :
     candidateRisk > 0 ? candidateTrigger + candidateRisk * rewardMultiple : na
displayPlanRisk = displayState == LONG ? tradeRisk : displayState == ARMED ? plannedRisk : candidateRisk
displayInitialShares = displayState == LONG ? tradeInitialQty :
     displayState == ARMED ? plannedShares : candidateShares
displayHasThirdRung = useThirdRung and not na(displayInitialShares) and displayInitialShares >= 4
displayT1 = not na(displayEntry) and not na(displayPlanRisk) and displayPlanRisk > 0 ?
     f_firstTarget(displayEntry, displayPlanRisk) : na

// ── V12.17 §5 / Scenario D: does 2R actually FIT before the wall? ────────
// The playbook is explicit: "vérifier qu'un objectif d'au moins 2R tient
// avant la première résistance probable", and Scenario D fails a trade for
// exactly this -- price 5.20, daily 200 EMA 5.50, stop needing 0.20, so 2R
// cannot be reached before the barrier: PASS.
//
// Nothing in this script measured that. It sized the trade, drew T1/T2/T3
// and let the operator discover the wall afterwards. The nearest OVERHEAD
// obstacle is whichever of these sits above the entry and is closest:
// high of day, the daily 200 EMA, the pre-market high, and the nearest
// confirmed resistance the structure map already found.
f_lowerOf(float a, float b) => na(a) ? b : na(b) ? a : math.min(a, b)

float roomEntry = displayEntry
// V12.19: a candidate inside a daily window is NOT resistance. The lesson is
// explicit -- "do not skip across a newer gap/window to use an older minor
// level as if the newer structure did not exist" -- and the strong-chart
// checklist opens with "large gaps/windows create room". V12.17 took the
// nearest level unconditionally, so a stale price the market had already run
// through could be reported as the ceiling and understate the room.
//
// HOD is exempt: it is today's own high, made by live trading, so it is real
// structure even when it sits inside an older window.
float wallHOD   = not na(dayHigh)      and not na(roomEntry) and dayHigh      > roomEntry ? dayHigh      : na
float wall200   = not na(ma200v)       and not na(roomEntry) and ma200v       > roomEntry and not f_inWindow(ma200v)     ? ma200v     : na
float wallPM    = not na(pmHigh)       and not na(roomEntry) and pmHigh       > roomEntry and not f_inWindow(pmHigh)     ? pmHigh     : na
float wallPiv   = not na(nearestRes)   and not na(roomEntry) and nearestRes   > roomEntry and not f_inWindow(nearestRes) ? nearestRes : na
// The EDGES of a window are real levels -- the checklist names "gap-edge or
// window-edge resistance" -- even though its interior is empty.
// V12.23 -- BOTH edges, not just the far one. An empty zone has two
// boundaries and each is a real price: the NEAR edge is the last price that
// actually traded before the void, the FAR edge is the first price that
// traded on the other side. V12.19 registered only winTop/gapTop, so with
// price beneath a void spanning 10.21-11.47 it reported 11.47 as the next
// resistance and silently skipped 10.21 -- overstating the room by the whole
// width of the near boundary. The interior stays suppressed, which is the
// part that was already right: nothing traded in there, so there is no level
// in there.
float wallWinLo = not na(winBot) and not na(roomEntry) and winBot > roomEntry ? winBot : na
float wallWinHi = not na(winTop) and not na(roomEntry) and winTop > roomEntry ? winTop : na
float wallGapLo = not na(gapBot) and not na(roomEntry) and gapBot > roomEntry ? gapBot : na
float wallGapHi = not na(gapTop) and not na(roomEntry) and gapTop > roomEntry ? gapTop : na
float wallWinE  = f_lowerOf(wallWinLo, wallWinHi)
float wallGapE  = f_lowerOf(wallGapLo, wallGapHi)
float nearestWall = f_lowerOf(f_lowerOf(f_lowerOf(wallHOD, wall200), f_lowerOf(wallPM, wallPiv)),
     f_lowerOf(wallWinE, wallGapE))

string wallSrc = na(nearestWall) ? "" :
     nearestWall == wallHOD  ? "HOD" :
     nearestWall == wall200  ? "daily 200 EMA" :
     nearestWall == wallPM   ? "PM high" :
     nearestWall == wallWinLo ? "window near edge" :
     nearestWall == wallWinHi ? "window far edge" :
     nearestWall == wallGapLo ? "gap near edge" :
     nearestWall == wallGapHi ? "gap far edge" : "pivot"

// Overhead empty space, reported as the room it is.
bool windowAbove = (not na(winBot) and not na(roomEntry) and winBot >= roomEntry) or
     (not na(gapBot) and not na(roomEntry) and gapBot >= roomEntry)

// Reward available before the wall, expressed in R.
float roomR = not na(nearestWall) and not na(roomEntry) and not na(displayPlanRisk) and displayPlanRisk > 0 ?
     (nearestWall - roomEntry) / displayPlanRisk : na
// No wall overhead means open air, which is room, not a failure.
bool room2R = na(nearestWall) or na(roomR) or roomR >= rewardMultiple
// §5 also flags a daily 200 EMA sitting close overhead as problematic in its
// own right, independent of the R arithmetic.
bool ema200Overhead = not na(wall200) and not na(roomEntry) and
     wall200 - roomEntry <= ema200WarnDist
displayRunnerTarget = displayHasThirdRung and not na(displayEntry) and not na(displayPlanRisk) ?
     displayEntry + displayPlanRisk * (rewardMultiple + 1.0) : na
displayRR = displayState == ARMED or displayState == LONG ? plannedRRtoPeak : candidateRRtoPeak
// V8 (re-audit F16 residual): in a trade, show the ACTUAL remaining
// position (half after T1), not the original full share count.
displayShares = displayState == LONG ? strategy.position_size :
     displayState == ARMED ? plannedShares : candidateShares
displayRiskDollar = displayState == LONG ? (t1Filled ? 0.0 : tradeRisk) :
     displayState == ARMED ? plannedRisk : candidateRisk
displayRiskCash = not na(displayShares) and not na(displayRiskDollar) ? displayShares * displayRiskDollar : na
// V8 (re-audit F14 residual): structural risk AND slippage-stressed risk,
// side by side — the stressed figure is what the modelled worst case loses.
displayStressCash = not na(displayShares) and not na(displayRiskDollar) ?
     displayShares * (displayRiskDollar + slipPerShare) : na

// V4.8: room to the prior high is a RED FLAG, not a quiet number.
// TRUG 2026-08-17 armed a trigger 4 cents under the impulse peak with a
// 5-cent stop — 0.4R of room — and the dashboard rendered that in silver
// next to the share count. A warning nobody can see is not a warning.
// V4.10: measured against the NEAREST obstacle, not always the impulse peak.
// A setup whose trigger already sits above the impulse peak still has the
// day's high overhead; before this, that case reported the peak's room and
// read as clear.
thinRoom = not na(nextObstacleR) and nextObstacleR < 1.0 and
     (displayState == PULLBACK or displayState == ARMED)
roomWarn = thinRoom ? "⚠ ONLY " + f_rr(nextObstacleR) + " TO " +
     (candidateTrigger < pushPeak ? "PRIOR HIGH" : "HIGH OF DAY") + " — " : ""
// V4.10: a first pullback under a LOWER high is a different trade from one
// making new highs. Named, not silently averaged in with the good case.
lowerHighTag = not peakIsHOD and not na(dayHigh) and
     (displayState == PULLBACK or displayState == ARMED) ?
     "  · LOWER HIGH (HOD " + str.tostring(dayHigh, format.mintick) + ")" : ""

stateColor =
     displayState == LONG ? color.lime :
     displayState == ARMED ? (thinRoom ? color.orange : color.yellow) :
     displayState == INVALID ? color.red :
     displayState == PULLBACK or displayState == IMPULSE ? color.orange :
     color.gray

momentumText = (macdBullish ? "MACD✓" : "MACD✕") + " " +
     (emaBullish ? "EMA✓" : "EMA✕") + " " +
     (not vwapKnown ? "VWAP n/a" : vwapBullish ? "VWAP✓" : "VWAP✕")

// V4.4: a verdict at EVERY moment — never a blank "wait". Outside a
// structured setup the chart gates still say yes/no continuously.
chartVerdict = macdBullish and emaBullish and vwapBullish ? "chart healthy" :
     "not yet — " + (not vwapKnown ? "VWAP not started (RTH anchor)" :
     not vwapBullish ? "price below VWAP " + str.tostring(vwapValue, format.mintick) :
     not emaBullish ? "price below EMA9 " + str.tostring(ema9, format.mintick) : "MACD not positive")
// V8.1 (V7.4 operator directive): windowTag retired from the verdict —
// the clock lives on the TREND row and the PLAN tag.
// V4.7: provisional reads are labelled. A verdict that can still flip
// before the close must say so — the design pack's fail-closed rule.
// V8 (re-audit F17 residual): with liveEval OFF the forming bar previously
// showed NO tag at all — provisional-looking reads with no marker. Now both
// modes name themselves on the forming bar. (Full confirmed-snapshot mode
// stays deliberately unbuilt — freezing the display while orders stay live
// would manufacture a new display-vs-reality split; see AUDIT-RESPONSE-V6.)
liveTag = not barstate.isconfirmed ?
     (liveEval ? " · LIVE display; orders wait for close" :
          " · LIVE indicators; forming-low extension off") : ""
// V5.3: verdict compressed by operator request — one glance, not a sentence.
// Nothing vanished: levels moved to the PLAN row, the lower high to the HOD
// row, gate failures to the GATES row.
// V6 (finding 18d): with no impulse, peakIsHOD is vacuously false and the
// display called EVERY quiet moment a lower high. Comparison needs a peak.
hodComparable = not na(pushPeak) and not na(dayHigh)
shortLH = hodComparable and not peakIsHOD and
     (displayState == PULLBACK or displayState == ARMED) ? " · LH" : ""
// V6 (finding 18a): every state gets an explicit branch — INVALID used to
// fall through to chartVerdict and print "CHART OK" beside a red NO header.
// V6 (finding 17): the LIVE tag is appended again — it was computed and
// dropped in the V5.3 compression, so provisional reads looked final.
// V8: branches read the EFFECTIVE state; a pending-cancel bar shows the
// rejection, not the rolled-back ARMED plan (statusReason itself rolled
// back, so the cancelledPending text is explicit).
// V9 (defect 4): four verbs, one always present — BUY / WAIT / NO / MANAGE.
// onlyClockBlocks is computed from the gate BOOLEANS, never from the
// gateReason display string (design rule: display strings key nothing).
bool onlyClockBlocks = pushGate and pullbackCountGate and retracementGate and
     volumeGate and momentumGate and riskGate and rrGate and scanGate and
     confluenceGate and pullbackIndexGate and v11RiskGovernorOK and
     not (sessionGate and venueGate and entryTimeOK)
// V11: a locked account that displays nothing is the zombie-display defect
// V9 already fixed once. §8 stopping the day is the rule WORKING, and the
// operator has to be able to see that it is why nothing is arming — so the
// lock outranks every other verb except the ones about the chart itself.
// Empty string rather than na: a ternary whose branches are a string and na
// is a type-inference trap in Pine, and "" tests the same way here.
string v11LockLine = useRiskGovernor and v11Locked ?
     "NO — §8 " + v11LockReason + ", account stopped" +
          (v11AcctLocked ? " (walkaway — survives the session)" : " today") :
     useRiskGovernor and v11DayTrades >= maxTradesPerDay ?
          "NO — §8 daily trade cap reached (" + str.tostring(v11DayTrades) + ")" : ""

// V12.1 (operator: "the verdict is way longer than it should be"). One verb
// and a short reason — the operator needs to read it in a glance mid-session,
// not parse a sentence. The provenance clauses (live-vs-confirmed, playbook
// warning, room warning) are diagnostics: they move behind the full-dashboard
// toggle instead of riding on every verdict. Nothing is deleted, only demoted.
// V12.29 (operator): the verdict row carries the VERDICT. "refuse normally"
// and the pattern names were bloating it -- the PATTERN row is intended for
// exactly that, so alignment, the big-bar warning and the pattern names all
// live there now.
string verdictTail = dashFull ? liveTag : ""
string roomShort = dashFull ? roomWarn : ""

actionText =
     (not isOneMinute ? "1-MIN CHART ONLY" :
     not supportedMarket ? "NO · unsupported symbol" :
     v11LockLine != "" and displayState != LONG ? v11LockLine :
     displayState == LONG ? "MANAGE · " + f_n(mfeR, "#.0") + "R · stop " +
          f_px(t1Filled ? tradeEntryPrice : structuralStop) :
     displayState == ARMED ? roomShort + "BUY >" + f_px(triggerPrice) + " · working" :
     displayState == PULLBACK ? (hardGatesOK ?
          roomShort + "BUY >" + f_px(candidateTrigger) + " · at close" :
          onlyClockBlocks ? "WAIT · window shut" :
               "WAIT · " + gateReason) :
     displayState == IMPULSE ? "WAIT · dip not started" :
     displayState == INVALID ? (cancelledPending ?
          "NO · stopped before entry" :
          "NO · " + str.replace(statusReason, "Rejected — ", "")) :
     displayState == DONE ? "NO · trade over" :
     "WAIT · " + chartVerdict) + verdictTail

// ───────────────────────── Minimal chart ─────────────────────────
activeStructure = displayState == PULLBACK or displayState == ARMED or displayState == LONG

plot(showLevels and showContextPlots and activeStructure ? pushPeak : na, "Impulse peak", color=color.fuchsia, linewidth=1, style=plot.style_linebr, display = display.pane)
// V4.10: the day's high drawn as the obstacle it is. Dotted so it never reads
// as an entry/stop/target level — green and red stay reserved for TP and SL.
plot(showLevels and showContextPlots and not na(dayHigh) ? dayHigh : na, "High of day", color=color.new(color.fuchsia, 45), linewidth=1, style=plot.style_circles, display = display.pane)
plot(showLevels and showContextPlots and not na(pmHigh) and pmHigh != dayHigh ? pmHigh : na, "Pre-market high", color=color.new(color.teal, 40), linewidth=1, style=plot.style_circles, display = display.pane)
// V5: the BROKEN high — the level a retest is testing. Drawn only while a
// retest is live, so it does not clutter a normal pullback chart.
// V8 (re-audit ND-10): the frozen level plot keys on the SETUP'S frozen copy
// (setupRetestLevel), not the mutable global episode — which V8 now clears
// on consumption, so the old condition would have hidden the level exactly
// while the retest trade is live.
plot(showLevels and enableRetest and not na(setupRetestLevel) and
     (displayState == PULLBACK or displayState == ARMED) and setupKind == KIND_RETEST
     ? setupRetestLevel : na, "Broken HOD (retest level)",
     color=color.new(color.aqua, 20), linewidth=2, style=plot.style_linebr, display = display.pane)
plot(showLevels and activeStructure ? displayEntry : na, "Entry", color=color.yellow, linewidth=2, style=plot.style_linebr, display = display.pane)
// V4.9: half-width follows the instrument's own volatility so the band
// keeps the same visual weight whatever the price scale.
bandHalfWidth = bandMode == "Fixed ticks" ? bandHalfWidthTicks * syminfo.mintick :
     math.max(atr * bandATRfrac, syminfo.mintick)
// V4.1: candidate stop/target bands visible from the PULLBACK stage, not
// only once armed — the level should be on screen while you decide.
showTradeLevels = activeStructure
plot(showLevels and showTradeLevels ? displayStop : na, "Stop", color=color.red, linewidth=2, style=plot.style_linebr, display = display.pane)
stopBandUpperPlot = plot(showPriceBands and showTradeLevels ? displayStop + bandHalfWidth : na, "Stop band upper", color=color.new(color.red, 100), linewidth=1, style=plot.style_linebr, display = display.pane)
stopBandLowerPlot = plot(showPriceBands and showTradeLevels ? displayStop - bandHalfWidth : na, "Stop band lower", color=color.new(color.red, 100), linewidth=1, style=plot.style_linebr, display = display.pane)
fill(stopBandUpperPlot, stopBandLowerPlot, color=color.new(color.red, 80), title="Stop loss band (SL)")
plot(showLevels and showTradeLevels and not t1Filled ? displayT1 : na, "T1 (1R)", color=color.aqua, linewidth=1, style=plot.style_linebr, display = display.pane)
plot(showLevels and showTradeLevels ? displayTarget : na, "T2 / target", color=color.lime, linewidth=2, style=plot.style_linebr, display = display.pane)
plot(showLevels and showTradeLevels and displayHasThirdRung ? displayRunnerTarget : na,
     "Runner target", color=color.new(color.lime, 25), linewidth=1, style=plot.style_circles, display = display.pane)
targetBandUpperPlot = plot(showPriceBands and showTradeLevels ? displayTarget + bandHalfWidth : na, "Target band upper", color=color.new(color.lime, 100), linewidth=1, style=plot.style_linebr, display = display.pane)
targetBandLowerPlot = plot(showPriceBands and showTradeLevels ? displayTarget - bandHalfWidth : na, "Target band lower", color=color.new(color.lime, 100), linewidth=1, style=plot.style_linebr, display = display.pane)
fill(targetBandUpperPlot, targetBandLowerPlot, color=color.new(color.lime, 80), title="Target price band (TP)")

// V4.2: nearest structural levels as CLEAN bands — one box per level,
// anchored a few bars back and extended right. No historical trail (the
// stepped plot ribbons looked like debris across the chart).
// V7.1 (operator): the chart must read as a MAP even with no signal — the
// key levels traced, not just the single nearest band. Up to 3 resistances
// above and 3 supports below from confirmed pivots, deduplicated within an
// ATR-fraction so a cluster prints one line, plus the prior-day close.
// ═══════════════ V12.11 STRUCTURE MAP — RESTORED FROM V9 ═════════════════
// The operator: "go back to V8 or V9; figure out how you did manage these
// indicators in the chart". Correct instruction. Below this comment is the
// V9.6 structure block, restored verbatim from ross_fp_v11.pine (V11 is
// V9.12 merged with the V10 fixes, so this IS the V9 code).
//
// WHAT I BROKE, AND WHY IT KEPT GETTING WORSE.
//
// V9 draws a level with extend=extend.both — a horizontal rule across the
// WHOLE chart, past and future. In V12.4 I called that a bug ("a line
// extending into empty margin") and replaced it with finite segments. It was
// not a bug, it was the point: a level is a price that matters everywhere,
// so it has to be visible wherever you have scrolled. My finite segments
// only spanned from the level's origin bar to a few bars right of now, which
// is why the operator kept reporting levels that "make no sense" and lines
// that seemed detached from the candles.
//
// V9 also draws TWO levels each side (R1/R2, S1/S2), deduplicated within
// half an ATR so a cluster prints once, plus the prior-day close dashed. I
// had narrowed that to a single level per side behind an ATR reach cap that
// could — and on DAIC did — suppress everything, producing "no support
// neither resistance".
//
// And V9 builds its trend line as a TANGENT: from each candidate anchor it
// takes the MINIMUM slope to any later low, which is the line that cannot cut
// through the lows, then keeps it only if at least two lows touch it. My
// V12.10 required two confirmed ta.pivotlow pivots, which in a tight range
// never confirm — so no trend line was drawn at all.
//
// Three separate regressions, each from me generalising one real defect into
// a rule that discarded working code. Restored as it was.

// V4.2: nearest structural levels as CLEAN bands — one box per level,
// anchored a few bars back and extended right. No historical trail (the
// stepped plot ribbons looked like debris across the chart).
// V7.1 (operator): the chart must read as a MAP even with no signal — the
// key levels traced, not just the single nearest band. Up to 3 resistances
// above and 3 supports below from confirmed pivots, deduplicated within an
// ATR-fraction so a cluster prints one line, plus the prior-day close.
maxSRlines = input.int(3, "S/R levels each side [V12.21: 3, ranked by touches]", minval=1, maxval=6, group=gVisual)
// V12.13 (operator: levels "overlapped in the graph"): every label used to
// print at bar_index + 2, so two levels a few cents apart landed on the same
// pixel row and their texts collided. Each label now gets its own x slot.
srLabelStagger = input.int(4, "Bars between S/R label columns", minval=0, maxval=20, group=gVisual, display = display.none)
srBothPolarities = input.bool(false, "S/R: let any pivot be either role (V9.5) — off = V8 highs/lows", group=gVisual, display = display.none)
// V12.12 (operator, live DAIC +500%): V9 scores a trend line by
// touches*2 - distance, so distance can always be outvoted by touch count.
// On DAIC the winner was anchored on the session low at 2.05 while price was
// 3.66 — 1.6 dollars of empty space below the candles. Two costs: the line
// describes nothing tradeable, and because TradingView auto-scales the pane
// to fit every drawing, it dragged the axis down to 1.20 and squashed the
// candles into the top half of the chart. A hard ceiling, not a score term.
// V12.14: 3.0 ATR was too tight and suppressed legitimate lines. On VNRX
// (ATR ~0.01) a downtrend line projecting 0.02-0.04 above a 0.68 price is
// 2-4 ATR away -- and that is precisely the line a breakout has to break, so
// it must be drawn. 6.0 still rejects DAIC's session-low tangent at 8.94 ATR.
maxTLdistATR = input.float(6.0, "Hide a trend line further than N ATR from price", minval=0.5, maxval=20.0, group=gVisual, display = display.none)
// V12.14 (operator: "levels are still overlapped"). The band boxes below
// print their own "R <price>" from nearestRes, which is computed from allPiv
// in a different block and never deduplicated against the R1/R2 lines. On
// VNRX that produced R1 0.7146 and R 0.7097 -- 0.0049 apart, inside the
// half-ATR dedup tolerance, i.e. the same level drawn twice with two labels
// on top of each other. The first drawn level of each side is remembered so
// the box can skip itself when it would only restate it.
var float srR1 = na
var float srS1 = na
var array<line> srLines = array.new_line()
var array<label> srLabels = array.new_label()
// V9.4: S/R back on the DECISION layer — hiding the key levels behind
// the diagnostics toggle was over-cleaning (operator, live MMA).
// V12.22: level STRENGTH = the volume that changed hands at that price.
//
// Counting touches was already better than counting nearness, but a touch is
// a touch whether 200 shares or 200,000 traded there -- and the reason a
// level matters at all is that ORDERS CLUSTER THERE ("half dollars and whole
// dollars are psychological levels because orders cluster there", ch.5). What
// clusters is volume, not visits. A shelf tested twice on the day's heaviest
// bars is a wall; one brushed six times on 300-share bars is noise.
//
// Returns both, so the count can still break ties and be displayed.
f_levelStrength(float lvl, float tol) =>
    int   n = 0
    float v = 0.0
    if array.size(tlBars) > 0
        for k = 0 to array.size(tlBars) - 1
            if math.abs(array.get(tlHighs, k) - lvl) <= tol or
                 math.abs(array.get(tlLows, k) - lvl) <= tol
                n += 1
                v += nz(array.get(tlVols, k), 0.0)
    [n, v]

f_near(array<float> src, bool above_, int n_, float tol) =>
    array<float> out = array.new_float()
    if array.size(src) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(src) - 1
            float v = array.get(src, i)
            if (above_ ? v > close : v < close)
                bool dup = false
                if array.size(out) > 0
                    for j = 0 to array.size(out) - 1
                        if math.abs(array.get(out, j) - v) <= tol
                            dup := true
                if not dup
                    array.push(out, v)
    // V12.21: rank by STRENGTH, then proximity.
    //
    // Until now this sorted purely by price and kept the n NEAREST levels.
    // Nearest is not strongest, and the course is explicit that it is touches
    // that make a level credible: "more touches make them more credible"
    // (ch.5), with `touch_count = 3` in the corpus parameters -- 23 of 41
    // explicit counts say "the third touch". A level price has tested three
    // times outranks a closer one it has brushed once.
    array<float> ranked = array.new_float()
    while array.size(out) > 0 and array.size(ranked) < n_
        int   bestI = 0
        float bestV = -1.0
        float bestD = 1e12
        for i = 0 to array.size(out) - 1
            float v = array.get(out, i)
            [tn, tv] = f_levelStrength(v, tol)
            float dist = math.abs(v - close)
            if tv > bestV or (tv == bestV and dist < bestD)
                bestV := tv
                bestD := dist
                bestI := i
        array.push(ranked, array.get(out, bestI))
        array.remove(out, bestI)
    // draw nearest-first so R1 is always the one price meets next
    array.sort(ranked, above_ ? order.ascending : order.descending)
    ranked
if barstate.islast and showSR
    while array.size(srLines) > 0
        line.delete(array.pop(srLines))
    while array.size(srLabels) > 0
        label.delete(array.pop(srLabels))
    float tolSR = atr * 0.5
    // V9.5: both pivot kinds feed both sides (polarity flip) — f_near's
    // above/below filter assigns the role from the CURRENT price.
    // V12.13 POLARITY. V8 sourced resistance from pivot HIGHS and support
    // from pivot LOWS. V9.5 pointed both at allPiv so any pivot could play
    // either role ("a level is a level"), which doubles the candidate pool
    // and lets a pivot LOW be drawn as resistance above price. That is more
    // lines and less meaning, and it is one of the things that changed
    // between the version the operator liked and the ones he did not.
    // Default is the V8 behaviour; srBothPolarities restores V9.5.
    array<float> resSrc = srBothPolarities ? allPiv : pivHighs
    array<float> supSrc = srBothPolarities ? allPiv : pivLows
    array<float> resL = f_near(resSrc, true, maxSRlines, tolSR)
    array<float> supL = f_near(supSrc, false, maxSRlines, tolSR)
    srR1 := array.size(resL) > 0 ? array.get(resL, 0) : na
    srS1 := array.size(supL) > 0 ? array.get(supL, 0) : na
    if array.size(resL) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(resL) - 1
            float v = array.get(resL, i)
            array.push(srLines, line.new(bar_index - 1, v, bar_index, v,
                 extend=extend.both, color=color.new(color.blue, i == 0 ? 30 : 60),
                 width=i == 0 ? 2 : 1))
            array.push(srLabels, label.new(bar_index + 2 + i * srLabelStagger, v,
                 "R" + str.tostring(i + 1) + " " + str.tostring(v, format.mintick),
                 style=label.style_none, textcolor=color.new(color.blue, 20), size=size.small))
    if array.size(supL) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(supL) - 1
            float v = array.get(supL, i)
            array.push(srLines, line.new(bar_index - 1, v, bar_index, v,
                 extend=extend.both, color=color.new(color.purple, i == 0 ? 30 : 60),
                 width=i == 0 ? 2 : 1))
            array.push(srLabels, label.new(bar_index + 2 + i * srLabelStagger, v,
                 "S" + str.tostring(i + 1) + " " + str.tostring(v, format.mintick),
                 style=label.style_none, textcolor=color.new(color.purple, 20), size=size.small))
    if not na(prevDayClose)
        array.push(srLines, line.new(bar_index - 1, prevDayClose, bar_index, prevDayClose,
             extend=extend.both, color=color.new(color.gray, 40), style=line.style_dashed))
        array.push(srLabels, label.new(bar_index + 2 + maxSRlines * srLabelStagger, prevDayClose,
             "prev close " + str.tostring(prevDayClose, format.mintick),
             style=label.style_none, textcolor=color.new(color.gray, 20), size=size.small))

// ── V12.27: the flat top drawn where it is, in its own colour so it is not
// mistaken for an R-level. Labels only; nothing here gates a trade.
var line  ftLine = na
var label ftLab  = na
if barstate.islast
    if not na(ftLine)
        line.delete(ftLine)
        ftLine := na
    if not na(ftLab)
        label.delete(ftLab)
        ftLab := na
    if showPatterns and showSR and not na(flatTopPx)
        ftLine := line.new(bar_index - 1, flatTopPx, bar_index, flatTopPx,
             extend=extend.both, style=line.style_dotted, width=2,
             color=color.new(flatTopBroken ? color.lime : color.orange, 30))
        ftLab := label.new(bar_index + 2 + maxSRlines * srLabelStagger + srLabelStagger, flatTopPx,
             (flatTopBroken ? "FLAT TOP BROKEN " : "FLAT TOP ") +
             str.tostring(flatTopN) + "x " + str.tostring(flatTopPx, format.mintick),
             style=label.style_none, size=size.small,
             textcolor=color.new(flatTopBroken ? color.lime : color.orange, 10))

var box resBox = na
var box supBox = na
if barstate.islast and showSR
    if not na(resBox)
        box.delete(resBox)
    if not na(supBox)
        box.delete(supBox)
    // 0.75 ATR, deliberately WIDER than the 0.5 ATR line-dedup tolerance.
    // At exactly 0.5 the VNRX pair (0.7097 vs 0.7146, gap 0.0049, tol 0.0050)
    // was suppressed by one ten-thousandth -- true but not something to
    // depend on. Any level the line dedup let through is >0.5 ATR from its
    // neighbour, so a wider box tolerance cannot hide a distinct level.
    float boxTol = atr * 0.75
    if not na(nearestRes) and (na(srR1) or math.abs(nearestRes - srR1) > boxTol)
        // V4.9: extend.both — a 30-bar anchor slid out of view on any
        // horizontal zoom; the level exists across the whole chart.
        resBox := box.new(bar_index - 1, nearestRes + bandHalfWidth,
             bar_index, nearestRes - bandHalfWidth,
             border_color=color.new(color.gray, 55), border_width=1,
             bgcolor=color.new(color.blue, 88), extend=extend.both,
             text="R " + str.tostring(nearestRes, format.mintick),
             text_color=color.new(color.blue, 20), text_size=size.tiny,
             text_halign=text.align_left)
    if not na(nearestSup) and (na(srS1) or math.abs(nearestSup - srS1) > boxTol)
        supBox := box.new(bar_index - 1, nearestSup + bandHalfWidth,
             bar_index, nearestSup - bandHalfWidth,
             border_color=color.new(color.gray, 55), border_width=1,
             bgcolor=color.new(color.purple, 88), extend=extend.both,
             text="S " + str.tostring(nearestSup, format.mintick),
             text_color=color.new(color.purple, 20), text_size=size.tiny,
             text_halign=text.align_left)

// ── V9.6 TREND LINES (operator) ─────────────────────────────────────────
// Downtrend line: anchored at the HIGHEST pivot high in the window, drawn
// through the most recent LOWER pivot high after it — the line a breakout
// has to break. Uptrend line: the mirror on pivot lows — the line whose
// loss ends the trend. Both extend right; the label names the line and
// flips to BROKEN the moment the close is through it, so breakouts and
// trend failures read off the chart without measuring anything.
var line dnTL = na
var line upTL = na
var line     dnTL2  = na
var line     upTL2  = na
var linefill dnFill = na
var linefill upFill = na
var label dnTLlab = na
var label upTLlab = na
if barstate.islast and showTrendLine
    if not na(dnFill)
        linefill.delete(dnFill)
        dnFill := na
    if not na(upFill)
        linefill.delete(upFill)
        upFill := na
    if not na(dnTL)
        line.delete(dnTL)
        dnTL := na
    if not na(upTL)
        line.delete(upTL)
        upTL := na
    if not na(dnTL2)
        line.delete(dnTL2)
        dnTL2 := na
    if not na(upTL2)
        line.delete(upTL2)
        upTL2 := na
    if not na(dnTLlab)
        label.delete(dnTLlab)
        dnTLlab := na
    if not na(upTLlab)
        label.delete(upTLlab)
        upTLlab := na
    // V9.10 TREND LINES — tangent geometry (V9.8) + SCORED ANCHORS.
    // Live SDOT: on a name that doubled intraday, the tangent from the
    // session low sat $5 under price — correct geometry describing a leg
    // that ended hours ago. A trend line is only useful if it describes
    // the CURRENT leg, so every candidate swing anchor is now scored and
    // the best line wins:
    //   touches  bars whose low sits ON the line (within 0.2 ATR) — a
    //            line with 4 touches is real structure, 2 is a guess
    //   distance how far the projected line sits from price, in ATR —
    //            a line 10 ATR away cannot be broken, so it says nothing
    //   score    touches * 2 - distance   (structure first, then relevance)
    // The winner is still a TANGENT from its anchor: it can touch price
    // and never cut it, so only LIVE price breaks it. No candidate with
    // >= 2 touches and a valid slope = no line, honestly.
    int nB = array.size(tlBars)
    // V12.15: was a hard 20-bar minimum, with anchors additionally kept nine
    // bars off the right edge. On PPCB, which began printing at 12:33, the
    // chart held about 17 bars at 12:49 and no trend line could exist -- while
    // the first 15-30 minutes is exactly when this strategy trades. Both
    // bounds are inputs now: 12 bars minimum, anchors allowed to within 4 bars
    // of the right edge, so a swing formed minutes ago can still anchor.
    if nB >= tlMinBars
        int fromB = tlLookback > 0 ? math.max(0, nB - tlLookback) : 0
        float tolTL = math.max(atr * 0.20, syminfo.mintick)
        // ── uptrend: candidate anchors = local lows + the session low ──
        array.clear(tlCand)
        for i = fromB + 2 to nB - tlAnchorGap
            bool isMin = true
            for j = math.max(fromB, i - 2) to math.min(nB - 1, i + 2)
                if array.get(tlLows, j) < array.get(tlLows, i)
                    isMin := false
            if isMin
                array.push(tlCand, i)
        while array.size(tlCand) > 10
            array.shift(tlCand)
        int dayLoI = fromB
        for i = fromB + 1 to nB - tlAnchorGap
            if array.get(tlLows, i) < array.get(tlLows, dayLoI)
                dayLoI := i
        array.push(tlCand, dayLoI)
        float bestScore = na
        int bestA = -1
        float bestSlope = na
        int bestTouch = -1
        if array.size(tlCand) > 0
            for ci = 0 to array.size(tlCand) - 1
                int a = array.get(tlCand, ci)
                int barA = array.get(tlBars, a)
                float lowA = array.get(tlLows, a)
                float sl = na
                int tch = -1
                for k = a + 2 to nB - 1
                    float s = (array.get(tlLows, k) - lowA) / (array.get(tlBars, k) - barA)
                    if na(sl) or s < sl
                        sl := s
                        tch := k
                if not na(sl) and sl >= 0 and tch > 0
                    int touches = 1
                    for k = a + 2 to nB - 1
                        float lineK = lowA + sl * (array.get(tlBars, k) - barA)
                        if math.abs(array.get(tlLows, k) - lineK) <= tolTL
                            touches += 1
                    float lineNow = lowA + sl * (bar_index - barA)
                    float distATR = f_safeDiv(close - lineNow, atr, 99.0)
                    float score = touches * 2.0 - math.min(math.max(distATR, 0.0), 20.0)
                    if touches >= 2 and distATR <= maxTLdistATR and (na(bestScore) or score > bestScore)
                        bestScore := score
                        bestA := a
                        bestSlope := sl
                        bestTouch := tch
        if bestA >= 0
            float lowA2 = array.get(tlLows, bestA)
            float upNow = lowA2 + bestSlope * (bar_index - array.get(tlBars, bestA))
            bool upLost = close < upNow
            // V12.19b GUARD 1 -- a flat line is not a trend. On AEHL the
            // uptrend anchored on pre-market chop at 5.88 with almost no
            // slope and ran the full chart width. That is a horizontal
            // support level, and S1/S2 already draw those. Tested BEFORE the
            // line is created, so a flat fit produces no drawing at all.
            // Measured over the FITTED span (anchor -> touch), not anchor ->
            // now. Travel to the current bar grows with elapsed time, so a
            // near-flat premarket line accumulates enough of it to pass after
            // a few hours -- which is how AEHL's 5.88 line survived the first
            // version of this guard. The line is only evidenced across the
            // span its two anchors span.
            float upTravel = math.abs(bestSlope) *
     math.max(1, array.get(tlBars, bestTouch) - array.get(tlBars, bestA))
            bool  upSloped = not na(atr) and atr > 0 and upTravel >= atr * tlMinSlopeATR
            if upSloped
                upTL := line.new(array.get(tlTimes, bestA), lowA2,
                 array.get(tlTimes, bestTouch), array.get(tlLows, bestTouch),
                 xloc=xloc.bar_time, extend=extend.right,
                 color=color.new(color.teal, upLost ? 70 : 25),
                 style=upLost ? line.style_dashed : line.style_solid, width=2)
            // V12.15: the label used to print at `time`, on top of the last
            // candles. It now sits in the empty right margin at the price the
            // line actually holds there, so it reads as a continuation of the
            // line instead of covering price action.
            // ── the opposite rail ──────────────────────────────────────
            // Widest the HIGHS ever got above the fitted floor across the
            // same span. That excursion, applied as a parallel offset, is the
            // ceiling the move has actually respected — so floor and ceiling
            // together are the range this trend is travelling inside.
            float upWidth = 0.0
            for k = bestA to nB - 1
                float lk = lowA2 + bestSlope * (array.get(tlBars, k) - array.get(tlBars, bestA))
                float dv = array.get(tlHighs, k) - lk
                if dv > upWidth
                    upWidth := dv
            float upTop = upNow + upWidth
            // GUARD 2 -- the opposite rail is offset by the LARGEST
            // excursion, so across a vertical spike that excursion is the
            // spike itself. AEHL: 5.88 floor, 7.71 ceiling, 1.83 wide on a
            // $6.79 stock -- roughly 15 ATR. That is not a channel, it spans
            // a regime change. Above the cap the fitted rail stands alone.
            bool upChannelOK = not na(atr) and atr > 0 and upWidth <= atr * tlMaxWidthATR
            if showTrendChannel and upSloped and upWidth > 0 and upChannelOK
                upTL2 := line.new(array.get(tlTimes, bestA), lowA2 + upWidth,
                     array.get(tlTimes, bestTouch), array.get(tlLows, bestTouch) + upWidth,
                     xloc=xloc.bar_time, extend=extend.right,
                     color=color.new(color.teal, upLost ? 80 : 45),
                     style=line.style_dashed, width=1)
                if fillTrendChannel
                    upFill := linefill.new(upTL, upTL2, color.new(color.teal, 94))
            float upAt = lowA2 + bestSlope * (bar_index + tlLabelOffset - array.get(tlBars, bestA))
            string upTxt = (upLost ? "uptrend lost  " : "uptrend  ") +
                 str.tostring(upNow, format.mintick) +
                 (showTrendChannel and upSloped and upWidth > 0 and upChannelOK ?
                      "  –  " + str.tostring(upTop, format.mintick) : "")
            upTLlab := upSloped ? label.new(bar_index + tlLabelOffset, upAt,
                 upTxt,
                 xloc=xloc.bar_index, yloc=yloc.price, style=label.style_none, size=size.small,
                 textcolor=upLost ? color.new(color.orange, 0) : color.new(color.teal, 10)) : na
        // ── downtrend: mirror, candidates = local highs + the session high ──
        array.clear(tlCand)
        for i = fromB + 2 to nB - tlAnchorGap
            bool isMax = true
            for j = math.max(fromB, i - 2) to math.min(nB - 1, i + 2)
                if array.get(tlHighs, j) > array.get(tlHighs, i)
                    isMax := false
            if isMax
                array.push(tlCand, i)
        while array.size(tlCand) > 10
            array.shift(tlCand)
        int dayHiI = fromB
        for i = fromB + 1 to nB - tlAnchorGap
            if array.get(tlHighs, i) > array.get(tlHighs, dayHiI)
                dayHiI := i
        array.push(tlCand, dayHiI)
        float bestScoreD = na
        int bestAD = -1
        float bestSlopeD = na
        int bestTouchD = -1
        if array.size(tlCand) > 0
            for ci = 0 to array.size(tlCand) - 1
                int a = array.get(tlCand, ci)
                int barA = array.get(tlBars, a)
                float highA = array.get(tlHighs, a)
                float sl = na
                int tch = -1
                for k = a + 2 to nB - 1
                    float s = (array.get(tlHighs, k) - highA) / (array.get(tlBars, k) - barA)
                    if na(sl) or s > sl
                        sl := s
                        tch := k
                if not na(sl) and sl <= 0 and tch > 0
                    int touches = 1
                    for k = a + 2 to nB - 1
                        float lineK = highA + sl * (array.get(tlBars, k) - barA)
                        if math.abs(array.get(tlHighs, k) - lineK) <= tolTL
                            touches += 1
                    float lineNow = highA + sl * (bar_index - barA)
                    float distATR = f_safeDiv(lineNow - close, atr, 99.0)
                    float score = touches * 2.0 - math.min(math.max(distATR, 0.0), 20.0)
                    if touches >= 2 and distATR <= maxTLdistATR and (na(bestScoreD) or score > bestScoreD)
                        bestScoreD := score
                        bestAD := a
                        bestSlopeD := sl
                        bestTouchD := tch
        if bestAD >= 0
            float highA2 = array.get(tlHighs, bestAD)
            float dnNow = highA2 + bestSlopeD * (bar_index - array.get(tlBars, bestAD))
            bool dnBroken = close > dnNow
            float dnTravel = math.abs(bestSlopeD) *
     math.max(1, array.get(tlBars, bestTouchD) - array.get(tlBars, bestAD))
            bool  dnSloped = not na(atr) and atr > 0 and dnTravel >= atr * tlMinSlopeATR
            if dnSloped
                dnTL := line.new(array.get(tlTimes, bestAD), highA2,
                 array.get(tlTimes, bestTouchD), array.get(tlHighs, bestTouchD),
                 xloc=xloc.bar_time, extend=extend.right,
                 color=color.new(color.red, dnBroken ? 70 : 25),
                 style=dnBroken ? line.style_dashed : line.style_solid, width=2)
            // ── the opposite rail: deepest the LOWS fell below the ceiling ──
            float dnWidth = 0.0
            for k = bestAD to nB - 1
                float lk = highA2 + bestSlopeD * (array.get(tlBars, k) - array.get(tlBars, bestAD))
                float dv = lk - array.get(tlLows, k)
                if dv > dnWidth
                    dnWidth := dv
            float dnBot = dnNow - dnWidth
            bool dnChannelOK = not na(atr) and atr > 0 and dnWidth <= atr * tlMaxWidthATR
            if showTrendChannel and dnSloped and dnWidth > 0 and dnChannelOK
                dnTL2 := line.new(array.get(tlTimes, bestAD), highA2 - dnWidth,
                     array.get(tlTimes, bestTouchD), array.get(tlHighs, bestTouchD) - dnWidth,
                     xloc=xloc.bar_time, extend=extend.right,
                     color=color.new(color.red, dnBroken ? 80 : 45),
                     style=line.style_dashed, width=1)
                if fillTrendChannel
                    dnFill := linefill.new(dnTL, dnTL2, color.new(color.red, 94))
            float dnAt = highA2 + bestSlopeD * (bar_index + tlLabelOffset - array.get(tlBars, bestAD))
            string dnTxt = (dnBroken ? "downtrend broken  " : "downtrend  ") +
                 (showTrendChannel and dnSloped and dnWidth > 0 and dnChannelOK ?
                      str.tostring(dnBot, format.mintick) + "  –  " : "") +
                 str.tostring(dnNow, format.mintick)
            dnTLlab := dnSloped ? label.new(bar_index + tlLabelOffset, dnAt,
                 dnTxt,
                 xloc=xloc.bar_index, yloc=yloc.price, style=label.style_none, size=size.small,
                 textcolor=dnBroken ? color.new(color.lime, 0) : color.new(color.red, 10)) : na


// V5: retest triggers get their own glyph so the two setups are separable on
// the chart and, later, in the trade log.
// V12.1 (operator: markers "don't sync with the graph and remain unusable when
// zooming the price in or out, way above or below the candles").
//
// location.abovebar / location.belowbar offset the shape by a fraction of the
// VISIBLE PRICE RANGE, so the gap between marker and candle grows every time
// the price scale is zoomed out — at a wide zoom the marker ends up nowhere
// near the bar it describes. location.absolute pins the shape to a price, and
// the small clearance below is a fraction of ATR, which is denominated in
// price and therefore holds at any zoom.
markOffset = nz(atr, 0.0) * 0.15
mkArmed    = not na(triggerPrice) ? triggerPrice - markOffset : low - markOffset
mkEntry    = not na(tradeEntryPrice) ? tradeEntryPrice : close
mkReject   = high + markOffset
mkExit     = high + markOffset
mkGhost    = not na(ghostTrig) ? ghostTrig - markOffset : low - markOffset

// Marker visibility, split by size so each glyph has a tiny and a normal
// variant and only one of the pair is ever live. Declared HERE, immediately
// above the plotshape block that consumes them: V12.6 replaced a block that
// happened to end on these two lines and took them with it (CE10272,
// "Undeclared identifier sm"). Keeping a declaration adjacent to its only
// use is what stops a block edit from silently orphaning it again.
sm = showMarkers and not bigMarkers
lg = showMarkers and bigMarkers

plotshape(sm and eventArmed and setupKind == KIND_RETEST ? mkArmed : na, title="Trigger set (retest)", style=shape.diamond, location=location.absolute, color=color.aqua, size=size.tiny, text="SET")
plotshape(lg and eventArmed and setupKind == KIND_RETEST ? mkArmed : na, title="Trigger set (retest, large)", style=shape.diamond, location=location.absolute, color=color.aqua, size=size.normal, text="SET")
plotshape(sm and eventArmed and setupKind != KIND_RETEST ? mkArmed : na, title="Trigger set", style=shape.circle, location=location.absolute, color=color.yellow, size=size.tiny, text="SET")
plotshape(sm and eventLong ? mkEntry : na, title="Entry filled", style=shape.labelup, location=location.absolute, color=color.lime, textcolor=color.black, size=size.tiny, text="BUY")
plotshape(sm and eventInvalid ? mkReject : na, title="Setup rejected", style=shape.xcross, location=location.absolute, color=color.red, size=size.tiny, text="NO")
plotshape(sm and eventBailout ? mkExit : na, title="Bailout", style=shape.labeldown, location=location.absolute, color=color.orange, textcolor=color.black, size=size.tiny, text="EXIT")
plotshape(lg and eventArmed and setupKind != KIND_RETEST ? mkArmed : na, title="Trigger set (large)", style=shape.circle, location=location.absolute, color=color.yellow, size=size.normal, text="SET")
plotshape(lg and eventLong ? mkEntry : na, title="Entry filled (large)", style=shape.labelup, location=location.absolute, color=color.lime, textcolor=color.black, size=size.normal, text="BUY")
plotshape(lg and eventInvalid ? mkReject : na, title="Setup rejected (large)", style=shape.xcross, location=location.absolute, color=color.red, size=size.normal, text="NO")
plotshape(lg and eventBailout ? mkExit : na, title="Bailout (large)", style=shape.labeldown, location=location.absolute, color=color.orange, textcolor=color.black, size=size.normal, text="EXIT")
plotshape(sm and showDiagnostics and eventGhost ? mkGhost : na, title="Pattern seen, no order", style=shape.circle, location=location.absolute, color=color.new(color.gray, 30), size=size.tiny, text="SEEN")
plotshape(lg and showDiagnostics and eventGhost ? mkGhost : na, title="Pattern seen, no order (large)", style=shape.circle, location=location.absolute, color=color.new(color.gray, 30), size=size.normal, text="SEEN")

// ── V12.1 (operator: "in case of a trade I need to see directly in the graph
// the profit/loss in dollars so I can know if it's a winning trade").
//
// A live P&L tag riding the last bar of an open position, in dollars, green
// when ahead and red when behind. strategy.openprofit is already net of the
// modelled commission, so this is the same number the SOLD label prints when
// the position closes — not a gross figure that shrinks at the exit.
//
// One label, moved each bar rather than one per bar: labels are a capped
// resource and a per-bar trail would exhaust max_labels_count and start
// dropping the oldest markers.
var label livePnlLab = na
if showTradeResult and strategy.position_size > 0 and barstate.islast
    float openPnl = strategy.openprofit
    float openPct = f_safeDiv(openPnl, math.max(strategy.position_avg_price *
         strategy.position_size, 1.0), 0.0) * 100.0
    bool winning = openPnl >= 0
    if not na(livePnlLab)
        label.delete(livePnlLab)
    livePnlLab := label.new(time, close,
         (winning ? "▲ +$" : "▼ -$") + f_n(math.abs(openPnl), "#.##") +
         "  (" + (winning ? "+" : "") + f_n(openPct, "#.0") + "%)  " +
         f_n(strategy.position_size, "#") + " sh",
         xloc=xloc.bar_time, yloc=yloc.price, style=label.style_label_left,
         size=size.small, color=winning ? color.new(color.green, 10) : color.new(color.red, 10),
         textcolor=color.white)
if strategy.position_size == 0 and not na(livePnlLab)
    label.delete(livePnlLab)
    livePnlLab := na

// ───────────────────────── Dashboard ─────────────────────────
// V4.2: the original two-column layout (labels left, values right — the
// look that worked), sized down: tiny text, no borders, short strings,
// em dashes for absents. dashFull adds the three diagnostic rows.
LBL = color.rgb(28, 28, 30)
DSZ = dashSize == "tiny" ? size.tiny : dashSize == "normal" ? size.normal : size.small
// V9.2 (operator): ONE text size for every row — emphasis comes from the
// VERDICT row's state-coloured background and the green titles, not fonts.
// V7.2: INVALID/DONE verdicts age in candles, so a stale NO cannot read live.
int barsInState = na(stateStartBar) ? 0 : bar_index - stateStartBar
ageTag = barsInState <= 0 ? "" : " (" + str.tostring(barsInState) + (barsInState == 1 ? " candle ago" : " candles ago") + ")"
// V7.2 universe check. Computed at global scope: a ta.* call inside the
// islast branch would execute conditionally and return garbage.
// V8.2 (live CDTG/JZ 2026-08-20): liquidity is the BEST of the 5-bar burst,
// the 20-bar average and the day average $/min. The 20-bar-only measure
// called CDTG "too thin ($17.6k/min)" 40 minutes after it traded millions,
// and vetoed JZ MID-SQUEEZE because 15 of its last 20 bars were dead. The
// floor itself stays [UNTESTED local]; its job is filtering dead tape,
// never vetoing an active spike.
avgDollarVol20 = ta.sma(hlc3 * volume, 20)
avgDollarVol5 = ta.sma(hlc3 * volume, 5)
avgDollarVolDay = f_safeDiv(dayDollarCum, dayBarCount, na)
liquidPerMin = math.max(nz(avgDollarVol20, 0.0), math.max(nz(avgDollarVol5, 0.0), nz(avgDollarVolDay, 0.0)))
// V9.1 (operator, live BTCT 2026-08-20): the criteria GRID. Pine colours
// CELLS, so every criterion gets its own cell — a chip: green when met,
// orange when failed, slate with a · when not judgeable yet (V5.2 rule).
// A row whose judged chips are all green paints its TITLE green too.
// V9.2 (operator, live PCLA): ONE text size everywhere; the table holds
// EXACTLY the rows currently shown (it is rebuilt when the row set
// changes — a few times a day at most — so no blank rows ever render);
// PLAN loses its tag noise; SIZE says shares, $ position vs the account's
// real equity, and risk — nothing else.
var table dash = na
var int lastRowSig = -1
var bool dashMerged = false

CHIP_OK = color.rgb(8, 153, 129)
CHIP_NO = color.rgb(245, 124, 0)
CHIP_NA = color.rgb(42, 46, 57)

f_label(int r, string txt, bool allMet) =>
    table.cell(dash, 0, r, txt, bgcolor=allMet ? CHIP_OK : LBL,
         text_color=color.white, text_size=DSZ, text_halign=text.align_left)

f_text(int r, string value, color vcolor) =>
    table.cell(dash, 1, r, value, text_color=vcolor, text_size=DSZ,
         text_halign=text.align_left)

// one criterion, one cell: 1 met · 0 failed · -1 not judgeable yet
f_chip(int c, int r, string nm, int st) =>
    table.cell(dash, c, r, st == -1 ? nm + " ·" : nm,
         bgcolor=st == 1 ? CHIP_OK : st == 0 ? CHIP_NO : CHIP_NA,
         text_color=st == -1 ? color.new(color.silver, 30) : color.white,
         text_size=DSZ, text_halign=text.align_center)

f_b(bool ok) =>
    ok ? 1 : 0

if barstate.islast
    // ── row layout: fixed rows 0..7, optional rows packed after them ──
    // V9.3 (operator): HALT BAND and DASH LANE rows retired. The halt
    // band's one decision fact — an unenforceable stop — is a red warning
    // on SIZE when it fires; the lane row's one decision fact — his 2+
    // hits rule — is a chip on STOCK FIT. Everything else those rows
    // showed was reference, not decision.
    bool showFitRows = showScanPanel
    // V12.1: a permanent caveat does not need a permanent row. It reappears
    // the moment it carries live information — a non-zero ambiguity count —
    // which is the one case where it is a finding rather than boilerplate.
    bool showLimits = not dashCompact or dashFull or historicalFillAmbiguities > 0
    int rFit = showFitRows ? 8 : -1
    int nextRow = showFitRows ? 9 : 8
    int rVwap = dashFull ? nextRow : -1
    int rRS = dashFull ? nextRow + 1 : -1
    int rQual = dashFull ? nextRow + 2 : -1
    nextRow += dashFull ? 3 : 0
    int rLim = showLimits ? nextRow : -1
    nextRow += showLimits ? 1 : 0
    int rowSig = nextRow * 100 + (showFitRows ? 1 : 0) +
         (dashFull ? 4 : 0) + (showLimits ? 8 : 0) + (dashChips ? 16 : 0)
    if na(dash) or rowSig != lastRowSig
        if not na(dash)
            table.delete(dash)
        dash := table.new(position.bottom_right, 7, nextRow, border_width=2,
             border_color=color.rgb(15, 15, 17), frame_color=color.rgb(15, 15, 17), frame_width=2)
        lastRowSig := rowSig
        dashMerged := false

    f_label(0, "ROSS FP " + REV, false)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 0, isOneMinute ? f_stateName(displayState) +
         (displayState == PULLBACK or displayState == ARMED or displayState == LONG ?
              (setupKind == KIND_RETEST ? " · retest buy" :
               setupKind == KIND_FAST or setupKind == KIND_UPTREND ? " · quick buy" :
               " · dip buy") : "") : "WRONG TF",
         bgcolor=stateColor, text_color=color.black, text_size=DSZ, text_halign=text.align_center)

    // V8.2: the banner claims the row only when the machine is idle+flat.
    bool thinTape = liquidPerMin < minDollarVolume
    outOfUniverse = strategy.position_size == 0 and displayState == IDLE and
         (not pillarPrice or thinTape)

    // ── VERDICT: actionText IS the row (four verbs, always one).
    string vLine = outOfUniverse ?
         "NO — not a playbook stock: " + (not pillarPrice ?
              "price " + f_px(close) + " outside $" + f_n(scanMinPrice, "#") + "-" + f_n(scanMaxPrice, "#") :
              "volume thin (best $" + f_n(liquidPerMin, "#") + "/min)") :
         actionText +
              (displayState == INVALID or displayState == DONE ? ageTag : "") +
              (not pillarPrice or thinTape ? "  · ⚠ not a playbook stock" : "")
    color vCol = outOfUniverse ? color.gray :
         thinRoom ? color.red : displayState == ARMED ? color.yellow :
         displayState == LONG ? color.lime : color.white
    f_label(1, "VERDICT", hardGatesOK)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 1, vLine, text_color=vCol,
         bgcolor=color.new(stateColor, 82), text_size=DSZ, text_halign=text.align_left)

    // V11: when liquidity or cash — not risk — set the size, §7's 1-2% of
    // account is NOT what is being traded and §9's expectancy scales down
    // with it. Say which bound bit rather than printing a share count that
    // looks like the plan.
    // ── PLAN + SIZE: one live plan, always (V7.5 5-source chain).
    bool ghostFresh = not na(ghostTrig) and not na(ghostBar) and bar_index - ghostBar <= 10
    bool candLive = displayState == PULLBACK and not na(candidateTrigger) and
         candidateRisk > 0 and candidateShares >= 1
    int planSrc = displayState == LONG ? 5 : displayState == ARMED ? 4 :
         candLive ? 3 : ghostFresh ? 2 : 1
    float pEntry = planSrc == 5 ? tradeEntryPrice : planSrc == 4 ? triggerPrice :
         planSrc == 3 ? candidateTrigger : planSrc == 2 ? ghostTrig : close
    float pRisk = planSrc == 5 ? tradeRisk : planSrc == 4 ? plannedRisk :
         planSrc == 3 ? candidateRisk : planSrc == 2 ? ghostTrig - ghostStop : anyRisk
    float pStop = planSrc == 5 and t1Filled ? tradeEntryPrice :
         planSrc == 5 ? structuralStop : planSrc == 4 ? structuralStop :
         planSrc == 3 ? candidateStop : planSrc == 2 ? ghostStop : close - anyRisk
    float pT1 = pEntry + pRisk
    float pT2 = planSrc == 5 ? activeTarget : planSrc == 4 ? plannedTarget :
         planSrc == 2 ? ghostTgt : pEntry + pRisk * rewardMultiple
    float pT3 = pEntry + pRisk * (rewardMultiple + 1.0)
    float pShares = planSrc == 5 or planSrc == 4 ? displayShares :
         planSrc == 3 ? candidateShares : planSrc == 2 ? ghostShares : anyShares
    float pThirdBasis = planSrc == 5 ? tradeInitialQty : pShares
    bool pHasThirdRung = useThirdRung and not na(pThirdBasis) and pThirdBasis >= 4
    // V9.2: tags cut to two words — the row colour already carries state.
    string planTag = planSrc == 5 ?
         (t2Filled ? " · ¾ sold, stop@entry" : t1Filled ? " · ½ sold, stop@entry" : "") :
         planSrc == 4 ? " · working" +
              (useCappedStopLimit ? " · cap " + f_px(triggerPrice + entryCapTicks * syminfo.mintick) : "") :
         planSrc == 3 ? " · live" :
         planSrc == 2 ? " · no order (clock)" : ""
    color planCol = planSrc == 5 ? color.lime : planSrc == 4 ? color.yellow :
         planSrc == 3 ? color.white : color.gray
    string atrMark = planSrc >= 4 ? (plannedUsesATRStop ? "ᵃᵗʳ" : "") :
         (planSrc == 3 and usingATRstop ? "ᵃᵗʳ" : "")
    f_label(2, planSrc >= 4 ? "▶ PLAN" : "PLAN", planSrc >= 4)
    // V9.3 (operator): the three levels in bold capitals. Pine tables
    // have no bold — these are Unicode bold-sans capitals, which
    // TradingView renders.
    float pQtyBase = nz(pThirdBasis, 0.0)
    float pQtyT1 = pQtyBase >= 2 ? math.floor(pQtyBase / 2.0) : 0.0
    float pQtyT2 = pHasThirdRung ? math.floor(pQtyBase / 4.0) : 0.0
    float pQtyRunner = math.max(pQtyBase - pQtyT1 - pQtyT2, 0.0)
    // V12.1 (operator): name the rungs. "88@7.20" does not say which target
    // it is; T1/T2/T3 does, and the share count still rides with each one.
    string ladderText = (pQtyT1 > 0 ?
         "  T1 " + f_px(pT1) + " (" + f_n(pQtyT1, "#") + ")" : "") +
         (pQtyT2 > 0 ? "  T2 " + f_px(pT2) + " (" + f_n(pQtyT2, "#") + ")" : "") +
         (pQtyRunner > 0 ? "  T3 " + f_px(pHasThirdRung ? pT3 : pT2) +
              " (" + f_n(pQtyRunner, "#") + ")" : "")
    f_text(2, "𝗕𝗨𝗬 " + f_px(pEntry) + " · 𝗦𝗧𝗢𝗣 " + f_px(pStop) + atrMark +
         ladderText + planTag, planCol)

    // ── V9.2 SIZE: shares, $ position against the REAL equity base, risk.
    // The % is the POSITION's share of equity, labelled as such — the
    // sizing rule itself (2% risk, PARAMETERS.md §7) lives in the code.
    f_label(3, "SIZE", false)
    bool haltWarn = inRTH and stopExceedsHaltBand
    float pRiskToStop = math.max(pEntry - pStop, 0.0)
    float pAdversePerShare = planSrc == 5 ? pRiskToStop + exitAdversePerShare :
         pRisk + slipPerShare
    float pRemainingFees = planSrc == 5 ? commissionPerOrderInput *
         (pHasThirdRung ? (t2Filled ? 1.0 : t1Filled ? 2.0 : 3.0) :
              (t1Filled ? 1.0 : 2.0)) : commissionReserve
    float pModeledCashRisk = pShares * pAdversePerShare + pRemainingFees
    string pBound = planSrc == 5 or planSrc == 4 ? plannedSizeBoundBy :
         planSrc == 3 ? v11SizeBoundBy : planSrc == 2 ? "ghost" : "hypothetical"
    // V12.1 (operator): SIZE answers one question — how many shares and how
    // much money. The percent-of-equity figure read as a risk number and was
    // not one; modeled risk, the budget and the binding constraint moved to
    // the full dashboard where they are diagnostics, not the headline.
    f_text(3, f_n(pShares, "#") + " sh · $" + f_n(pShares * pEntry, "#") +
         (dashFull ? "  ·  risk $" + f_n(pModeledCashRisk, "#") + " / $" +
              f_n(riskBudget, "#") + " · " + pBound : "") +
         (haltWarn ? "  ⚠ stop wider than LULD heuristic " + f_px(haltBandWidth) : "") +
         (thinRoom and planSrc >= 3 ? "  ⚠ only " + f_rr(nextObstacleR) + " room above" : ""),
         haltWarn or (thinRoom and planSrc >= 3) ? color.red : planCol)

    // ── CLOCK (V9 defect 1): market phase chip + THIS strategy's window.
    string mktPhase = minuteET < 570 ? "PRE-MKT" : minuteET < 960 ? "OPEN" : "AFTER-HRS"
    // V9.12: with the gate off by default, "off" is no longer an alarm —
    // the row reports the phase and where we are versus the prime window,
    // and only flags the window when it is actually gating.
    bool inPrime = minuteET >= 7 * 60 and minuteET < 11 * 60 + 30
    bool clockOK = useSessionWindow ? (inSession and entryTimeOK) : true
    // V12.29 (operator: "instead of the clock windows, place the pattern").
    // The session phase keeps its one chip -- PRE-MKT / OPEN / AH is a fact
    // worth one cell -- but the long window sentence is gone: when the clock
    // actually blocks, the VERDICT already says "WAIT · window shut". The
    // remaining five cells carry what the operator asked to see: the pattern,
    // the 1m/5m alignment, and the oversized-5m-bar stop warning.
    string alignShort = alignState == "aligned" ? "1m+5m aligned" :
         alignState == "5m n/a"  ? "" :
         alignState == "1m weak" ? "5m ok, 1m weak" :
         alignState == "1m leads" ? "1m leads 5m" : "no timeframe constructive"
    string patCore = not showPatterns ? "" :
         (abcdBroken ? "ABCD broken" : abcdOK ? "ABCD forming" : "") +
         (flatTopBroken or not na(flatTopPx) ?
              ((abcdOK or abcdBroken) ? " · " : "") +
              (flatTopBroken ? "flat top BROKEN " + str.tostring(flatTopPx, format.mintick) :
                   "flat top " + str.tostring(flatTopN) + "x " + str.tostring(flatTopPx, format.mintick)) : "")
    string patLine = patCore +
         (patCore != "" and alignShort != "" ? " · " : "") + alignShort +
         (bigBar5 ? " · ⚠ huge 5m bar" : "")
    bool patGood = (abcdOK or abcdBroken or flatTopBroken) and alignState != "1m weak"
    f_label(4, "PATTERN", patGood)
    f_chip(1, 4, mktPhase, minuteET >= 570 and minuteET < 960 ? 1 : -1)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 4, patLine == "" ? "—" : patLine,
         text_color=patGood ? CHIP_OK : color.silver,
         text_size=DSZ, text_halign=text.align_left)

    // ── SETUP: is THIS dip tradeable. TREND: is the tape behind it.
    pbApplicable = setupState == PULLBACK or setupState == ARMED
    bool setupAll = pbApplicable and pushGate and pullbackCountGate and
         retracementGate and volumeGate and riskGate and confluenceGate and
         pullbackIndexGate
    f_label(5, "SETUP · PB#" + str.tostring(v11PbIndex), setupAll)
    // V12.22 (operator: "it's complicated to decrypt"). Every chip now says
    // what it MEASURES in plain words, and the two that are really counters
    // print the count against the requirement instead of a bare number.
    // V12.28: one plain judgment, naming the FIRST thing that is wrong --
    // which is the only thing that matters, since any one of them is fatal.
    string setupLine = not pbApplicable ?
          (pushGate ? "impulse seen — waiting for the dip to form" : "no impulse yet") :
     not pushGate            ? "impulse not strong enough" :
     not pullbackCountGate   ? "dip is the wrong length (needs " + str.tostring(minPullbackBars) +
          "-" + str.tostring(maxPullbackBars) + " candles)" :
     not retracementGate     ? "dip too deep or too shallow" :
     not volumeGate          ? "too much selling in the dip" :
     not riskGate            ? "stop too far — risk per share too large" :
     not confluenceGate      ? "only " + str.tostring(supportCount) + " of " +
          str.tostring(minConfluence) + " support reasons at the dip low" :
     not pullbackIndexGate   ? "pullback #" + str.tostring(v11PbIndex) + " — past the 1st/2nd" :
     "setup is clean"
    if not dashChips
        f_text(5, setupLine, setupAll ? CHIP_OK : pbApplicable ? CHIP_NO : color.silver)
    if dashChips
        f_chip(1, 5, "Impulse", f_b(pushGate))
        f_chip(2, 5, "Dip bars", pbApplicable ? f_b(pullbackCountGate) : -1)
        f_chip(3, 5, "Dip depth", pbApplicable ? f_b(retracementGate) : -1)
        f_chip(4, 5, "Dip vol", pbApplicable ? f_b(volumeGate) : -1)
        f_chip(5, 5, usingATRstop ? "Risk ATR" : "Risk", pbApplicable ? f_b(riskGate) : -1)
    // "Conf 0" was the least readable cell on the panel: a bare count with no
    // hint of the target. It now reads "Support 0/2" -- reasons found over
    // reasons required.
        f_chip(6, 5, "Support " + str.tostring(supportCount) + "/" + str.tostring(minConfluence),
         pbApplicable ? f_b(confluenceGate and pullbackIndexGate) : -1)

    bool trendAll = macdBullish and emaBullish and vwapBullish and rrGate and
         (not scanGates or scanGate) and v11RiskGovernorOK
    // V12.29 (operator: "restore the trend line where I had MACD, VWAP and
    // EMA — that was very important"). V12.28 spent this row on the pattern
    // sentence; the pattern lives on row 4 now and the trend chips are back
    // unconditionally. Day limits keeps its plain name (the §8 daily risk
    // governor: loss cap, trade cap, drawdown walkaway).
    f_label(6, "TREND", trendAll)
    f_chip(1, 6, "MACD", f_b(macdBullish))
    f_chip(2, 6, "EMA", f_b(emaBullish))
    f_chip(3, 6, "VWAP", vwapKnown ? f_b(vwapBullish) : -1)
    f_chip(4, 6, "Room", f_b(rrGate))
    f_chip(5, 6, "Scan fit", scanGates ? f_b(scanGate) : -1)
    f_chip(6, 6, "Day limits", f_b(v11RiskGovernorOK))

    // V9.2 (trading read, live PCLA: HOD 11.33 with price 7.99 and the row
    // said nothing): the DISTANCE off the high is the front-side/back-side
    // fact. >20% off the high = the move is over — the repo's own reject
    // language. Named, coloured, never silent.
    float pctOffHigh = not na(dayHigh) and dayHigh > 0 ?
         (dayHigh - close) / dayHigh * 100.0 : na
    bool backSide = not na(pctOffHigh) and pctOffHigh >= 20.0
    f_label(7, "HIGH OF DAY", hodComparable and peakIsHOD and not backSide)
    f_text(7, f_px(dayHigh) +
         (na(pctOffHigh) ? "" : backSide ?
              "  ⚠ BACK SIDE — " + f_n(pctOffHigh, "#") + "% off the high" :
              "  · " + f_n(pctOffHigh, "#") + "% off high") +
         (not hodComparable ? "" : peakIsHOD ? "  · this move IS the high" : "  ⚠ lower high") +
         (not na(candidateRRtoHOD) ? "  · " + f_rr(candidateRRtoHOD) + " away" : "") +
         // V12.17 Scenario D: name the wall and say whether 2R fits before it.
         (na(nearestWall) ? "" :
              "  · wall " + f_px(nearestWall) + " (" + wallSrc + ")" +
              (na(roomR) ? "" : "  " + f_n(roomR, "#.0") + "R room" +
                   (room2R ? "" : "  ⚠ under " + f_n(rewardMultiple, "#.#") + "R"))) +
         (ema200Overhead ? "  ⚠ daily 200 EMA overhead" : "") +
         (windowAbove ? "  · window overhead = room" : "") +
         (na(gapFillPx) ? "" : "  · gap fill " + f_px(gapFillPx)),
         backSide or not room2R ? CHIP_NO : not hodComparable ? color.silver : peakIsHOD ? CHIP_OK : CHIP_NO)

    // STOCK FIT = selection, not timing (fail-closed on unknowns, V8 r18).
    if rFit >= 0
        bool fitAll = pillarScore == 4 and floatVerified and rvolKnown
        f_label(rFit, "STOCK FIT " + str.tostring(pillarScore) + "/4", fitAll)
        f_chip(1, rFit, "Price", f_b(pillarPrice))
        // V9.3: chips show the MEASURED state. Float: Pine has no float
        // field — it gates only when typed AND provenance-verified (the
        // score stays fail-closed), but a typed value colours the chip.
        // Rvolᵗ: the TV same-time proxy IS calculated — the chip colours
        // from it once warmed; the score still demands the acknowledged
        // feed (V7 reviewer gate).
        f_chip(2, rFit, floatVerified ? "Float" : "Float~",
             na(scanFloat) ? -1 : f_b(scanFloat <= scanLowFloatMaxM))
        f_chip(3, rFit, "TV pace", na(scanRVOL) or not rvolWarm ? -1 : f_b(scanRVOL >= scanMinRVOL))
        f_chip(4, rFit, "Gap", f_b(pillarGap))
        // V12.17: the fifth pillar, and the grade it produces. Grey with a
        // dot = the operator has not answered the news question yet, which
        // is different from having answered "no".
        f_chip(6, rFit, setupGrade + " " + str.tostring(pillarScore5) + "/5",
             pillarScore5 >= 5 ? 1 : pillarScore5 == 4 ? -1 : 0)
        // his 2+ hits rule (KSPN, yg5E_mqGFGg @00:16:47): one alert is not
        // a candidate — the retired DASH LANE row's one decision fact.
        f_chip(5, rFit, str.tostring(laneHits) + " hits", f_b(laneHits >= 2))
        table.cell(dash, 6, rFit, f_n(scanGap, "#.0") + "% · TV-EWMA " + f_n(scanRVOL, "#.1") + "x" +
             " (" + f_n(dayVolCum / 1000000.0, "#.00") + "M/" +
             f_n(rvolBase / 1000000.0, "#.00") + "M exp)" +
             (na(scanFloat) ? " · float ?" : " · " + f_n(scanFloat, "#.1") + "M" +
                  (floatVerified ? "" : "~")),
             text_color=color.silver, text_size=DSZ, text_halign=text.align_left)
    if rVwap >= 0
        f_label(rVwap, "VWAP", vwapBullish)
        f_text(rVwap, f_px(vwapValue) + (vwapAnchorMode == "Regular hours only (09:30)" ? " (RTH anchor)" : " (incl. pre-mkt)"),
             vwapBullish ? CHIP_OK : CHIP_NO)
        f_label(rRS, "R / S (blue/purple)", false)
        f_text(rRS, f_px(nearestRes) + " / " + f_px(nearestSup) +
             "  · setup #" + str.tostring(setupsToday + (displayState == PULLBACK ? 1 : 0)), color.silver)
        f_label(rQual, "QUALITY*", false)
        f_text(rQual, f_n(displayQuality, "#") + " *display-only, anti-predictive 16/16", color.gray)
    // V8 ND-8 / V9: a non-zero ambiguity count forces LIMITS on — the
    // labels can hide (defect 3), the count cannot.
    // V9.3 (operator): one clause, no boilerplate — the fee/fill caveats
    // live in the header. The count is the audit artifact and stays.
    if rLim >= 0
        f_label(rLim, "LIMITS", false)
        f_text(rLim, historicalFillAmbiguities > 0 ?
             "⚠ " + str.tostring(historicalFillAmbiguities) + " ambiguous entries · OHLC/halts/queue unknown · TV pace ≠ Warrior" :
             "PAPER · OHLC/halts/queue unknown · TV pace ≠ Warrior · fees reserved $" +
                  f_n(commissionReserve, "#.##"),
             historicalFillAmbiguities > 0 ? CHIP_NO : color.gray)

    // merges once per rebuild, AFTER every top-left cell exists.
    if not dashMerged
        dashMerged := true
        // V11 (display hardening — no design change): the wide rows write
        // ONLY their top-left cell, so columns 2..6 of those rows are never
        // created. table.merge_cells wants the whole range to exist; when it
        // does not merge, a long string is left inside a chip-width column 1
        // and TradingView draws it overflowing across its neighbours — which
        // is what smears the SIZE and LIMITS rows. Creating the range empty
        // first costs nothing visually and lets the merge take.
        //
        // These writes happen ONCE, BEFORE the merge. Writing a non-top-left
        // cell of an already-merged range is what Pine warns against, so they
        // must never move below the merge calls.
        for cc = 2 to 6
            table.cell(dash, cc, 0, "", text_size=DSZ)
            table.cell(dash, cc, 1, "", text_size=DSZ)
            table.cell(dash, cc, 2, "", text_size=DSZ)
            table.cell(dash, cc, 3, "", text_size=DSZ)
            table.cell(dash, cc, 7, "", text_size=DSZ)
            if cc >= 3
                table.cell(dash, cc, 4, "", text_size=DSZ)
            if rVwap >= 0
                table.cell(dash, cc, rVwap, "", text_size=DSZ)
                table.cell(dash, cc, rRS, "", text_size=DSZ)
                table.cell(dash, cc, rQual, "", text_size=DSZ)
            if rLim >= 0
                table.cell(dash, cc, rLim, "", text_size=DSZ)
        table.merge_cells(dash, 1, 0, 6, 0)
        table.merge_cells(dash, 1, 1, 6, 1)
        table.merge_cells(dash, 1, 2, 6, 2)
        table.merge_cells(dash, 1, 3, 6, 3)
        table.merge_cells(dash, 2, 4, 6, 4)
        table.merge_cells(dash, 1, 7, 6, 7)
        if not dashChips
            table.merge_cells(dash, 1, 5, 6, 5)
        if rVwap >= 0
            table.merge_cells(dash, 1, rVwap, 6, rVwap)
            table.merge_cells(dash, 1, rRS, 6, rRS)
            table.merge_cells(dash, 1, rQual, 6, rQual)
        if rLim >= 0
            table.merge_cells(dash, 1, rLim, 6, rLim)

// ───────────────────────── Alerts ─────────────────────────
// V8 (V6 directive — duplicate-channel exclusion): this file has TWO alert
// sources — these manual alert() calls (operator narrative: TRIGGER SET /
// ENTRY FILLED / NO / BAILOUT) and the strategy ORDER events (via the
// //@strategy_alert_message header + per-order alert_message). When you
// create the TradingView alert, pick ONE: "alert() function calls only" for
// the narrative channel, or "order fills and alert() calls" / strategy
// order events for the machine channel. Creating both duplicates every
// entry notification. The dedup key on ENTRY FILLED exists so a journal
// receiver can collapse exactly that mistake.
if eventArmed
    alert("ROSS FP " + REV + " | TRIGGER SET | " + syminfo.ticker +
         " | entry " + str.tostring(triggerPrice, format.mintick) +
         " | cap " + (useCappedStopLimit ?
              str.tostring(triggerPrice + entryCapTicks * syminfo.mintick, format.mintick) : "MARKET") +
         " | stop " + str.tostring(structuralStop, format.mintick) +
         " | target " + str.tostring(plannedTarget, format.mintick) +
         " | qty " + str.tostring(plannedShares) +
         " | PAPER_ONLY", alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

if eventLong
    // V8 (P29): the payload carries a dedup key (ticker-time-entryBar) so a
    // journal receiver can collapse duplicates. The key is for deduplication
    // only — it is NOT authorization to route orders to a live broker.
    alert("ROSS FP " + REV + " | ENTRY FILLED | " + syminfo.ticker +
         " | entry " + str.tostring(tradeEntryPrice, format.mintick) +
         " | stop " + str.tostring(structuralStop, format.mintick) +
         " | target " + str.tostring(activeTarget, format.mintick) +
         " | qty " + str.tostring(tradeInitialQty) +
         " | PAPER_ONLY" +
         " | key " + syminfo.ticker + "-" + str.tostring(time_close) + "-" +
         str.tostring(tradeEntryBar), alert.freq_all)

if eventInvalid
    alert("ROSS FP " + REV + " | NO | " + syminfo.ticker + " | " + statusReason, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

if eventBailout
    alert("ROSS FP " + REV + " | BAILOUT | " + syminfo.ticker + " | " + statusReason, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
